1
00:00:42,835 --> 00:00:45,254
[SOMBER INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

2
00:01:18,579 --> 00:01:21,207
<i>Hi. My name is Peter Parker.</i>

3
00:01:23,250 --> 00:01:26,294
<i>You don't remember me,
but I have something to tell you</i>

4
00:01:26,295 --> 00:01:28,338
<i>that's gonna sound crazy.</i>

5
00:01:28,339 --> 00:01:31,090
[MACHINE WHIRRING]

6
00:01:31,091 --> 00:01:32,301
<i>But it's the truth.</i>

7
00:01:34,178 --> 00:01:35,930
<i>And I know you're gonna believe me,</i>

8
00:01:36,055 --> 00:01:37,515
<i>because you're very good
at telling...</i>

9
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,183
- [BEEPING]
<i>- ...when I'm lying.</i>

10
00:01:40,976 --> 00:01:43,561
E.V., can you check the calibration
of my targeting matrix?

11
00:01:43,562 --> 00:01:45,271
That doesn't feel zeroed in to me.

12
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:47,274
E.V.: <i>Checking target calibration.</i>

13
00:01:51,779 --> 00:01:54,448
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

14
00:01:56,075 --> 00:01:57,284
Hey, E.V., take five.

15
00:01:58,035 --> 00:01:59,078
E.V.: <i>Standing by.</i>

16
00:02:04,792 --> 00:02:06,210
PETER: <i>We used to know each other.</i>

17
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:09,380
<i>We were together.</i>

18
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:12,298
<i>But something bad was gonna happen,</i>

19
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:14,217
<i>and the only way to stop it</i>

20
00:02:14,218 --> 00:02:15,886
- <i>was to make everyone forget me.
-</i> [PHONE CHIMES]

21
00:02:20,766 --> 00:02:23,101
{\an8}<i>First day at MIT, let's go!</i>

22
00:02:23,102 --> 00:02:25,311
{\an8}[LAUGHING] <i>Oh, my gosh!
We're here! We made it!</i>

23
00:02:25,312 --> 00:02:27,146
<i>Oh, MJ, come on.</i>

24
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:28,314
{\an8}PETER: <i>Including you.</i>

25
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:29,774
{\an8}NED: <i>Pretend like you're not the happiest
you've ever been</i>

26
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:31,151
{\an8}<i>in your entire life right now.</i>

27
00:02:32,111 --> 00:02:33,278
{\an8}<i>-I can't.</i>
- [NED EXCLAIMS]

28
00:02:33,279 --> 00:02:34,904
{\an8}<i>-Let's just do this!
- Okay, okay, okay.</i>

29
00:02:34,905 --> 00:02:36,155
NED: <i>You're happy!</i>
MJ: <i>Okay.</i>

30
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:38,158
PETER: <i>Because I'm not just Peter Parker.</i>

31
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:41,327
<i>I'm Spider-Man.</i>

32
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:43,121
NED: [OVER PHONE] <i>I'm really, really
understanding the culture</i>

33
00:02:43,122 --> 00:02:44,664
<i>out here in Boston is just so different.</i>

34
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:47,584
PETER: <i>And sometimes,
Spider-Man has to do the hard thing,</i>

35
00:02:47,585 --> 00:02:49,669
<i>even if it breaks Peter Parker's heart.</i>

36
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:52,882
NED: <i>And everyone here is like,
"Pahk the cah by the hahba."</i>

37
00:02:54,216 --> 00:02:56,217
PETER: <i>And maybe that's my responsibility.</i>

38
00:02:56,218 --> 00:02:57,302
[NED TALKING INDISTINCTLY]

39
00:02:57,303 --> 00:02:58,804
PETER: <i>To live alone with the truth.</i>

40
00:03:00,222 --> 00:03:03,726
<i>But the truth is, MJ, that I love you.</i>

41
00:03:05,269 --> 00:03:06,519
<i>And I hope that deep down,</i>

42
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:09,314
<i>something inside of you
remembers that you love me, too.</i>

43
00:03:09,315 --> 00:03:10,607
[PHONE BEEPS]

44
00:03:10,608 --> 00:03:13,359
E.V.: <i>Suspect is 5'8", 5'10",
medium build.</i>

45
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:16,155
PETER: <i>But until then,
I'm just gonna be Spider-Man.</i>

46
00:03:18,407 --> 00:03:20,491
[SIREN WAILING]

47
00:03:20,492 --> 00:03:22,160
[EXHILARATING MUSIC PLAYING]

48
00:03:22,161 --> 00:03:23,829
- SPIDER-MAN: Incoming!
- [THUG GROANS]

49
00:03:24,455 --> 00:03:26,539
[ALL GROANING]

50
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,958
- Hey, get him!
- [THUG 2 GROANS]

51
00:03:28,959 --> 00:03:30,336
SPIDER-MAN: Hey, hey, hey.
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

52
00:03:31,045 --> 00:03:33,339
[THUG 3 SCREAMING]

53
00:03:37,009 --> 00:03:39,053
[SIREN WAILING]

54
00:03:41,263 --> 00:03:42,556
[CHUCKLING]

55
00:03:43,307 --> 00:03:45,391
ANCHOR: [ON TV] <i>Members of
the Manfredi crime syndicate</i>

56
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:48,102
<i>were apprehended by Spider-Man yesterday.</i>

57
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:50,189
[ROCK SONG PLAYING]

58
00:04:03,619 --> 00:04:04,620
[GROANS]

59
00:04:09,333 --> 00:04:12,461
- [ELEVATOR DINGS]
- Hey, we live on the same floor.

60
00:04:13,212 --> 00:04:15,464
Oh. Cool.

61
00:04:18,133 --> 00:04:19,175
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

62
00:04:19,176 --> 00:04:20,761
PETER: Does anybody ever come up here?

63
00:04:21,387 --> 00:04:23,472
LANDLORD: Not unless they like asbestos.

64
00:04:23,973 --> 00:04:26,684
We've just been using it for storage.

65
00:04:27,726 --> 00:04:29,103
[EXHALES] It's perfect.

66
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:33,107
NED: [ON PHONE] <i>Hey, everyone,
sophomore-year Ned is back.</i>

67
00:04:33,607 --> 00:04:36,526
{\an8}<i>Older, wiser, flyer.</i>

68
00:04:36,527 --> 00:04:39,320
{\an8}- [EXCLAIMS] <i>Let's go!
- Whoa.</i>

69
00:04:39,321 --> 00:04:41,781
{\an8}<i>-What is on your face?</i>
- NED: <i>How do you feel about it?</i>

70
00:04:41,782 --> 00:04:43,992
{\an8}<i>I mean, you look
like an assistant coach.</i>

71
00:04:43,993 --> 00:04:45,076
{\an8}<i>Huh.</i>

72
00:04:45,077 --> 00:04:47,162
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
- [PEOPLE SCREAMING]

73
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,332
SPIDER-MAN: You sure
you wanna do this, Scorpion?

74
00:04:50,708 --> 00:04:51,917
Did you miss me, Spidey?

75
00:04:55,671 --> 00:04:56,964
[TOMBSTONE GRUNTS]

76
00:04:58,090 --> 00:04:59,507
If I drop you from here,

77
00:04:59,508 --> 00:05:01,719
how long you think
it will take you to hit the ground?

78
00:05:02,761 --> 00:05:03,678
SPIDER-MAN: Well, I don't know.

79
00:05:03,679 --> 00:05:05,014
- You tell me.
- [TOMBSTONE YELPS]

80
00:05:05,556 --> 00:05:06,765
SPIDER-MAN: Let's end this
on a high note, huh?

81
00:05:08,392 --> 00:05:09,809
[SCORPION GRUNTS]

82
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:12,479
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
- [TOMBSTONE SCREAMING]

83
00:05:13,063 --> 00:05:14,189
Yo, Lonnie!

84
00:05:14,857 --> 00:05:16,065
{\an8}Wha ha happened?

85
00:05:16,066 --> 00:05:18,151
{\an8}SPIDER-MAN: DeWolff,
all the evidence you're gonna need

86
00:05:18,152 --> 00:05:19,694
is in the trunk of his car.

87
00:05:19,695 --> 00:05:21,904
You tryin' to take my job, Spider-Man?

88
00:05:21,905 --> 00:05:24,199
SPIDER-MAN: Hey, you guys are
the professionals, I'm just a volunteer.

89
00:05:26,285 --> 00:05:28,662
[ROCK SONG CONTINUES]

90
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:36,753
ANCHOR: [ON TV] <i>It's a new New York.</i>

91
00:05:36,754 --> 00:05:40,423
<i>Thanks to Spider-Man,
crime rates have dropped to a record low.</i>

92
00:05:40,424 --> 00:05:42,884
<i>Police and Damage Control
give much of the credit</i>

93
00:05:42,885 --> 00:05:44,052
<i>to the masked hero.</i>

94
00:05:44,053 --> 00:05:45,887
- PETER: Initiate HUD test.
- [PHONE BEEPING]

95
00:05:45,888 --> 00:05:47,597
E.V.: <i>Armed robbery at Civic Union Bank.</i>

96
00:05:47,598 --> 00:05:49,640
ANCHOR: <i>In the past six months,
he has taken down</i>

97
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:52,685
<i>every major crime lord
across the five boroughs,</i>

98
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:56,148
<i>including the superpowered
ninja group The Hand.</i>

99
00:06:00,027 --> 00:06:01,736
{\an8}<i>He is the pride of New York City.</i>

100
00:06:01,737 --> 00:06:06,033
{\an8}<i>The hero every grown-up relies on
and every kid wants to be.</i>

101
00:06:07,076 --> 00:06:09,535
NED: [ON PHONE] <i>Final semester, MIT.</i>

102
00:06:09,536 --> 00:06:11,830
{\an8}<i>Oh, my gosh, we're graduating in a month.</i>

103
00:06:12,247 --> 00:06:15,541
<i>We've made so many memories.
Where do I begin?</i>

104
00:06:15,542 --> 00:06:18,795
<i>Night swimming in the Charles River
with Jim and Wiley.</i>

105
00:06:18,796 --> 00:06:21,672
<i>The infamous food fight
at the Banana Lounge.</i>

106
00:06:21,673 --> 00:06:26,052
<i>Pulling all-nighters in Stud 5
with MJ and Nate Dawg.</i>

107
00:06:26,053 --> 00:06:28,888
<i>It feels like yesterday
I was sitting on a roof with MJ,</i>

108
00:06:28,889 --> 00:06:32,308
<i>dreaming about coming here together,
and I still can't believe we did it.</i>

109
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:35,103
<i>I'm so grateful
for all the friends that I've made.</i>

110
00:06:35,104 --> 00:06:37,522
<i>I couldn't imagine
going through this with anyone else.</i>

111
00:06:37,523 --> 00:06:39,607
{\an8}<i>Ned, who do you think
is actually watching these?</i>

112
00:06:39,608 --> 00:06:40,858
{\an8}[STUTTERING] <i>I don't know.</i>

113
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:42,235
{\an8}<i>-But maybe someone.
-</i> MJ: <i>Okay.</i>

114
00:06:42,236 --> 00:06:43,611
{\an8}<i>Okay, well, bye, someone.</i>

115
00:06:43,612 --> 00:06:44,654
{\an8}NED: <i>What?</i>
MJ: <i>Bye. We're done.</i>

116
00:06:44,655 --> 00:06:45,697
NED: <i>No!</i>
MJ: <i>Yeah, we're done.</i>

117
00:07:03,799 --> 00:07:07,093
I mean, we're talking about
downtown Brooklyn in broad daylight.

118
00:07:07,094 --> 00:07:10,096
High-profile job like that,
you know that Foswell was involved.

119
00:07:10,097 --> 00:07:12,390
Yeah, I hear you, but can you prove it?

120
00:07:12,391 --> 00:07:14,350
Yeah, I'm going through
his financial records

121
00:07:14,351 --> 00:07:15,935
and I'm following his crew every night.

122
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:18,938
DEWOLFF: [CHUCKLES]
<i>Do you do anything besides work?</i>

123
00:07:18,939 --> 00:07:20,565
You know the saying,
"You do something you love,

124
00:07:20,566 --> 00:07:21,899
"you don't work a day in your life."

125
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,401
[CHUCKLES, SPEAKING SPANISH]

126
00:07:23,402 --> 00:07:25,486
- [IN ENGLISH] Mom, where's my calculator?
- [SOFTLY] I don't know.

127
00:07:25,487 --> 00:07:29,532
<i>Trust me, aight?
Being married to the job never ends well.</i>

128
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:31,617
[CHUCKLES] Well, don't worry about it.
I'll be okay.

129
00:07:31,618 --> 00:07:34,246
Oh, yeah?
You still getting them headaches, though?

130
00:07:35,664 --> 00:07:38,166
Uh, yeah. But, um... But I'll be fine.

131
00:07:38,167 --> 00:07:39,417
DEWOLFF: <i>Mmm, I don't know, man.</i>

132
00:07:39,418 --> 00:07:41,502
<i>I think your body's tryin'
to tell you somethin'.</i>

133
00:07:41,503 --> 00:07:44,046
Like you need to get outta that suit
every once in a while.

134
00:07:44,047 --> 00:07:46,007
Mom, do you know where my calculator is?

135
00:07:46,008 --> 00:07:47,009
I don't know, <i>Papi.</i>

136
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:50,344
<i>What you need
is some real human connection.</i>

137
00:07:50,345 --> 00:07:52,054
Oh, what? And we're not connecting?

138
00:07:52,055 --> 00:07:53,097
DEWOLFF: <i>Nah, dude.</i>

139
00:07:53,098 --> 00:07:56,851
<i>I don't know your name, your face,
or nothing about you.</i>

140
00:07:56,852 --> 00:07:59,312
I don't think you've ever asked me
a question about my life.

141
00:07:59,313 --> 00:08:00,396
PETER: <i>Sure, I have.</i>

142
00:08:00,397 --> 00:08:01,856
DEWOLFF: <i>Yeah, what are my kids' names?</i>

143
00:08:01,857 --> 00:08:04,483
Uh, well, for starters,
your son's name's <i>Papi.</i>

144
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:05,777
[LAUGHING]

145
00:08:06,153 --> 00:08:07,320
Is it Spider-Man?

146
00:08:07,321 --> 00:08:09,239
I can't tell you that, sweetheart.

147
00:08:09,698 --> 00:08:11,199
That means it's Spider-Man.

148
00:08:11,200 --> 00:08:12,367
[SIGHS] Gosh.

149
00:08:12,993 --> 00:08:14,244
[ALARM BEEPING]

150
00:08:15,037 --> 00:08:18,039
DISPATCHER: <i>A hijacked tank
is heading southbound past 34th Street.</i>

151
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,458
<i>All available units respond.</i>

152
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:20,958
Hey, you getting this?

153
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,793
More work. Lucky you.

154
00:08:22,794 --> 00:08:24,003
Okay, I'll see you out there.

155
00:08:24,004 --> 00:08:25,213
I'm so sorry, I gotta go.

156
00:08:25,214 --> 00:08:27,340
[SIREN WAILING]

157
00:08:27,341 --> 00:08:29,384
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:08:34,056 --> 00:08:35,515
SPIDER-MAN: Whoo!

159
00:08:38,435 --> 00:08:39,436
[GROANS]

160
00:08:40,103 --> 00:08:41,980
[EXCLAIMING]

161
00:08:47,319 --> 00:08:49,029
[WIND WHISTLING]

162
00:08:52,741 --> 00:08:55,035
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

163
00:09:00,624 --> 00:09:02,251
Awoo!

164
00:09:02,918 --> 00:09:05,128
[WEB WARBLING INTENSELY]

165
00:09:08,215 --> 00:09:10,259
[EXPLOSIONS]

166
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:14,137
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

167
00:09:15,472 --> 00:09:17,266
[SIREN WAILING]

168
00:09:24,815 --> 00:09:26,483
[GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

169
00:09:27,985 --> 00:09:29,236
[SPIDER-MAN EXCLAIMS]

170
00:09:31,196 --> 00:09:32,197
SPIDER-MAN: Whoa!

171
00:09:35,784 --> 00:09:37,159
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

172
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,328
[METAL CLANGS]

173
00:09:40,831 --> 00:09:42,498
[MUSIC PLAYING OVER STEREO]

174
00:09:42,499 --> 00:09:43,874
I got you, Spidey!

175
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:45,251
SPIDER-MAN: No, no. I don't need your...

176
00:09:45,252 --> 00:09:47,296
- [ENGINE ACCELERATING]
- SPIDER-MAN: Whoa.

177
00:09:48,797 --> 00:09:50,048
[CLINKS]

178
00:09:55,304 --> 00:09:56,847
[SCREECHING]

179
00:09:59,516 --> 00:10:00,559
SPIDER-MAN: Hey! Heads up!

180
00:10:02,394 --> 00:10:06,148
You okay, kid? Yeah, you're okay.
See ya later. [GRUNTS]

181
00:10:06,857 --> 00:10:08,650
[SIREN WAILING]

182
00:10:10,235 --> 00:10:11,777
You wouldn't know it
just by looking at it,

183
00:10:11,778 --> 00:10:15,865
{\an8}but this very street was completely
destroyed in the Battle of New York.

184
00:10:15,866 --> 00:10:16,783
{\an8}[PEOPLE GASPING]

185
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:19,744
- [SPIDER-MAN SHOUTS]
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING]

186
00:10:19,745 --> 00:10:20,871
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

187
00:10:23,123 --> 00:10:24,833
[STRAINING] Come on, come on, come on.

188
00:10:26,501 --> 00:10:28,378
Come on.

189
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:32,132
[SCREAMING, GROANING]

190
00:10:38,513 --> 00:10:39,638
[SPIDER-SENSE TINGLING]

191
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:41,307
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

192
00:10:41,308 --> 00:10:43,685
Oh, God. [GRUNTS, GROANS]

193
00:10:46,063 --> 00:10:47,814
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

194
00:10:51,026 --> 00:10:52,027
Come on.

195
00:10:52,486 --> 00:10:54,488
- Hey. [GROANS]
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

196
00:10:54,988 --> 00:10:57,031
The hell, Frank?
You just hit me with the van!

197
00:10:57,032 --> 00:10:58,407
Quit your whimpering.

198
00:10:58,408 --> 00:11:00,034
SPIDER-MAN: We're not
doing that again, Frank.

199
00:11:00,035 --> 00:11:01,535
You're goddamn right we're not.

200
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:03,288
This time you're gonna
get the hell outta my way.

201
00:11:03,789 --> 00:11:05,331
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, you mean
instead of saving your life?

202
00:11:05,332 --> 00:11:08,709
Eh, you gonna talk about
that Staten Island bullshit again?

203
00:11:08,710 --> 00:11:10,419
SPIDER-MAN: Ah, well, you said it, not me.

204
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:11,504
Jeez.

205
00:11:11,505 --> 00:11:13,547
SPIDER-MAN: Look, man, you can't just
shoot yourself out of every situation.

206
00:11:13,548 --> 00:11:15,007
Innocent people get hurt.

207
00:11:15,008 --> 00:11:17,302
Who do you think's downrange of that tank,
dumb-dumb?

208
00:11:17,928 --> 00:11:19,054
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

209
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,182
[LAUGHS MOCKINGLY]

210
00:11:22,808 --> 00:11:23,809
Suit yourself.

211
00:11:25,018 --> 00:11:26,686
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

212
00:11:27,479 --> 00:11:28,562
Jackass.

213
00:11:28,563 --> 00:11:30,649
SPIDER-MAN: [EXHALES] This freakin' guy.

214
00:11:34,611 --> 00:11:35,695
[EXCLAIMS]

215
00:11:36,655 --> 00:11:38,489
[BOTH GROANING]

216
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:40,283
[GRUNTING]

217
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:42,661
[CLANGS]

218
00:11:44,496 --> 00:11:46,747
- Motherf...
- [PEOPLE CLAMORING]

219
00:11:46,748 --> 00:11:48,041
SPIDER-MAN: Go home, Frank!

220
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:49,918
[SPITS]

221
00:11:50,752 --> 00:11:51,586
[GRUNTS]

222
00:11:52,629 --> 00:11:54,213
I'm gonna kill this kid.

223
00:11:54,214 --> 00:11:56,216
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

224
00:11:57,676 --> 00:11:58,968
[CELL PHONE RINGING]

225
00:11:58,969 --> 00:12:01,345
- SPIDER-MAN: DeWolff?
- Are you gonna stop that thing or what?

226
00:12:01,346 --> 00:12:04,056
<i>It's heading straight
for the Damage Control Detention Center.</i>

227
00:12:04,057 --> 00:12:05,141
SPIDER-MAN: I'm trying.

228
00:12:05,142 --> 00:12:06,267
DEWOLFF: <i>Try harder.</i>

229
00:12:06,268 --> 00:12:08,102
<i>There's a lot of scary dudes
locked up in there.</i>

230
00:12:08,103 --> 00:12:09,728
SPIDER-MAN: Well, who do you think
put them in there?

231
00:12:09,729 --> 00:12:13,941
- [PRISON DOOR BEEPS]
- GUARD: Let's go, Scorpion. Moving day.

232
00:12:13,942 --> 00:12:15,944
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

233
00:12:21,032 --> 00:12:22,659
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS, SHOUTS]

234
00:12:27,706 --> 00:12:28,999
[GRUNTS]

235
00:12:31,084 --> 00:12:32,878
[ALL CLAMORING]

236
00:12:37,507 --> 00:12:39,800
[ALL EXCLAIMING]

237
00:12:39,801 --> 00:12:41,343
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

238
00:12:41,344 --> 00:12:43,138
GUARD: Please! Evac now!

239
00:12:44,097 --> 00:12:45,389
SPIDER-MAN: All right,
everybody, clear out!

240
00:12:45,390 --> 00:12:46,892
This guy is armed and dangerous.

241
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:50,937
[STRAINING]

242
00:12:53,815 --> 00:12:55,025
[SPIDER-MAN EXHALES]

243
00:12:57,652 --> 00:13:00,655
Uh... Get out of the vehicle, ma'am.

244
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:03,116
I was thinking the same thing.

245
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:06,077
[WHOOSHES]

246
00:13:08,997 --> 00:13:10,080
[SPIDER-SENSE TINGLING]

247
00:13:10,081 --> 00:13:11,916
[SPIDER-MAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

248
00:13:11,917 --> 00:13:13,376
Spider-Man?

249
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:15,837
Where am I?

250
00:13:21,468 --> 00:13:22,968
[WHOOSHES]

251
00:13:22,969 --> 00:13:24,136
SPIDER-MAN: What the...

252
00:13:24,137 --> 00:13:25,722
[INDISTINCT CLAMOR]

253
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,265
MAN: Move! Move! Move! Move! Move!

254
00:13:28,266 --> 00:13:30,018
SPIDER-MAN: Keep her for questioning.
Clear the building.

255
00:13:33,188 --> 00:13:35,189
GUARD: Enjoy the ride, Scorpion!

256
00:13:35,190 --> 00:13:37,817
You won't be seeing much daylight
in supermax.

257
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,862
Scorpions are nocturnal, buddy.

258
00:13:43,782 --> 00:13:45,449
GUARD 2: [OVER COMMS]
<i>The building is under attack.</i>

259
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:47,160
<i>Get the prisoner out of here now!</i>

260
00:13:47,911 --> 00:13:49,871
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

261
00:13:52,332 --> 00:13:53,415
- GUARD: Sir!
- [WHOOSHES]

262
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:55,126
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:13:56,419 --> 00:13:59,339
[WHOOSHING]

264
00:14:12,102 --> 00:14:13,727
GUARD: You gotta take off now!

265
00:14:13,728 --> 00:14:15,730
The building has been breached. Go! Go!

266
00:14:16,147 --> 00:14:18,733
Hey, fire it up! Go! Go!

267
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:23,863
[WHOOSHES]

268
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:28,368
Change of plans!

269
00:14:28,952 --> 00:14:30,829
Take him to the helipad at Bellevue.

270
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:33,330
- What?
- That's an order

271
00:14:33,331 --> 00:14:34,873
from Director Metzger. Go!

272
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:36,000
Now!

273
00:14:36,001 --> 00:14:37,043
Copy that.

274
00:14:48,013 --> 00:14:49,763
SPIDER-MAN: Hey! What...

275
00:14:49,764 --> 00:14:52,183
- How did I get up here?
- SPIDER-MAN: Uh...

276
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:55,477
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

277
00:14:55,478 --> 00:14:58,481
Spider-Man, save me, would you?

278
00:14:59,274 --> 00:15:00,525
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

279
00:15:04,195 --> 00:15:05,196
Who are you?

280
00:15:06,448 --> 00:15:07,990
You can see me.

281
00:15:07,991 --> 00:15:09,326
SPIDER-MAN: Tell me who you are.

282
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:12,078
- You first.
- [WHOOSHES]

283
00:15:13,038 --> 00:15:14,663
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

284
00:15:14,664 --> 00:15:16,833
MAY: Hey. Hey.

285
00:15:18,251 --> 00:15:20,879
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANING]
- [WHOOSHES]

286
00:15:22,714 --> 00:15:24,048
You pushed me out.

287
00:15:24,049 --> 00:15:25,924
- [SPIDER-MAN PANTING]
- GUARD: Interesting.

288
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:27,509
SPIDER-MAN: What the hell was that?

289
00:15:27,510 --> 00:15:29,678
Did you just try to jump into my mind?

290
00:15:29,679 --> 00:15:32,766
You know, the whole time
you've been chasing me,

291
00:15:33,516 --> 00:15:36,268
you forgot to ask yourself
a very important question.

292
00:15:36,269 --> 00:15:38,062
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:15:38,063 --> 00:15:39,356
What's in the tank?

294
00:15:41,316 --> 00:15:42,901
GUARD: Go! Move.

295
00:15:43,568 --> 00:15:45,236
[TIMER BEEPING]

296
00:15:52,452 --> 00:15:53,661
[WHOOSHES]

297
00:15:53,662 --> 00:15:55,246
[PANTING]

298
00:15:57,082 --> 00:15:58,083
Spider-Man?

299
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:01,293
- What just happened?
- [SIREN WAILING]

300
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:03,420
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

301
00:16:03,421 --> 00:16:04,464
I don't know.

302
00:16:06,633 --> 00:16:07,716
Hey, good job.

303
00:16:07,717 --> 00:16:08,884
FIREFIGHTER: Hey, way to go, Spidey.

304
00:16:08,885 --> 00:16:10,678
SPIDER-MAN: You guys okay? You good?

305
00:16:10,679 --> 00:16:13,681
I swear. All the things they said I did,
I don't remember doing any of them.

306
00:16:13,682 --> 00:16:15,849
SPIDER-MAN: It's okay, it's okay. Look,
let these people take good care of you.

307
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:17,017
I would never hurt you.

308
00:16:17,018 --> 00:16:18,435
- SPIDER-MAN: Okay.
- I love you, Spider-Man.

309
00:16:18,436 --> 00:16:19,978
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.
All right, buddy. All right.

310
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:22,147
- Hey, what do you got?
- Here, get this.

311
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:23,899
Chopper took Scorpion to Bellevue.

312
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:26,318
Ten minutes later,
a guard walked him right out the door.

313
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:27,653
SPIDER-MAN: What?
DEWOLFF: Mmm-hmm.

314
00:16:27,654 --> 00:16:28,821
SPIDER-MAN: What about the tank?

315
00:16:28,822 --> 00:16:31,532
Stolen from the Damage Control
warehouse in Brooklyn.

316
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:33,784
Driver was a janitor who worked there.

317
00:16:33,785 --> 00:16:34,868
SPIDER-MAN: You got a motive?

318
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:37,121
<i>Nada.</i> And no criminal record.

319
00:16:37,122 --> 00:16:39,124
Scorpion must've gotten to her somehow.

320
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:42,042
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah. Maybe.

321
00:16:42,043 --> 00:16:43,627
What do you mean, "maybe"?

322
00:16:43,628 --> 00:16:45,547
SPIDER-MAN: I mean, I... I don't know.

323
00:16:46,339 --> 00:16:47,756
But I know someone that might.

324
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:48,924
Where you going?

325
00:16:48,925 --> 00:16:50,676
SPIDER-MAN: You keep following
the leads on Scorpion.

326
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:52,428
I'm gonna go talk to someone.

327
00:16:52,429 --> 00:16:53,345
[WHOOSHES]

328
00:16:53,346 --> 00:16:56,182
[RUSSIAN POP SONG PLAYING]

329
00:17:04,065 --> 00:17:06,234
[SONG CONTINUES PLAYING
OVER SPEAKER]

330
00:17:07,902 --> 00:17:11,406
SPIDER-MAN: Hi, uh,
is this 3250 Brighton Beach?

331
00:17:12,407 --> 00:17:14,492
[SPEAKING RUSSIAN]

332
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:17,162
SPIDER-MAN: [IN ENGLISH] Okay.

333
00:17:17,871 --> 00:17:19,664
I think I know what that means.

334
00:17:24,753 --> 00:17:25,920
WOMAN: Take off your clothes.

335
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:30,008
SPIDER-MAN: Uh, what?

336
00:17:30,467 --> 00:17:32,427
You don't wear clothes in the <i>banya.</i>

337
00:17:33,595 --> 00:17:34,888
Ditch the leotard.

338
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,432
SPIDER-MAN: This is not a leotard.

339
00:17:38,266 --> 00:17:40,226
Your text said that this was your office.

340
00:17:41,561 --> 00:17:43,104
This is my office.

341
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:45,522
- Get in.
- [SPIDER-MAN CHUCKLES]

342
00:17:45,523 --> 00:17:47,608
Uh, I'm fine, thanks. I'll just...

343
00:17:47,609 --> 00:17:48,817
Wah-wah. [CHUCKLES]

344
00:17:48,818 --> 00:17:50,277
My office, my rules.

345
00:17:50,278 --> 00:17:54,239
This way, you get to enjoy
a nice, relaxing soak,

346
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:56,617
and I get to see that
you don't have any weapons,

347
00:17:56,618 --> 00:17:57,827
and we both win.

348
00:17:59,996 --> 00:18:00,997
SPIDER-MAN: Okay.

349
00:18:04,167 --> 00:18:05,251
[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

350
00:18:07,128 --> 00:18:08,630
[YELENA LAUGHING]

351
00:18:10,298 --> 00:18:12,841
Really? What, you never take that off?

352
00:18:12,842 --> 00:18:14,928
SPIDER-MAN: No, I... You know,
it defeats the whole anonymous thing.

353
00:18:15,136 --> 00:18:19,599
Even for your girlfriend
or boyfriend or whatever?

354
00:18:20,266 --> 00:18:21,893
There's a lot of conjecture online.

355
00:18:22,685 --> 00:18:25,230
And super graphic artwork. Have you seen?

356
00:18:25,438 --> 00:18:28,232
The one with you
and the ten Mysterios, it's...

357
00:18:28,233 --> 00:18:30,567
[STUTTERING]
I've... I've... I've seen it. I've...

358
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:32,110
It's hard to unsee, to be honest.

359
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:34,155
But, look, I don't have anyone.
I just kinda keep to myself.

360
00:18:34,948 --> 00:18:36,532
All by yourself? All the time?

361
00:18:36,533 --> 00:18:38,200
No wonder you're so sad.

362
00:18:38,201 --> 00:18:40,452
- [CHUCKLES] I'm not so sad.
- A little bit.

363
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:42,496
Could we just talk about
what I came here to talk to you about,

364
00:18:42,497 --> 00:18:43,914
the attack on Damage Control?

365
00:18:43,915 --> 00:18:47,710
Yes. So, that is more your area.

366
00:18:48,545 --> 00:18:50,922
Like, small potato stuff.

367
00:18:51,548 --> 00:18:57,637
Whereas the New Avengers
are focusing on big potato stuff.

368
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:02,183
SPIDER-MAN: Right, okay. Well, there's
more to it than that, you know, the, uh...

369
00:19:02,892 --> 00:19:05,435
[WHISPERING] ...the driver
and the others who were helping,

370
00:19:05,436 --> 00:19:08,021
it was like someone
was talking to me through them.

371
00:19:08,022 --> 00:19:10,524
Like someone was looking at me
through their eyes.

372
00:19:10,525 --> 00:19:12,818
And you're wondering if it's mind control?

373
00:19:12,819 --> 00:19:15,487
- Exactly.
- Like how they used on me in the Red Room?

374
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:17,197
- Exactly.
- And the other widows?

375
00:19:17,198 --> 00:19:19,241
- Right.
- Right. No, I don't think so.

376
00:19:19,242 --> 00:19:23,454
I actually think it's probably
more like possession.

377
00:19:23,997 --> 00:19:26,290
- SPIDER-MAN: Possession?
- Hmm. Hmm.

378
00:19:26,291 --> 00:19:28,292
Like a ghost or a demon.

379
00:19:28,293 --> 00:19:30,085
- SPIDER-MAN: Oh, man.
- Or in Russia, we have leshy.

380
00:19:30,086 --> 00:19:33,715
Leshy rules the forest and can possess...

381
00:19:36,175 --> 00:19:37,176
SPIDER-MAN: Sorry.

382
00:19:37,719 --> 00:19:39,928
Whatever it is,
they are looking for something.

383
00:19:39,929 --> 00:19:43,433
This is the fourth attack
on the Damage Control facility this month.

384
00:19:44,267 --> 00:19:45,934
And what do you think they're looking for?

385
00:19:45,935 --> 00:19:47,227
YELENA: I don't know.

386
00:19:47,228 --> 00:19:48,812
But you know what?

387
00:19:48,813 --> 00:19:50,981
After the attack today,

388
00:19:50,982 --> 00:19:54,944
there was a cross-agency cybersecurity
alert that got triggered.

389
00:19:55,403 --> 00:19:58,864
Someone accessed
the Damage Control restricted servers

390
00:19:58,865 --> 00:20:02,367
using credentials from 30 employees
from the way station.

391
00:20:02,368 --> 00:20:04,746
They all searched for the same thing.

392
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:07,205
V-Max.

393
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:08,916
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

394
00:20:08,917 --> 00:20:10,209
SPIDER-MAN: V-Max.

395
00:20:11,377 --> 00:20:12,878
Well, what does that mean?

396
00:20:12,879 --> 00:20:15,714
I mean, it could be alien tech,

397
00:20:15,715 --> 00:20:19,468
or secretive weapon programs,

398
00:20:19,469 --> 00:20:22,722
or launch codes or...

399
00:20:24,098 --> 00:20:26,266
I don't know,
this is for you to figure out.

400
00:20:26,267 --> 00:20:28,101
This is small, baby potato stuff...

401
00:20:28,102 --> 00:20:29,770
- SPIDER-MAN: Okay, okay.
- ...not big potato brain stuff.

402
00:20:29,771 --> 00:20:31,229
SPIDER-MAN: You don't
have to shout about it. Jeez.

403
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:33,191
Maybe I'll just go ask
Damage Control myself.

404
00:20:35,777 --> 00:20:38,695
You know, you're not
completely anonymous anymore.

405
00:20:38,696 --> 00:20:40,530
I've seen your belly button.

406
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:43,868
SPIDER-MAN: [CHUCKLES] Okay.
YELENA: Bye.

407
00:21:07,225 --> 00:21:08,684
[DOOR SLAMS]

408
00:21:08,685 --> 00:21:09,769
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, God.

409
00:21:11,145 --> 00:21:12,813
Hi, I got an appointment with, uh...

410
00:21:12,814 --> 00:21:14,189
Director Metzger. Yes.

411
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:15,692
Please step through the scanner.

412
00:21:17,193 --> 00:21:18,610
[SCANNER POWERS ON]

413
00:21:18,611 --> 00:21:20,613
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Enhanced human detected.</i>

414
00:21:21,322 --> 00:21:23,365
<i>Superior strength.</i>

415
00:21:23,366 --> 00:21:25,492
<i>Superior agility.</i>

416
00:21:25,493 --> 00:21:27,202
<i>Heightened senses.</i>

417
00:21:27,203 --> 00:21:29,497
<i>Exogenous DNA. Arachnid.</i>

418
00:21:30,999 --> 00:21:33,333
Please remove your face covering
for identity scan.

419
00:21:33,334 --> 00:21:34,626
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, no, I can't do that.

420
00:21:34,627 --> 00:21:36,753
- That's not possible.
- Failure to remove your face covering

421
00:21:36,754 --> 00:21:38,755
will result in defensive measures.

422
00:21:38,756 --> 00:21:40,674
SPIDER-MAN: Defensive measures?
What are you talk...

423
00:21:40,675 --> 00:21:41,717
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

424
00:21:41,718 --> 00:21:44,136
Guys, guys, guys!
I can't take my mask off. I'm...

425
00:21:44,137 --> 00:21:46,263
- METZGER: Spider-Man.
- [ALARM BLARING]

426
00:21:46,264 --> 00:21:48,599
- He's all right. At ease.
- [ALARM STOPS]

427
00:21:52,895 --> 00:21:54,855
METZGER: My apologies.

428
00:21:54,856 --> 00:21:56,065
We are so glad you're here.

429
00:21:56,607 --> 00:21:59,317
Bill Metzger, Director of Damage Control.
How are you?

430
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:00,361
SPIDER-MAN: I'm good, thank you.

431
00:22:00,903 --> 00:22:03,655
We had to beef up security around here,
but I hope we didn't give you a fright.

432
00:22:03,656 --> 00:22:05,907
- SPIDER-MAN: No, not at all.
- All right, come on. This way.

433
00:22:05,908 --> 00:22:07,492
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

434
00:22:07,493 --> 00:22:09,787
METZGER: This floor is mostly
research and administrative.

435
00:22:10,371 --> 00:22:13,957
Downstairs, we have incident cleanup,
laboratories, agent training.

436
00:22:13,958 --> 00:22:15,459
SPIDER-MAN: Oh.

437
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:17,170
- Hey, what are they doing here?
- It's okay.

438
00:22:18,129 --> 00:22:19,714
The Hand works for us now.

439
00:22:20,256 --> 00:22:22,007
After you brought them in,
I realized that

440
00:22:22,008 --> 00:22:24,593
fundamentally, they're a group of kids
without a leader.

441
00:22:24,594 --> 00:22:26,595
All they needed was a little direction.

442
00:22:26,596 --> 00:22:28,555
Then, suddenly,
all the things that made them dangerous

443
00:22:28,556 --> 00:22:30,933
turned them into an invaluable part
of our security team.

444
00:22:31,809 --> 00:22:33,936
[SPEAKING JAPANESE]

445
00:22:36,606 --> 00:22:39,358
[IN ENGLISH] You can look at the many
threats that face us and see only danger.

446
00:22:40,735 --> 00:22:42,195
Or you can see opportunity.

447
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:44,781
SPIDER-MAN: Uh, okay.

448
00:22:46,949 --> 00:22:49,326
- [ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]
- [SPIDER-MAN WHISTLES]

449
00:22:49,327 --> 00:22:50,620
Wow, look at that.

450
00:22:51,412 --> 00:22:53,581
In the hands of Shocker,
these are a nuisance.

451
00:22:54,248 --> 00:22:55,791
[CLANGS, ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

452
00:22:55,792 --> 00:22:57,584
But it doesn't mean
we can't learn from the technology,

453
00:22:57,585 --> 00:22:59,045
or respect the innovation.

454
00:22:59,962 --> 00:23:04,049
Our mission is to redirect destructive
energy into something useful.

455
00:23:04,050 --> 00:23:05,718
That's the true meaning of Damage Control.

456
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:11,098
[KNOCKING]

457
00:23:11,099 --> 00:23:12,308
SPIDER-MAN: Be careful with that.

458
00:23:13,226 --> 00:23:14,227
Right this way.

459
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:19,106
SPIDER-MAN: I, uh...
I wanted to talk to you

460
00:23:19,107 --> 00:23:20,775
about the recent attacks on the agency.

461
00:23:21,234 --> 00:23:23,151
There's been four, right?

462
00:23:23,152 --> 00:23:24,237
Please have a seat.

463
00:23:25,363 --> 00:23:26,781
You are right.

464
00:23:27,281 --> 00:23:29,784
It appears we're faced with a threat
we can't control.

465
00:23:30,326 --> 00:23:31,410
One we can't even see.

466
00:23:34,205 --> 00:23:35,414
But you can.

467
00:23:36,290 --> 00:23:37,917
I saw the security footage.

468
00:23:39,377 --> 00:23:41,504
I also read Detective DeWolff's report.

469
00:23:42,547 --> 00:23:45,048
I believe you understand
exactly what we're up against.

470
00:23:45,049 --> 00:23:48,845
SPIDER-MAN: [SIGHS] Someone or something
that can hop into people's minds.

471
00:23:49,887 --> 00:23:50,971
But not yours.

472
00:23:50,972 --> 00:23:53,683
SPIDER-MAN: No,
I mean, it tried, but it couldn't.

473
00:24:02,859 --> 00:24:04,402
I'm gonna be honest with you.

474
00:24:05,278 --> 00:24:06,571
We're on our heels right now.

475
00:24:07,738 --> 00:24:10,615
God forbid if it were to get in here
and find whatever it is it's looking for,

476
00:24:10,616 --> 00:24:14,328
the consequences could be unimaginable.

477
00:24:17,123 --> 00:24:18,957
SPIDER-MAN: Well, let me guess,
is whatever it's looking for

478
00:24:18,958 --> 00:24:20,084
in that giant vault?

479
00:24:23,045 --> 00:24:25,380
There are some things,
because of the nature of my job

480
00:24:25,381 --> 00:24:26,632
I cannot tell you.

481
00:24:27,133 --> 00:24:29,594
But I believe you are our
best defense against this.

482
00:24:30,011 --> 00:24:31,512
You're the only one who can sense it.

483
00:24:32,013 --> 00:24:33,431
You're the only one who's immune to it.

484
00:24:34,056 --> 00:24:35,683
I'm counting on you to defeat it.

485
00:24:39,228 --> 00:24:41,314
SPIDER-MAN: That's a pretty good speech,
Director.

486
00:24:42,064 --> 00:24:43,482
I'll do everything that I can, I promise.

487
00:24:45,234 --> 00:24:47,611
Well, then consider yourself
a friend of Damage Control.

488
00:24:47,612 --> 00:24:48,613
SPIDER-MAN: Thank you.

489
00:24:49,572 --> 00:24:50,573
I'll be in touch.

490
00:24:51,908 --> 00:24:54,243
Oh. Uh, I wanted to ask, um...

491
00:24:54,869 --> 00:24:57,537
the phrase "V-Max"
doesn't mean anything to you, does it?

492
00:24:57,538 --> 00:24:58,955
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

493
00:24:58,956 --> 00:25:01,334
No. Where'd you hear that?

494
00:25:01,834 --> 00:25:04,753
Oh, it's just, you know,
nature of being a superhero,

495
00:25:04,754 --> 00:25:06,171
there are some things
I just can't tell ya.

496
00:25:06,172 --> 00:25:07,422
[LAUGHING]

497
00:25:07,423 --> 00:25:08,716
SPIDER-MAN: Anyway, I'll see you later.

498
00:25:09,759 --> 00:25:11,260
You guys are doing great. Keep it up.

499
00:25:11,677 --> 00:25:13,845
<i>I don't think Metzger knows
any more than we do,</i>

500
00:25:13,846 --> 00:25:15,972
<i>but I told him
I'd do whatever I can to help.</i>

501
00:25:15,973 --> 00:25:18,433
You wanna help?
The best thing you could do

502
00:25:18,434 --> 00:25:20,644
<i>is find Scorpion.
He's our only lead.</i>

503
00:25:20,645 --> 00:25:22,520
Yeah, I know.
I have every camera in the city

504
00:25:22,521 --> 00:25:24,398
running a facial recognition scan for him.

505
00:25:24,941 --> 00:25:28,318
That sounds super illegal, Spider-Man.
I'mma pretend I didn't hear that.

506
00:25:28,319 --> 00:25:29,778
Yeah, probably for the best. [CHUCKLES]

507
00:25:29,779 --> 00:25:31,321
But look, if he shows his face,
we'll know.

508
00:25:31,322 --> 00:25:32,823
MAN: Do you have any mini-kegs?

509
00:25:33,616 --> 00:25:34,866
CASHIER: Down at the end.

510
00:25:34,867 --> 00:25:35,868
Thanks.

511
00:25:39,121 --> 00:25:40,248
I'll call you back.

512
00:25:42,458 --> 00:25:45,293
- Aha.
- [SLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

513
00:25:45,294 --> 00:25:46,295
Easy.

514
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:53,969
Hey, uh, also,
you got any Sharkfire Energy?

515
00:25:53,970 --> 00:25:55,346
Yeah.

516
00:25:56,514 --> 00:25:57,889
{\an8}Oh, no, no, no. [CHUCKLES]

517
00:25:57,890 --> 00:25:59,684
[STUTTERS] I don't want any.
That stuff will kill you.

518
00:26:00,101 --> 00:26:01,810
You know, all my friends
were drinking them during finals

519
00:26:01,811 --> 00:26:03,061
and now they're addicted.

520
00:26:03,062 --> 00:26:06,147
And so I'm gonna need you
to not sell me any.

521
00:26:06,148 --> 00:26:07,316
Memorize my face.

522
00:26:08,484 --> 00:26:12,029
Please do not sell this guy any Sharkfire.

523
00:26:12,905 --> 00:26:14,073
Sure. Whatever.

524
00:26:15,032 --> 00:26:16,242
NED: Actually, I'll take one.

525
00:26:16,993 --> 00:26:18,243
Last one.

526
00:26:18,244 --> 00:26:19,703
[STUTTERING] Maybe two.

527
00:26:19,704 --> 00:26:21,831
And then never sell me any.

528
00:26:23,416 --> 00:26:25,583
- [SOFTLY] Damn it.
- [CASH REGISTER BEEPING]

529
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:26,585
[CASH REGISTER DINGS]

530
00:26:39,390 --> 00:26:41,434
[POP SONG PLAYING]

531
00:26:52,403 --> 00:26:53,237
[EXHALES]

532
00:26:58,617 --> 00:26:59,868
MAN 1: Yo, Ned!

533
00:26:59,869 --> 00:27:01,244
- Oh, what?
- MAN 2: Ned!

534
00:27:01,245 --> 00:27:02,954
- Give me that.
- Oh, my guy, appreciate you.

535
00:27:02,955 --> 00:27:04,581
- Let's go!
- Yeah, man.

536
00:27:04,582 --> 00:27:05,583
Let's go!

537
00:27:20,348 --> 00:27:22,807
[SONG CONTINUES PLAYING OVER SPEAKER]

538
00:27:22,808 --> 00:27:24,810
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

539
00:27:32,693 --> 00:27:34,403
[WOMEN LAUGHING]

540
00:27:40,201 --> 00:27:42,952
You need a drink.
Take this, take this, take it.

541
00:27:42,953 --> 00:27:43,954
Thanks.

542
00:27:47,124 --> 00:27:48,125
WOMAN: Excuse me.

543
00:27:48,709 --> 00:27:50,544
[INDISTINCT CHATTER CONTINUES]

544
00:28:31,794 --> 00:28:32,628
Oh.

545
00:28:34,338 --> 00:28:35,713
Oh. Um...

546
00:28:35,714 --> 00:28:38,591
See you've stumbled across my board.
[CHUCKLES]

547
00:28:38,592 --> 00:28:40,094
I'm not one of those weirdos, I swear.

548
00:28:40,678 --> 00:28:43,013
He actually saved me and my friends' lives
a few times in high school.

549
00:28:44,181 --> 00:28:46,057
- Oh, cool.
- NED: Yeah, yeah.

550
00:28:46,058 --> 00:28:48,436
And ever since, I've just been trying
to figure out who he is.

551
00:28:48,727 --> 00:28:53,022
[STUTTERS] Not to unmask him to the world
or anything, just to know, you know?

552
00:28:53,023 --> 00:28:55,317
And to, hopefully, thank him face to face.

553
00:28:57,820 --> 00:29:01,157
I actually created this app
that monitors his sightings.

554
00:29:01,490 --> 00:29:03,116
Wait, you created Spidey Tracker?

555
00:29:03,117 --> 00:29:04,993
You heard of it? Nice. [CHUCKLES]

556
00:29:04,994 --> 00:29:06,077
{\an8}[<i>SPIDER-MAN</i> THEME PLAYING ON DEVICE]

557
00:29:06,078 --> 00:29:07,454
{\an8}APP VOICE: <i>Where is Spider-Man?</i>

558
00:29:07,455 --> 00:29:09,622
{\an8}NED: Little chat room
right there. [CHUCKLES]

559
00:29:09,623 --> 00:29:12,208
Now, we know he's definitely from Queens.

560
00:29:12,209 --> 00:29:13,419
Not the biggest revelation.

561
00:29:13,919 --> 00:29:18,549
But I have been able to narrow it down
to two prime suspects.

562
00:29:22,553 --> 00:29:25,930
Yeah, if you knew who they were,
it would really blow your mind.

563
00:29:25,931 --> 00:29:27,724
- I'm sure.
- [SIGHS]

564
00:29:27,725 --> 00:29:28,726
[CLICKS TONGUE] Ned, by the way.

565
00:29:29,643 --> 00:29:30,852
Oh, I'm, um...

566
00:29:30,853 --> 00:29:33,354
[EXHALES] God, there's, like,
50 people in our apartment.

567
00:29:33,355 --> 00:29:36,192
Statistically speaking, that means
at least two of them are sociopaths,

568
00:29:36,609 --> 00:29:38,861
- which is kind of cool.
- [NED LAUGHS]

569
00:29:40,946 --> 00:29:41,947
Nice flowers.

570
00:29:43,157 --> 00:29:46,576
Oh, they're, uh,
a housewarming gift.

571
00:29:46,577 --> 00:29:47,702
- MJ: Really?
- Yeah.

572
00:29:47,703 --> 00:29:50,538
Oh, okay. [CHUCKLES]
Most people just brought beer and chips.

573
00:29:50,539 --> 00:29:51,831
That's very nice.

574
00:29:51,832 --> 00:29:52,875
Uh, I'm MJ.

575
00:29:54,001 --> 00:29:57,421
I'm, uh... [CLEARS THROAT]
I'm, uh, Maynard.

576
00:29:58,339 --> 00:29:59,715
Uh, Maynard.

577
00:30:00,466 --> 00:30:02,926
Oh, you two don't know each other?

578
00:30:02,927 --> 00:30:04,969
Uh, no, I'm a neighbor.

579
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:06,055
Hmm, friendly neighbor.

580
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:08,015
[COUGHING]

581
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:10,935
[CHUCKLING] Sorry.

582
00:30:11,477 --> 00:30:13,020
So, how was the interview?

583
00:30:13,687 --> 00:30:14,855
I'm gonna go put these in water.

584
00:30:15,356 --> 00:30:17,273
It was nice to meet you, Maynard. Nerd.

585
00:30:17,274 --> 00:30:18,275
Maynard. Yeah.

586
00:30:18,943 --> 00:30:20,693
Excuse me. I'm sorry.

587
00:30:20,694 --> 00:30:23,571
Did you go? Please tell me that you went.

588
00:30:23,572 --> 00:30:24,781
MJ: Yeah. No, I went.

589
00:30:24,782 --> 00:30:26,324
And?

590
00:30:26,325 --> 00:30:27,534
And I got the job.

591
00:30:27,535 --> 00:30:29,744
Oh, my God, MJ, that's amazing.

592
00:30:29,745 --> 00:30:31,621
I turned it down.

593
00:30:31,622 --> 00:30:32,872
NED: What?

594
00:30:32,873 --> 00:30:35,250
MJ: Yeah. I don't wanna work
for some soulless corporation.

595
00:30:35,251 --> 00:30:38,128
NED: [SIGHS, STUTTERS]
They're not all soulless.

596
00:30:39,088 --> 00:30:41,047
Okay. They're all mostly soulless.

597
00:30:41,048 --> 00:30:43,007
But don't you want, like,
health insurance?

598
00:30:43,008 --> 00:30:45,343
Yeah, of course I do. But at what cost?

599
00:30:45,344 --> 00:30:46,971
Depends on your deductible.
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

600
00:30:48,055 --> 00:30:49,847
Oh, you mean,
like, your principles?

601
00:30:49,848 --> 00:30:51,015
- MJ: Yes.
- Sorry.

602
00:30:51,016 --> 00:30:52,433
I don't know. I know it sounds cheesy,

603
00:30:52,434 --> 00:30:54,852
but something is just telling me

604
00:30:54,853 --> 00:30:58,357
that I'm supposed to be waiting
for something great, you know?

605
00:30:59,567 --> 00:31:01,317
NED: Okay. Well, um,

606
00:31:01,318 --> 00:31:03,487
to, uh, waiting for something great.

607
00:31:04,113 --> 00:31:05,905
- MJ: To waiting for something great.
- [CLINKING]

608
00:31:05,906 --> 00:31:07,741
BOYFRIEND: Well, the wait is over.

609
00:31:08,117 --> 00:31:10,201
- Uh-oh. [LAUGHS]
- To your new home.

610
00:31:10,202 --> 00:31:11,619
Dude, this is top-shelf.

611
00:31:11,620 --> 00:31:12,745
BOYFRIEND: Just like you.

612
00:31:12,746 --> 00:31:15,416
- MJ: Aw!
- Aw! Dude. [GRUNTS]

613
00:31:16,041 --> 00:31:17,459
- I'm gonna hide this.
- [SNAPS FINGERS]

614
00:31:19,461 --> 00:31:20,879
I lifted this off of him again.

615
00:31:22,756 --> 00:31:25,466
But what if Ned needs
the fire of a thousand sharks?

616
00:31:25,467 --> 00:31:27,845
- You mean heart palpitations?
- [LAUGHING]

617
00:31:28,804 --> 00:31:30,514
- You can't save everyone.
- I can try.

618
00:31:33,058 --> 00:31:34,059
BOYFRIEND: That's my girl.

619
00:31:37,396 --> 00:31:39,565
[POIGNANT MUSIC PLAYING]

620
00:31:44,236 --> 00:31:45,946
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

621
00:31:50,701 --> 00:31:51,744
I'm sorry. I gotta...

622
00:31:56,874 --> 00:31:57,708
[GRUNTS]

623
00:31:59,460 --> 00:32:01,462
[POIGNANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

624
00:32:12,848 --> 00:32:15,768
When we get into MIT,
we should live together.

625
00:32:16,393 --> 00:32:18,228
PETER: <i>Yeah, for sure.</i>
MJ: <i>Yeah, I'd love that.</i>

626
00:32:18,687 --> 00:32:21,440
Be a fresh start.
And we'll all be together.

627
00:32:23,108 --> 00:32:24,567
Yeah, no, you're right. Yeah. [CHUCKLES]

628
00:32:24,568 --> 00:32:25,694
Fresh start.

629
00:32:28,781 --> 00:32:30,115
PETER: <i>You're gonna
forget who I am.</i>

630
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:32,825
MJ: <i>Forget who you are?
What are you talking about?</i>

631
00:32:32,826 --> 00:32:36,997
PETER: <i>It's okay. I'm gonna come
and find you, and I'll explain everything.</i>

632
00:32:38,290 --> 00:32:40,209
- I love...
- Just wait. [SNIFFLES]

633
00:32:40,793 --> 00:32:42,836
[VOICE SHAKING] Wait and tell me
when you see me again.

634
00:32:47,383 --> 00:32:51,428
My name is Peter Parker,
and I would like a coffee.

635
00:32:53,055 --> 00:32:55,224
Is there anything else?

636
00:32:57,267 --> 00:32:59,144
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

637
00:33:04,650 --> 00:33:05,651
No.

638
00:33:14,243 --> 00:33:15,869
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

639
00:33:19,415 --> 00:33:20,708
[RAIN PATTERING]

640
00:33:36,890 --> 00:33:38,308
[GRUNTING]

641
00:33:47,901 --> 00:33:49,445
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

642
00:34:05,753 --> 00:34:07,378
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

643
00:34:07,379 --> 00:34:08,464
MAY: <i>Hey.</i>

644
00:34:09,715 --> 00:34:10,716
Hey.

645
00:34:13,010 --> 00:34:16,346
You think you don't have to listen to me
now that you've got powers?

646
00:34:16,722 --> 00:34:18,724
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

647
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:26,732
You know, this... this whole thing
can get really scary.

648
00:34:27,524 --> 00:34:28,525
You know that?

649
00:34:29,902 --> 00:34:31,487
Well, yeah, it's already pretty scary.

650
00:34:33,781 --> 00:34:34,782
Yeah.

651
00:34:35,365 --> 00:34:38,326
And things can change,
like... [SNAPS FINGERS] ...very quickly,

652
00:34:38,327 --> 00:34:40,579
in ways that we can't
even imagine right now.

653
00:34:41,246 --> 00:34:42,581
Believe me, I know.

654
00:34:45,918 --> 00:34:47,252
I don't think you do know.

655
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:50,963
What do you mean?

656
00:34:50,964 --> 00:34:53,675
- [GASPS, PANTS]
- [SIRENS WAILING DISTANTLY]

657
00:35:10,234 --> 00:35:12,276
[GRUNTS, BREATHES HEAVILY]

658
00:35:12,277 --> 00:35:13,654
[GROANING]

659
00:35:16,490 --> 00:35:18,158
Oh, God. Whoa!

660
00:35:18,867 --> 00:35:21,328
[YELPING]

661
00:35:23,622 --> 00:35:25,414
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

662
00:35:25,415 --> 00:35:27,376
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

663
00:35:33,090 --> 00:35:35,383
[EXCLAIMS, YELPS]

664
00:35:35,384 --> 00:35:36,218
[THUDS]

665
00:35:39,680 --> 00:35:41,056
[EXCLAIMING IN PAIN]

666
00:35:48,772 --> 00:35:49,898
[GROANS]

667
00:35:59,908 --> 00:36:00,909
[SOFTLY] What?

668
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:03,579
[SIREN WAILS]

669
00:36:05,914 --> 00:36:07,291
[GRUNTING]

670
00:36:10,043 --> 00:36:11,253
[GROANS]

671
00:36:13,463 --> 00:36:14,464
[WINCES]

672
00:36:16,550 --> 00:36:18,885
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

673
00:36:18,886 --> 00:36:19,887
Oh, I, uh...

674
00:36:21,138 --> 00:36:22,264
I live here. I just, um...

675
00:36:24,766 --> 00:36:25,809
I'm gonna grab my stuff.

676
00:36:29,146 --> 00:36:30,230
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

677
00:36:44,536 --> 00:36:45,579
Is that my shirt?

678
00:36:46,538 --> 00:36:48,164
[CHUCKLES]

679
00:36:48,165 --> 00:36:49,166
No.

680
00:36:49,917 --> 00:36:51,208
- Oh, cute dog.
- [BARKS]

681
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:52,210
Oh, sh...

682
00:36:53,128 --> 00:36:55,379
[MASHING BUTTON]

683
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:57,049
- [CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]
- [ELEVATOR DINGS]

684
00:36:57,758 --> 00:36:59,176
PETER: [SIGHS] Okay.

685
00:37:03,263 --> 00:37:04,764
[GRUNTS, PANTING]

686
00:37:04,765 --> 00:37:06,767
[MYSTERIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

687
00:37:19,655 --> 00:37:23,074
E.V.: <i>Hi, Peter. You have 107 new alerts.</i>

688
00:37:23,075 --> 00:37:24,618
<i>Please check backlog.</i>

689
00:37:25,702 --> 00:37:27,703
[MACHINE WHIRRING]

690
00:37:27,704 --> 00:37:28,789
[MACHINE STOPS]

691
00:37:31,166 --> 00:37:34,461
What is happening?

692
00:37:35,545 --> 00:37:38,756
{\an8}E.V.: <i>The results of your body scan
show a surge in the hormones</i>

693
00:37:38,757 --> 00:37:41,051
<i>associated with your arachnid DNA,</i>

694
00:37:41,218 --> 00:37:44,095
<i>resulting in the formation
of organic web spinnerets</i>

695
00:37:44,096 --> 00:37:47,139
<i>and dangerously heightened
sensory receptors.</i>

696
00:37:47,140 --> 00:37:49,226
- [STUTTERS] Okay, but I feel fine.
- [WEB SHOOTER CLICKING]

697
00:37:49,476 --> 00:37:51,852
{\an8}E.V.: <i>Prolonged isolation
or emotional trauma</i>

698
00:37:51,853 --> 00:37:54,397
{\an8}<i>could be contributing
to this sudden change.</i>

699
00:37:54,398 --> 00:37:57,067
<i>Have you experienced any
recent traumatic events?</i>

700
00:37:59,903 --> 00:38:00,904
<i>Peter?</i>

701
00:38:01,530 --> 00:38:03,155
SPIDER-MAN: I'm fine, E.V.

702
00:38:03,156 --> 00:38:04,615
E.V.: <i>You don't seem fine.</i>

703
00:38:04,616 --> 00:38:05,783
<i>I recommend you take</i>

704
00:38:05,784 --> 00:38:07,326
<i>- some time to rebalance.</i>
- [GADGET BEEPS]

705
00:38:07,327 --> 00:38:09,079
Well, that's not really an option, is it?

706
00:38:12,207 --> 00:38:14,584
- [FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [CLATTERING]

707
00:38:15,419 --> 00:38:17,421
[SQUELCHING]

708
00:38:20,048 --> 00:38:21,132
[CLANKING]

709
00:38:21,133 --> 00:38:22,134
[OBJECTS SHATTER]

710
00:38:25,595 --> 00:38:28,055
E.V.: <i>Mechanical web shooters
and organic webs</i>

711
00:38:28,056 --> 00:38:30,225
<i>cannot be used simultaneously.</i>

712
00:38:31,727 --> 00:38:32,978
SPIDER-MAN: Come on, Peter.

713
00:38:34,271 --> 00:38:36,022
[CAR HORN HONKING]

714
00:38:36,023 --> 00:38:38,316
- [BREATHING DEEPLY]
- [TIME SLOWS DOWN]

715
00:38:39,443 --> 00:38:42,487
- [SLOWED WATER DRIPPING]
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]

716
00:38:46,283 --> 00:38:48,160
[REVERBERATES]

717
00:38:48,785 --> 00:38:50,829
[PRONOUNCED CRINKLING]

718
00:38:52,831 --> 00:38:55,416
E.V.: <i>Alert. Senses are overloaded.</i>

719
00:38:55,417 --> 00:38:57,460
- [WINGS FLAPPING SHARPLY]
- [SIREN CHIRPS, WAILS SHARPLY]

720
00:38:57,461 --> 00:38:59,837
- [PANTING]
- E.V.: <i>Alert. Senses are overloaded.</i>

721
00:38:59,838 --> 00:39:02,173
[GARBLED, OVERLAPPING SOUNDS]

722
00:39:02,174 --> 00:39:05,217
E.V.: [ECHOING] <i>Alert. Alert.
Senses are overloaded. Alert.</i>

723
00:39:05,218 --> 00:39:07,888
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANS, PANTS]
- [SOUNDS SUBSIDE]

724
00:39:08,889 --> 00:39:10,557
What the hell was that?

725
00:39:11,058 --> 00:39:14,977
E.V.: <i>Your heightened senses are taking in
too much information at once.</i>

726
00:39:14,978 --> 00:39:18,272
SPIDER-MAN: [BREATHING HEAVILY]
Okay. It's okay.

727
00:39:18,273 --> 00:39:19,356
It's okay.

728
00:39:19,357 --> 00:39:22,068
All right, organic webs.
Peter Two had 'em.

729
00:39:22,069 --> 00:39:23,862
He was cool. You're cool.

730
00:39:24,654 --> 00:39:27,157
[SQUELCHING]

731
00:39:27,616 --> 00:39:29,825
[GAGS, RETCHES]

732
00:39:29,826 --> 00:39:31,786
[COUGHS]

733
00:39:31,787 --> 00:39:34,205
Ugh! Oh, my God, that's hideous.

734
00:39:34,206 --> 00:39:36,041
[EXCLAIMS] Okay, here we go.

735
00:39:36,750 --> 00:39:37,834
[GRUNTS]

736
00:39:38,293 --> 00:39:41,087
Okay, that didn't work. [GRUNTS, GROANS]

737
00:39:41,088 --> 00:39:43,297
Organic webs. Come on! And web!

738
00:39:43,298 --> 00:39:45,133
[GROANING]

739
00:39:46,843 --> 00:39:47,844
No, no!

740
00:39:50,889 --> 00:39:52,724
Stop! [PANTING]

741
00:39:54,142 --> 00:39:56,394
- [SUIT BEEPING]
- What's going on, E.V.?

742
00:39:57,020 --> 00:40:00,731
E.V.: <i>Shots fired at the Damage Control
Data Center in Manhattan.</i>

743
00:40:00,732 --> 00:40:03,192
<i>Suspect facial match with Scorpion.</i>

744
00:40:03,193 --> 00:40:04,528
SPIDER-MAN: Okay, I'm on my way.

745
00:40:05,237 --> 00:40:06,947
Come on. Three, two...

746
00:40:07,280 --> 00:40:08,364
Web! [GRUNTS]

747
00:40:08,365 --> 00:40:11,700
[STRAINING, SCREAMING]

748
00:40:11,701 --> 00:40:14,662
- Web, stop! [GROANS]
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

749
00:40:14,663 --> 00:40:15,788
[SCREAMS]

750
00:40:15,789 --> 00:40:17,915
Web! Stop! Birds, birds, birds!

751
00:40:17,916 --> 00:40:19,750
[GROANING] Web! Stop.

752
00:40:19,751 --> 00:40:22,212
- [PIGEON COOS]
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

753
00:40:24,047 --> 00:40:25,340
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

754
00:40:26,133 --> 00:40:27,716
Web! Stop.

755
00:40:27,717 --> 00:40:29,552
Oh, God! [GROANS]

756
00:40:29,553 --> 00:40:32,346
- Web! Stop, stop, stop. [YELLS]
- [MUSIC ENDS]

757
00:40:32,347 --> 00:40:34,098
- [PEOPLE SCREAMING]
- [SIREN WAILING]

758
00:40:34,099 --> 00:40:36,101
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

759
00:40:37,686 --> 00:40:39,812
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

760
00:40:39,813 --> 00:40:41,398
[GUARD SCREAMS, GROANS]

761
00:40:42,566 --> 00:40:43,567
[GUNS FIRING]

762
00:40:45,861 --> 00:40:47,279
[BULLETS RICOCHETING]

763
00:40:48,989 --> 00:40:51,282
- [OFFICERS SCREAMING]
- [CAR ALARMS BLARING]

764
00:40:51,283 --> 00:40:52,868
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

765
00:40:55,453 --> 00:40:57,538
I don't know what you're looking for.

766
00:40:57,539 --> 00:40:59,499
I'm looking for V-Max.

767
00:41:00,417 --> 00:41:02,084
[GUARD GASPING]

768
00:41:02,085 --> 00:41:04,336
I don't know anything.

769
00:41:04,337 --> 00:41:05,839
SCORPION: I'll see for myself.

770
00:41:06,673 --> 00:41:08,966
[SPIDER-MAN SCREAMING]

771
00:41:08,967 --> 00:41:11,093
- Oh, God, oh, God!
- [THUDDING]

772
00:41:11,094 --> 00:41:13,096
[SPIDER-MAN YELPING]

773
00:41:14,306 --> 00:41:15,682
- [GROANS]
- Hmm.

774
00:41:16,641 --> 00:41:18,310
- [GUARD YELPS]
- [BODY THUDS]

775
00:41:18,602 --> 00:41:21,229
SPIDER-MAN: I'm sorry I'm late.
I've had a really crazy day.

776
00:41:22,772 --> 00:41:24,524
[GROANING]

777
00:41:29,571 --> 00:41:31,156
[BOTH GRUNTING]

778
00:41:39,831 --> 00:41:43,210
SPIDER-MAN: Scorpion, do we really gotta
keep doing this? My head is killing me.

779
00:41:44,252 --> 00:41:45,712
You think I'm Scorpion?

780
00:41:47,464 --> 00:41:48,465
- Web!
- [SQUIRTS]

781
00:41:50,467 --> 00:41:51,885
What's happening to you?

782
00:41:52,344 --> 00:41:53,637
[BOTH GRUNTING]

783
00:41:58,308 --> 00:41:59,767
Huh.

784
00:41:59,768 --> 00:42:01,311
You can't sense me anymore.

785
00:42:01,770 --> 00:42:03,146
[BOTH GRUNTING]

786
00:42:04,773 --> 00:42:05,856
SPIDER-MAN: You.

787
00:42:05,857 --> 00:42:07,733
What's going on with you, Spider-Man?

788
00:42:07,734 --> 00:42:09,736
- [METAL CREAKING]
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

789
00:42:16,993 --> 00:42:19,662
{\an8}E.V.: <i>Warning.
Arachnid hormones increasing.</i>

790
00:42:19,663 --> 00:42:21,288
- [SUIT BEEPING]
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

791
00:42:21,289 --> 00:42:22,290
[DISTORTED WARBLE]

792
00:42:23,792 --> 00:42:25,794
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

793
00:42:27,963 --> 00:42:29,881
[SCORPION GROANING]

794
00:42:34,052 --> 00:42:34,886
[GROANS]

795
00:42:35,345 --> 00:42:36,388
SPIDER-MAN: Who are you?

796
00:42:37,347 --> 00:42:38,806
Do you know who you are?

797
00:42:38,807 --> 00:42:40,225
[SIREN WAILING]

798
00:42:42,644 --> 00:42:44,020
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

799
00:42:48,483 --> 00:42:50,193
[SIRENS APPROACHING]

800
00:42:51,111 --> 00:42:53,530
- [CRACKLING]
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

801
00:42:57,409 --> 00:42:58,868
[SCORPION GROANING]

802
00:43:02,914 --> 00:43:04,957
OFFICER 1: We need some help over here.
OFFICER 2: Get back! Coming through.

803
00:43:04,958 --> 00:43:06,459
[BOTH GRUNT]

804
00:43:08,837 --> 00:43:10,213
- [EXHALES]
- [WHOOSHES]

805
00:43:11,047 --> 00:43:12,841
[GASPS, BREATHES DEEPLY]

806
00:43:13,925 --> 00:43:15,010
Spider-Man.

807
00:43:16,136 --> 00:43:17,678
[EXHALES]

808
00:43:17,679 --> 00:43:18,805
What the hell?

809
00:43:19,139 --> 00:43:20,681
DEWOLFF: Somebody get a medic.

810
00:43:20,682 --> 00:43:22,808
[SPIDER-MAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

811
00:43:22,809 --> 00:43:24,893
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

812
00:43:24,894 --> 00:43:26,896
[CHATTER ECHOING]

813
00:43:37,615 --> 00:43:38,992
[SPIDER-MAN EXHALES]

814
00:43:40,994 --> 00:43:42,037
DeWolff, is she hurt?

815
00:43:43,204 --> 00:43:44,205
Is she okay?

816
00:43:44,622 --> 00:43:46,040
- Is she okay?
- DEWOLFF: No!

817
00:43:46,041 --> 00:43:48,208
- SPIDER-MAN: Just let me go...
- Don't! What is going on with you?

818
00:43:48,209 --> 00:43:49,460
SPIDER-MAN: That wasn't Scorpion, okay?

819
00:43:49,461 --> 00:43:50,544
[STUTTERING] I mean it was,

820
00:43:50,545 --> 00:43:53,380
but he was possessed by whatever hijacked
that tank, okay?

821
00:43:53,381 --> 00:43:55,591
- Look, please can I just...
- All right, listen. Slow down.

822
00:43:55,592 --> 00:43:58,052
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING IN PAIN]

823
00:43:58,053 --> 00:44:01,848
Listen, I don't know what this is,
but I need you to pull it together.

824
00:44:02,432 --> 00:44:03,933
You almost killed a cop.

825
00:44:06,728 --> 00:44:08,354
This isn't you.

826
00:44:08,355 --> 00:44:09,397
SPIDER-MAN: I know. I'm sorry.

827
00:44:09,981 --> 00:44:12,567
If you act like this again,
I cannot protect you.

828
00:44:13,568 --> 00:44:16,403
Whatever this is, you need to fix it.

829
00:44:16,404 --> 00:44:18,406
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

830
00:44:27,374 --> 00:44:28,375
[GRUNTS]

831
00:44:31,878 --> 00:44:32,921
[GROANS SOFTLY]

832
00:44:35,173 --> 00:44:36,800
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

833
00:44:37,592 --> 00:44:39,886
PROFESSOR: <i>Through lattice chromodynamics,</i>

834
00:44:41,262 --> 00:44:45,057
we can arrange time and space in a grid.

835
00:44:45,058 --> 00:44:50,021
Which allows us to simulate
the quarks binding into the protons.

836
00:44:51,064 --> 00:44:53,399
Cindy, is this a question about protons

837
00:44:53,400 --> 00:44:55,567
- or more stuff about Avengers?
- [SCATTERED LAUGHTER]

838
00:44:55,568 --> 00:44:59,029
[CHUCKLES] Okay.
Guys, I love to tell stories,

839
00:44:59,030 --> 00:45:02,116
but you know I... I gotta teach you
some physics at some point here.

840
00:45:02,117 --> 00:45:04,035
[STUDENTS BOOING, JEERING]

841
00:45:06,413 --> 00:45:08,747
All right. Let it rip, Cindy.

842
00:45:08,748 --> 00:45:11,543
If Thanos was so worried
about over-population,

843
00:45:12,001 --> 00:45:15,004
why didn't he just use the magic glove
to make more food?

844
00:45:15,839 --> 00:45:17,757
[STUDENTS MURMURING]

845
00:45:19,092 --> 00:45:21,219
Arthur, you wanna answer that question?

846
00:45:22,053 --> 00:45:25,639
Hulk smash!

847
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:27,434
[STUDENTS CHEERING]

848
00:45:29,060 --> 00:45:30,186
There you have it.

849
00:45:30,770 --> 00:45:33,815
- [BANNER HUMMING]
- Uh, excuse me, Dr. Banner, I, um...

850
00:45:34,649 --> 00:45:35,650
Uh...

851
00:45:36,234 --> 00:45:38,152
- You okay?
- Yeah, sorry, it's just a headache.

852
00:45:38,153 --> 00:45:40,822
Um, have you got a minute? I wanted
to talk to you about your inhibitor.

853
00:45:41,781 --> 00:45:45,784
Oh. Sure. Don't worry.
It's got fail-safes.

854
00:45:45,785 --> 00:45:49,956
I'm not gonna turn into the big green
raging monster machine in the cafeteria.

855
00:45:50,540 --> 00:45:53,125
But if you do see me
with this thing off, run.

856
00:45:53,126 --> 00:45:55,420
- [GROWLS]
- [BOTH LAUGHING]

857
00:45:56,588 --> 00:45:59,883
No, but you're using target-specific
short interfering RNA, right?

858
00:46:01,384 --> 00:46:04,304
It's like gene silencing, you're just
incorporating the gamma radiation?

859
00:46:06,931 --> 00:46:08,057
What'd you say your name was?

860
00:46:09,350 --> 00:46:11,978
Uh, Ned... Leeds.

861
00:46:12,604 --> 00:46:15,731
So you found a way
to suppress the expression of DNA

862
00:46:15,732 --> 00:46:18,775
even as it's undergoing the mutation
due to gamma radiation, right?

863
00:46:18,776 --> 00:46:21,279
- Yes.
- Okay, so my question is,

864
00:46:22,071 --> 00:46:26,993
would that same thing be possible with DNA
that's mutating for another reason?

865
00:46:29,078 --> 00:46:30,121
What's the reason?

866
00:46:31,581 --> 00:46:34,124
[CHUCKLING] I don't know.
Uh... [SNIFFS]

867
00:46:34,125 --> 00:46:38,170
Let's say that the... the host genome
is mixed with some kind of foreign DNA.

868
00:46:38,171 --> 00:46:39,214
Theoretically.

869
00:46:40,340 --> 00:46:42,926
Theoretically? Yes, that's possible. Yes.

870
00:46:43,927 --> 00:46:47,262
So, could you suppress
only some parts of that DNA expression?

871
00:46:47,263 --> 00:46:49,807
Like the bad aspects
but just keep all of the good stuff?

872
00:46:50,683 --> 00:46:53,769
You mean, like, if I wanted to keep
some parts of Hulk but not others?

873
00:46:53,770 --> 00:46:54,979
Right.

874
00:46:55,396 --> 00:46:59,400
It would be enormously dangerous
and complex, but...

875
00:47:00,693 --> 00:47:04,489
if you were able to target
the correct mRNA strand...

876
00:47:05,365 --> 00:47:06,532
Possibly.

877
00:47:06,533 --> 00:47:09,076
Wait, so you could just
turn the mutating gene on and off

878
00:47:09,077 --> 00:47:11,621
as long as you do it
before the mRNA transcription?

879
00:47:12,247 --> 00:47:13,248
Maybe.

880
00:47:15,500 --> 00:47:17,710
I mean, if you apply the same thinking,
you could even...

881
00:47:18,419 --> 00:47:20,546
develop some kind of automatic inhibitor

882
00:47:20,547 --> 00:47:23,508
that would just adjust
to any type of mutation.

883
00:47:24,592 --> 00:47:27,511
Well, now you're talking about
a universal inhibitor

884
00:47:27,512 --> 00:47:30,640
that would control anyone
who has any powers.

885
00:47:32,016 --> 00:47:33,226
It's a dangerous idea.

886
00:47:34,435 --> 00:47:36,437
Well, yeah. But it's theoretical, right?

887
00:47:39,148 --> 00:47:40,650
You're not one of my students, are ya?

888
00:47:43,152 --> 00:47:44,946
- No. I'm a grad student.
- Hmm.

889
00:47:45,488 --> 00:47:47,573
I've, uh... [CLEARS THROAT]

890
00:47:47,574 --> 00:47:48,740
I've taken enough of your time.

891
00:47:48,741 --> 00:47:50,660
I gotta get some books
back to the library.

892
00:47:51,244 --> 00:47:52,579
The library is that way.

893
00:47:54,581 --> 00:47:56,832
Right. Right. [CHUCKLES] Duh.

894
00:47:56,833 --> 00:47:58,167
How would you decide?

895
00:47:59,043 --> 00:48:00,044
What's that?

896
00:48:01,129 --> 00:48:03,089
Well, what parts of nature
are good or bad?

897
00:48:03,923 --> 00:48:05,924
What if you're trying
to control the expression

898
00:48:05,925 --> 00:48:07,927
of something that needs to be expressed?

899
00:48:08,970 --> 00:48:10,930
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

900
00:48:13,725 --> 00:48:15,184
Good luck with your studies, Ned.

901
00:48:17,186 --> 00:48:18,605
Thank you, Professor.

902
00:48:19,439 --> 00:48:20,647
NARRATOR: <i>Like reptiles...</i>

903
00:48:20,648 --> 00:48:23,108
{\an8}- PETER: Oh, God.
<i>- ...amphibians and arthropods,</i>

904
00:48:23,109 --> 00:48:24,401
{\an8}<i>spiders shed skin</i>

905
00:48:24,402 --> 00:48:26,321
<i>- at key points in their life cycles.
-</i> [CRACKLING]

906
00:48:26,613 --> 00:48:28,780
<i>- The process is known as molting.
-</i> [COMPUTER TRILLS, BEEPS]

907
00:48:28,781 --> 00:48:31,325
E.V.: <i>Fourth inhibitor prototype complete.</i>

908
00:48:31,326 --> 00:48:32,492
NARRATOR: <i>While molting is a natural</i>

909
00:48:32,493 --> 00:48:34,870
<i>- part of a spider's life cycle...</i>
- PETER: Okay, come on. Come on.

910
00:48:34,871 --> 00:48:36,913
NARRATOR: <i>...it can leave the spider
vulnerable to threats.</i>

911
00:48:36,914 --> 00:48:39,333
Upload inhibitor beta build seven.

912
00:48:39,334 --> 00:48:40,709
{\an8}NARRATOR: <i>...process is
initiated by hormonal changes...</i>

913
00:48:40,710 --> 00:48:42,837
{\an8}E.V.: <i>Uploaded.
Would you like to run a test?</i>

914
00:48:43,504 --> 00:48:44,588
Yeah, run it.

915
00:48:44,589 --> 00:48:46,423
{\an8}NARRATOR: <i>...few hours to several days.</i>

916
00:48:46,424 --> 00:48:50,136
{\an8}<i>Spiders have three stages
in their life cycle.</i>

917
00:48:50,303 --> 00:48:53,597
{\an8}<i>Each stage is characterized
by physical changes,</i>

918
00:48:53,598 --> 00:48:58,811
{\an8}<i>with the largest changes occurring during
the beautiful transition to adulthood.</i>

919
00:49:01,397 --> 00:49:02,774
<i>For those who make it through,</i>

920
00:49:03,274 --> 00:49:05,651
<i>molting amounts to a kind of rebirth.</i>

921
00:49:05,652 --> 00:49:07,110
Can you turn that spider stuff off?

922
00:49:07,111 --> 00:49:08,488
E.V.: <i>Turning off video.</i>

923
00:49:09,364 --> 00:49:10,906
<i>- Inhibitor active.</i>
- Okay, here we go.

924
00:49:10,907 --> 00:49:12,909
Come on. Come on. [SNIFFS]

925
00:49:13,826 --> 00:49:15,328
Keep an eye on my vitals.

926
00:49:16,537 --> 00:49:17,788
- [DEVICE BEEPS]
- [PETER GROANS]

927
00:49:17,789 --> 00:49:19,373
E.V.: <i>Inhibitor engaged.</i>

928
00:49:19,374 --> 00:49:21,376
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

929
00:49:23,294 --> 00:49:26,881
{\an8}<i>Suppressing arachnid hormones
to your baseline levels.</i>

930
00:49:27,548 --> 00:49:28,925
[SIGHS SOFTLY]

931
00:49:29,759 --> 00:49:30,760
Okay.

932
00:49:33,554 --> 00:49:34,805
[GRUNTS]

933
00:49:34,806 --> 00:49:36,390
All right, E.V., let's do this.

934
00:49:36,391 --> 00:49:38,351
E.V.: <i>Initiating field test one.</i>

935
00:49:40,311 --> 00:49:42,020
SPIDER-MAN: That's working.
E.V.: <i>Alert.</i>

936
00:49:42,021 --> 00:49:44,272
{\an8}- [SUIT BEEPING RAPIDLY]
<i>- Inhibitor is overheating.</i>

937
00:49:44,273 --> 00:49:45,524
{\an8}<i>Functionality reducing.</i>

938
00:49:45,525 --> 00:49:47,317
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, I'm sensing that.

939
00:49:47,318 --> 00:49:49,277
- E.V.: <i>Alert. Senses are overloaded.
-</i> [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

940
00:49:49,278 --> 00:49:51,154
E.V.: [ECHOING] <i>Alert.
Senses are overloaded.</i>

941
00:49:51,155 --> 00:49:53,490
<i>- Senses are overloaded. Alert.</i>
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

942
00:49:53,491 --> 00:49:56,034
- [WEB CARTRIDGES CLINK, CLATTER]
- E.V.: <i>Web grenades activated.</i>

943
00:49:56,035 --> 00:49:57,036
{\an8}[BEEPING RAPIDLY]

944
00:49:58,037 --> 00:49:59,705
- SPIDER-MAN: Oh, sh...
- [EXPLOSION]

945
00:49:59,706 --> 00:50:01,833
- [PEOPLE GASPING]
- [CLATTERING]

946
00:50:03,960 --> 00:50:06,754
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANING]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

947
00:50:11,509 --> 00:50:13,969
E.V.: <i>Inhibitor field test one, failure.</i>

948
00:50:13,970 --> 00:50:16,139
- [DEVICE POWERS OFF]
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

949
00:50:16,723 --> 00:50:19,559
Yo, Spider-Man, you okay?

950
00:50:20,226 --> 00:50:22,311
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.
I'm just trying out some new tech.

951
00:50:22,854 --> 00:50:25,773
Oh, yeah. To get rid
of that monster inside you?

952
00:50:26,357 --> 00:50:28,359
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

953
00:50:31,195 --> 00:50:32,613
Still can't sense me, huh?

954
00:50:34,282 --> 00:50:36,159
Guess your technology isn't working.

955
00:50:37,326 --> 00:50:39,662
You know, you're the only person
I've met that I can't...

956
00:50:40,705 --> 00:50:41,914
hop into.

957
00:50:42,749 --> 00:50:44,833
SPIDER-MAN: I'm sure that's really
frustrating for you.

958
00:50:44,834 --> 00:50:46,334
Oh, I'll get in there one day.

959
00:50:46,335 --> 00:50:47,462
SPIDER-MAN: What do you want?

960
00:50:47,587 --> 00:50:48,588
Oh, boy.

961
00:50:49,338 --> 00:50:54,843
I wanna know why a half-human, half-spider
would decide to work for an organization

962
00:50:54,844 --> 00:50:58,472
whose sworn mission
is to hunt down anybody who's different.

963
00:50:58,473 --> 00:51:01,934
SPIDER-MAN: [SCOFFS] Damage Control
isn't after you because you're different.

964
00:51:02,685 --> 00:51:04,644
They're hunting you down
because you're dangerous.

965
00:51:04,645 --> 00:51:06,314
Now, what do you want?

966
00:51:06,939 --> 00:51:10,985
Since you're a very simple spider,
let me spell it out for you.

967
00:51:12,111 --> 00:51:14,530
Damage Control has something that I need.

968
00:51:15,448 --> 00:51:16,824
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, you mean V-Max?

969
00:51:19,827 --> 00:51:23,039
I was planning to use Scorpion to get it,
but you keep getting in my way.

970
00:51:23,790 --> 00:51:26,374
SPIDER-MAN: I will always be in your way.

971
00:51:26,375 --> 00:51:28,961
Oh, you sure about that, Peter Parker?

972
00:51:29,587 --> 00:51:31,589
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CRESCENDOES]

973
00:51:34,133 --> 00:51:37,302
<i>You know, your apartment
is kinda like a parody</i>

974
00:51:37,303 --> 00:51:40,598
of where you think a sad single guy
in his 20s might live.

975
00:51:41,057 --> 00:51:45,770
Take-out containers,
free weights, protein powder.

976
00:51:47,021 --> 00:51:49,232
[LAUGHING]

977
00:51:50,608 --> 00:51:52,025
SPIDER-MAN: You're bluffing.

978
00:51:52,026 --> 00:51:53,903
You know,
you're not hard to track down, Peter.

979
00:51:54,529 --> 00:51:57,573
Well, at least not for someone like me.

980
00:51:58,866 --> 00:52:00,952
I did find one interesting thing, though.

981
00:52:02,203 --> 00:52:03,496
<i>In of all places...</i>

982
00:52:05,706 --> 00:52:06,749
coffee cup.

983
00:52:09,377 --> 00:52:11,087
SPIDER-MAN: E.V.,
display home work station.

984
00:52:13,631 --> 00:52:17,134
MAN: You spent four years
erasing Peter Parker from existence?

985
00:52:18,094 --> 00:52:20,680
No wonder the spider's
trying to swallow up the man.

986
00:52:21,222 --> 00:52:23,182
I wonder if MJ would even recognize you.

987
00:52:24,433 --> 00:52:26,643
- [GROANS]
- [WHOOSHES]

988
00:52:26,644 --> 00:52:28,353
I think I might go see how she's doing.

989
00:52:28,354 --> 00:52:29,563
SPIDER-MAN: I'm not gonna let that happen.

990
00:52:29,564 --> 00:52:31,565
No, her roommate was nice enough

991
00:52:31,566 --> 00:52:33,775
- to post a new address online.
- [WHOOSHES]

992
00:52:33,776 --> 00:52:36,445
How about this? I'll race you there.

993
00:52:36,946 --> 00:52:37,947
SPIDER-MAN: If you touch her...

994
00:52:38,614 --> 00:52:40,282
Better start swinging.

995
00:52:40,283 --> 00:52:41,741
I'm fast.

996
00:52:41,742 --> 00:52:42,909
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

997
00:52:42,910 --> 00:52:45,204
- [WHOOSHING]
- [PEOPLE GROANING]

998
00:52:50,042 --> 00:52:51,668
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

999
00:52:51,669 --> 00:52:54,130
[GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

1000
00:52:55,882 --> 00:52:58,301
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1001
00:53:02,305 --> 00:53:04,223
[YELLS, GRUNTS]

1002
00:53:05,016 --> 00:53:06,182
MAN: Hey.

1003
00:53:06,183 --> 00:53:08,310
It's a long way to MJ's.

1004
00:53:08,311 --> 00:53:10,854
- [WHOOSHES]
- You better pick up the pace.

1005
00:53:10,855 --> 00:53:13,357
- [WHOOSHING]
- [PEOPLE GROANING]

1006
00:53:17,695 --> 00:53:19,697
SPIDER-MAN: E.V.,
track physical anomalies.

1007
00:53:20,865 --> 00:53:22,365
{\an8}E.V.: <i>Searching for physical anomalies</i>

1008
00:53:22,366 --> 00:53:23,909
{\an8}<i>-between subjects.</i>
- [COMPUTER BEEPING]

1009
00:53:23,910 --> 00:53:25,035
{\an8}<i>Please stand by.</i>

1010
00:53:25,036 --> 00:53:27,663
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING, SCREAMING]

1011
00:53:28,456 --> 00:53:29,581
[SPIDER-MAN EXCLAIMS]

1012
00:53:29,582 --> 00:53:32,083
Thank you all so much for coming today.

1013
00:53:32,084 --> 00:53:34,836
- [SHATTERING]
- [PEOPLE EXCLAIMING]

1014
00:53:34,837 --> 00:53:36,756
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1015
00:53:37,882 --> 00:53:40,383
Uh... I'm sorry about that.

1016
00:53:40,384 --> 00:53:42,427
Give it up for Spider-Man,

1017
00:53:42,428 --> 00:53:45,764
in a race for the love of his life,
and it's not looking good.

1018
00:53:45,765 --> 00:53:47,933
- [WHOOSHES]
- [BRIDE GASPS]

1019
00:53:47,934 --> 00:53:50,186
Come on, Spidey. Keep up.

1020
00:53:51,270 --> 00:53:52,354
SPIDER-MAN: Excuse me. Sorry.

1021
00:53:52,355 --> 00:53:54,899
- [WHOOSHING]
- [PEOPLE GROANING]

1022
00:53:58,110 --> 00:54:00,112
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

1023
00:54:01,155 --> 00:54:02,238
WOMAN: Spider-Man!

1024
00:54:02,239 --> 00:54:03,908
[TRACKER BEEPING]

1025
00:54:05,826 --> 00:54:07,662
SPIDER-MAN: E.V.,
run these numbers with the others.

1026
00:54:09,121 --> 00:54:10,122
[GRUNTS]

1027
00:54:10,957 --> 00:54:13,375
{\an8}E.V.: <i>Analyzing jump distances
for patterns.</i>

1028
00:54:13,376 --> 00:54:15,669
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1029
00:54:15,670 --> 00:54:17,004
Get me that jump data.

1030
00:54:17,421 --> 00:54:18,505
{\an8}E.V.: <i>Calculating.</i>

1031
00:54:18,506 --> 00:54:19,840
[SPIDER-MAN SCREAMING]

1032
00:54:22,301 --> 00:54:24,010
Come on, I need an answer!

1033
00:54:24,011 --> 00:54:25,553
{\an8}[COMPUTER BEEPING]

1034
00:54:25,554 --> 00:54:27,139
{\an8}E.V.: <i>Calculations complete.</i>

1035
00:54:30,851 --> 00:54:33,062
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
- [MAN GRUNTS]

1036
00:54:42,738 --> 00:54:44,907
SPIDER-MAN: You have a limit
to your jump radius, don't ya?

1037
00:54:45,491 --> 00:54:46,575
Thirty-three feet.

1038
00:54:47,576 --> 00:54:49,829
I don't see anybody up here
for you to hop into.

1039
00:54:51,205 --> 00:54:52,331
Very clever.

1040
00:54:52,790 --> 00:54:55,960
Like I said, you're not getting near her.

1041
00:54:56,794 --> 00:54:59,130
[HEROIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1042
00:55:06,429 --> 00:55:09,015
[UPBEAT SONG PLAYING OVER HEADPHONES]

1043
00:55:09,974 --> 00:55:12,225
- [THUDS]
- MJ: [GASPS] Hey, hey, hey.

1044
00:55:12,226 --> 00:55:13,268
SPIDER-MAN: I'm sorry,
but you're in danger.

1045
00:55:13,269 --> 00:55:14,352
- Where's your roommate?
- What?

1046
00:55:14,353 --> 00:55:15,437
SPIDER-MAN: Where's Ned?

1047
00:55:15,438 --> 00:55:16,688
Uh, in Boston with friends. Why?

1048
00:55:16,689 --> 00:55:18,064
SPIDER-MAN: Okay, good.
You gotta come with me.

1049
00:55:18,065 --> 00:55:19,858
What? I don't know
if you're the real Spider-Man.

1050
00:55:19,859 --> 00:55:21,443
- I'm not coming with you.
- We don't have time for this.

1051
00:55:21,444 --> 00:55:23,695
- Please. Come on.
- You need to get out of my apartment.

1052
00:55:23,696 --> 00:55:25,155
Look, this is gonna sound insane,

1053
00:55:25,156 --> 00:55:27,741
but there is someone who is after you
who is really dangerous, okay?

1054
00:55:27,742 --> 00:55:29,617
And I promised you
that I would keep you safe.

1055
00:55:29,618 --> 00:55:32,580
[PANTING] Please,
you just have to trust me. Come on.

1056
00:55:36,042 --> 00:55:37,208
Fine.

1057
00:55:37,209 --> 00:55:39,544
[SOMBER INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

1058
00:55:39,545 --> 00:55:42,256
- [CARS HONKING]
- [SIREN WAILING]

1059
00:55:43,799 --> 00:55:44,967
SPIDER-MAN: [SOFTLY] Web. Stop.

1060
00:55:48,471 --> 00:55:49,472
Web. Stop.

1061
00:55:53,642 --> 00:55:54,727
Web. Stop.

1062
00:55:59,190 --> 00:56:01,775
- [GRUNTS] Are you okay?
- MJ: Yeah, yeah, I'm fine.

1063
00:56:01,776 --> 00:56:04,360
SPIDER-MAN: Okay.
Uh, we should be safe up here.

1064
00:56:04,361 --> 00:56:05,528
MJ: Okay, well, safe from what?

1065
00:56:05,529 --> 00:56:08,198
SPIDER-MAN: Uh, I'm not entirely sure.

1066
00:56:08,199 --> 00:56:09,824
Okay, well, what do they want with me?

1067
00:56:09,825 --> 00:56:12,161
SPIDER-MAN: [STUTTERS] I don't know.
MJ: You don't know?

1068
00:56:12,703 --> 00:56:15,289
[STUTTERS] It doesn't make any sense.
Why would they choose me?

1069
00:56:15,873 --> 00:56:18,124
SPIDER-MAN: Um, I wish I could tell you.
I just...

1070
00:56:18,125 --> 00:56:19,126
Uh...

1071
00:56:20,753 --> 00:56:22,296
We knew each other, didn't we?

1072
00:56:25,966 --> 00:56:26,967
SPIDER-MAN: What?

1073
00:56:27,968 --> 00:56:29,303
It's the only explanation.

1074
00:56:30,638 --> 00:56:32,097
It's been driving me crazy for years,

1075
00:56:32,098 --> 00:56:34,433
all the times that Spider-Man
saved either me or Ned.

1076
00:56:35,184 --> 00:56:36,351
It was the Washington Monument,

1077
00:56:36,352 --> 00:56:38,896
and then it was London and Prague
and the Night Monkey.

1078
00:56:39,814 --> 00:56:42,233
I mean, twice is a coincidence,
but over and over again...

1079
00:56:44,652 --> 00:56:46,362
We knew each other. Tell me I'm wrong.

1080
00:56:48,405 --> 00:56:49,572
SPIDER-MAN: Well, you're wrong.

1081
00:56:49,573 --> 00:56:52,368
What were we? Were we classmates
or friends or something?

1082
00:56:52,952 --> 00:56:55,370
SPIDER-MAN: [STUTTERS] Look, I...
I don't know what you're talking about.

1083
00:56:55,371 --> 00:56:56,539
MJ: Were we something more?

1084
00:56:58,707 --> 00:57:01,043
I just, I can't... I can't remember.

1085
00:57:01,168 --> 00:57:03,253
And I feel like
someone scrambled my brain.

1086
00:57:03,254 --> 00:57:05,131
And you're the only one
who would know why.

1087
00:57:05,756 --> 00:57:07,590
SPIDER-MAN: [EXHALES]
This is crazy. I can't...

1088
00:57:07,591 --> 00:57:09,510
MJ: I know that you can't
tell me the truth.

1089
00:57:12,471 --> 00:57:13,722
But I need to know.

1090
00:57:14,640 --> 00:57:16,725
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

1091
00:57:18,894 --> 00:57:20,896
Maybe there's a part of me
that still remembers.

1092
00:58:01,520 --> 00:58:02,521
Peter.

1093
00:58:04,565 --> 00:58:05,732
MJ.

1094
00:58:05,733 --> 00:58:06,817
MJ: Hey, Peter.

1095
00:58:09,570 --> 00:58:10,738
[PETER CRYING]

1096
00:58:13,073 --> 00:58:14,783
PETER: I've missed you so much.

1097
00:58:19,747 --> 00:58:21,457
I can't believe you figured it out.

1098
00:58:21,874 --> 00:58:22,917
MJ: I did.

1099
00:58:28,672 --> 00:58:31,133
Go ahead, Peter. Touch her.

1100
00:58:32,551 --> 00:58:33,844
Hold her.

1101
00:58:35,221 --> 00:58:36,763
You've been wanting to for so long.

1102
00:58:36,764 --> 00:58:38,766
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

1103
00:58:45,564 --> 00:58:47,233
True love's kiss breaks the spell

1104
00:58:48,108 --> 00:58:49,944
and reunites the star-crossed lovers.

1105
00:58:52,196 --> 00:58:53,364
MJ would vomit.

1106
00:58:56,116 --> 00:58:57,743
You really are a simple spider,
aren't you?

1107
00:59:01,288 --> 00:59:02,289
I see why you like her.

1108
00:59:02,957 --> 00:59:03,999
She's, uh...

1109
00:59:05,167 --> 00:59:06,585
she's smart...

1110
00:59:07,127 --> 00:59:08,170
funny...

1111
00:59:09,046 --> 00:59:10,339
and a little dark and twisted.

1112
00:59:12,091 --> 00:59:13,092
[CHUCKLES]

1113
00:59:14,385 --> 00:59:15,469
I mean, it is sad.

1114
00:59:16,595 --> 00:59:19,723
There is, like,
no thoughts of you in here...

1115
00:59:21,100 --> 00:59:22,309
whatsoever.

1116
00:59:23,852 --> 00:59:25,187
But you knew that, didn't you?

1117
00:59:26,563 --> 00:59:27,856
You're a monster.

1118
00:59:28,816 --> 00:59:30,692
If you loved someone
the way that I love her,

1119
00:59:30,693 --> 00:59:33,569
then you'd know that what you're doing
right now is unforgivable.

1120
00:59:33,570 --> 00:59:34,655
Oh, is that so?

1121
00:59:41,662 --> 00:59:44,707
You know, some people would kill to hold
the person they love one last time.

1122
00:59:46,625 --> 00:59:48,002
Stop it now.

1123
00:59:50,671 --> 00:59:51,672
[GROANING]

1124
00:59:52,965 --> 00:59:54,383
[DISTORTED WARBLE]

1125
00:59:55,384 --> 00:59:56,385
Oof.

1126
00:59:57,803 --> 00:59:59,179
You're running out of time, Peter.

1127
01:00:00,347 --> 01:00:03,851
Soon enough, it won't just be your friends
who don't remember Peter Parker.

1128
01:00:05,352 --> 01:00:07,062
Maybe you should write a letter
to yourself.

1129
01:00:07,604 --> 01:00:09,023
[GRUNTING]

1130
01:00:11,692 --> 01:00:12,735
Get out of her.

1131
01:00:14,278 --> 01:00:15,654
Who's the monster now, Peter?

1132
01:00:17,656 --> 01:00:20,492
- [PETER GRUNTS]
- [GRIPPING MUSIC PLAYING]

1133
01:00:22,911 --> 01:00:24,662
[WHOOSHES]

1134
01:00:24,663 --> 01:00:26,623
[GASPS, WHIMPERS]

1135
01:00:33,255 --> 01:00:34,798
[MJ SCREAMS]

1136
01:00:37,009 --> 01:00:39,010
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS, PANTS]

1137
01:00:39,011 --> 01:00:40,012
MJ.

1138
01:00:40,637 --> 01:00:43,056
MJ. No, no, no. Oh, God.

1139
01:00:43,057 --> 01:00:44,766
Oh, God, please, no, come on.

1140
01:00:44,767 --> 01:00:46,517
Come on, come on, come on.

1141
01:00:46,518 --> 01:00:49,145
Oh, thank God. Oh, thank God.

1142
01:00:49,146 --> 01:00:52,148
Oh, you're okay. Oh, you're okay.

1143
01:00:52,149 --> 01:00:53,984
- Oh, I'm so sorry.
- [CAR DOOR CLOSES]

1144
01:00:55,861 --> 01:00:58,196
Stop. Wait, wait, stop, stop,
please, I'll quit.

1145
01:00:58,197 --> 01:01:00,324
You... You win, you win, you win.
Just don't hurt her.

1146
01:01:03,369 --> 01:01:04,828
You're a mess, Spider-Man.

1147
01:01:07,539 --> 01:01:09,165
Anytime I want...

1148
01:01:09,166 --> 01:01:10,501
I can be anyone I want.

1149
01:01:11,752 --> 01:01:13,504
So you can't protect MJ,

1150
01:01:14,880 --> 01:01:16,547
even from herself.

1151
01:01:16,548 --> 01:01:18,425
[SPIDER-MAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

1152
01:01:23,680 --> 01:01:25,349
It really is a nice letter.

1153
01:01:26,308 --> 01:01:27,433
Little heavy-handed.

1154
01:01:27,434 --> 01:01:28,602
But not bad.

1155
01:01:33,399 --> 01:01:36,359
[CAR DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

1156
01:01:36,360 --> 01:01:38,529
[SCANNER BEEPING]

1157
01:01:42,366 --> 01:01:43,951
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

1158
01:01:47,579 --> 01:01:50,206
You're okay.
I'm gonna take you someplace safe.

1159
01:01:50,207 --> 01:01:51,208
MJ: [WEAKLY] What?

1160
01:01:52,626 --> 01:01:53,918
Take me to 3165...

1161
01:01:53,919 --> 01:01:55,253
Lafayette Street.

1162
01:01:55,254 --> 01:01:57,589
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Navigating
to Empire State University.</i>

1163
01:02:02,636 --> 01:02:03,929
MJ: Wait, wait, wait! Okay.

1164
01:02:05,973 --> 01:02:07,306
SPIDER-MAN: I got you. I got you.
MJ: Are you sure?

1165
01:02:07,307 --> 01:02:08,391
- SPIDER-MAN: Yep.
- Okay.

1166
01:02:08,392 --> 01:02:09,642
'Cause I feel like
I'm slipping a little bit.

1167
01:02:09,643 --> 01:02:10,644
- You're not slipping.
- MJ: Okay.

1168
01:02:11,603 --> 01:02:12,520
[MJ EXCLAIMS]

1169
01:02:12,521 --> 01:02:13,855
SPIDER-MAN: You're okay,
you're okay, you're okay.

1170
01:02:13,856 --> 01:02:15,524
MJ: Yeah, yeah, yeah. I'm fine. I'm fine.

1171
01:02:18,360 --> 01:02:19,902
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
- MJ: Okay.

1172
01:02:19,903 --> 01:02:21,279
Can we just slow down

1173
01:02:21,280 --> 01:02:22,655
- for like two seconds, please?
- Well, we're almost there.

1174
01:02:22,656 --> 01:02:25,074
Yeah, yeah, but you just told me
I was mind controlled.

1175
01:02:25,075 --> 01:02:26,159
SPIDER-MAN: Well, not technically.

1176
01:02:26,160 --> 01:02:27,410
I mean, you're lucky
I believe in that stuff, okay?

1177
01:02:27,411 --> 01:02:28,661
Because governments
have been doing it for years,

1178
01:02:28,662 --> 01:02:30,246
- especially the French.
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1179
01:02:30,247 --> 01:02:31,539
- Are you okay?
- SPIDER-MAN: Yeah...

1180
01:02:31,540 --> 01:02:34,000
Look. Sorry. I'm just trying
to take you someplace safe, okay?

1181
01:02:34,001 --> 01:02:35,961
- [WEB CREAKS]
- [METAL GROANS]

1182
01:02:37,379 --> 01:02:38,546
[CLANKING]

1183
01:02:38,547 --> 01:02:39,881
I don't feel safe.

1184
01:02:39,882 --> 01:02:41,883
- [BOTH PANTING]
- [CREAKING]

1185
01:02:41,884 --> 01:02:42,885
MJ: Oh, shit.

1186
01:02:43,886 --> 01:02:45,094
[METAL GROANS]

1187
01:02:45,095 --> 01:02:46,637
[MJ SCREAMING]

1188
01:02:46,638 --> 01:02:47,889
[BOTH GRUNTING]

1189
01:02:47,890 --> 01:02:49,683
SPIDER-MAN: Sorry.
MJ: Oh, watch out! [YELPS]

1190
01:02:50,976 --> 01:02:52,895
[SPIDER-MAN STRAINING]

1191
01:02:58,692 --> 01:02:59,943
FRANK: You're losing it, kid.

1192
01:03:00,319 --> 01:03:02,945
Thought you'd be able to see that coming
a mile away.

1193
01:03:02,946 --> 01:03:04,113
SPIDER-MAN: What is wrong with you?

1194
01:03:04,114 --> 01:03:05,324
- You could've killed us.
- FRANK: Excuse me.

1195
01:03:05,741 --> 01:03:08,367
You show up to my house unannounced,
what do you think's gonna happen?

1196
01:03:08,368 --> 01:03:09,494
MJ: Wait, this is your house?

1197
01:03:09,495 --> 01:03:10,537
- SPIDER-MAN: No, no. Don't, don't, don't.
- Who the hell is that?

1198
01:03:10,996 --> 01:03:12,079
Who the hell are you?

1199
01:03:12,080 --> 01:03:13,748
SPIDER-MAN: [STUTTERS] She's, um...

1200
01:03:13,749 --> 01:03:15,708
Uh, you know.

1201
01:03:15,709 --> 01:03:17,877
No, I don't know.
That's why I just asked you.

1202
01:03:17,878 --> 01:03:20,796
SPIDER-MAN: She's in danger, Frank.
Look, I need your help, okay?

1203
01:03:20,797 --> 01:03:22,924
FRANK: Yeah, looks like it.
SPIDER-MAN: Well, come on. You owe me.

1204
01:03:22,925 --> 01:03:24,800
Ah, for... Aren't you sick of this story?

1205
01:03:24,801 --> 01:03:25,885
SPIDER-MAN: Staten Island!

1206
01:03:25,886 --> 01:03:27,428
Nah, Staten Island.

1207
01:03:27,429 --> 01:03:29,972
SPIDER-MAN: What more do you want
me to do? I literally saved your life.

1208
01:03:29,973 --> 01:03:31,057
You're out of your mind, kid!

1209
01:03:31,058 --> 01:03:32,225
SPIDER-MAN: What, I gotta save it twice

1210
01:03:32,226 --> 01:03:33,518
- to get a favor out of you?
- That guy couldn't hit me

1211
01:03:33,519 --> 01:03:35,686
- with a handful of rice.
- I mean, what does that sound like to you?

1212
01:03:35,687 --> 01:03:36,938
- I had him exactly where I want him.
- A drug dealer was gonna shoot a guy...

1213
01:03:36,939 --> 01:03:38,397
- I'm seein' him right there.
- ...then I webbed the gun

1214
01:03:38,398 --> 01:03:39,524
- out of the drug dealer's hand...
- I know exactly what

1215
01:03:39,525 --> 01:03:40,900
- I'm completely up for.
- ...and then kicked that drug dealer...

1216
01:03:40,901 --> 01:03:42,109
- Okay, fine, go ahead.
- ...back into a storage container.

1217
01:03:42,110 --> 01:03:43,445
- What would you call that?
- What does that sound like to you?

1218
01:03:44,780 --> 01:03:45,864
I don't care. I just wanna go home.

1219
01:03:46,865 --> 01:03:49,158
That's an excellent idea. Kick rocks.

1220
01:03:49,159 --> 01:03:50,326
- Go home.
- SPIDER-MAN: No, no, wait, wait.

1221
01:03:50,327 --> 01:03:51,828
Frank, Frank, Frank, wait. Please.

1222
01:03:52,996 --> 01:03:56,625
I have got to keep her safe, okay?
And I don't have anywhere else to go.

1223
01:04:00,587 --> 01:04:01,588
You like chili?

1224
01:04:02,839 --> 01:04:03,840
I made chili.

1225
01:04:05,634 --> 01:04:06,635
All right. Just...

1226
01:04:07,469 --> 01:04:08,678
watch out for the claymores.

1227
01:04:08,679 --> 01:04:11,306
Don't wanna pick up pieces of you
for the next two weeks.

1228
01:04:12,724 --> 01:04:14,810
SPIDER-MAN: Hey, I definitely
would not eat that chili.

1229
01:04:16,687 --> 01:04:18,563
FRANK: So, you telling me that maniac

1230
01:04:18,564 --> 01:04:21,983
behind all that tank nonsense
is nothing but a goddamn teenager?

1231
01:04:21,984 --> 01:04:23,150
SPIDER-MAN: And it's not just the tank,

1232
01:04:23,151 --> 01:04:25,820
it's every attack on Damage Control
this past month.

1233
01:04:25,821 --> 01:04:27,822
And how does a kid learn
how to drive a tank?

1234
01:04:27,823 --> 01:04:29,073
SPIDER-MAN: I don't know, Frank.

1235
01:04:29,074 --> 01:04:30,700
FRANK: Beat your ass
all over the street like that.

1236
01:04:30,701 --> 01:04:31,784
SPIDER-MAN: She did not beat my ass.

1237
01:04:31,785 --> 01:04:33,035
- FRANK: Eh.
- [SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

1238
01:04:33,036 --> 01:04:34,121
This your family?

1239
01:04:37,124 --> 01:04:38,834
Would you get the hell away from that?

1240
01:04:39,585 --> 01:04:41,877
Look, I got one rule in this house.

1241
01:04:41,878 --> 01:04:44,714
You don't touch anything.
You don't move anything.

1242
01:04:44,715 --> 01:04:47,676
You sure as shit don't ask me
any goddamn questions about anything.

1243
01:04:49,303 --> 01:04:51,221
- So, three rules?
- [FRANK GRUNTS]

1244
01:04:53,599 --> 01:04:54,975
I see why you like her.

1245
01:04:56,018 --> 01:04:57,352
I'll go put some pants on.

1246
01:04:58,895 --> 01:05:01,064
- Don't touch the chili.
- [SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

1247
01:05:02,149 --> 01:05:03,150
MJ: I like him.

1248
01:05:03,984 --> 01:05:05,027
SPIDER-MAN: Of course you do.

1249
01:05:06,612 --> 01:05:10,239
So I managed to pull this image from
my HUD and run it through the system.

1250
01:05:10,240 --> 01:05:12,284
[COMPUTER BEEPING]

1251
01:05:13,327 --> 01:05:14,493
MJ: Who is she?

1252
01:05:14,494 --> 01:05:16,997
SPIDER-MAN: Until a couple months ago, nobody.

1253
01:05:17,873 --> 01:05:20,499
She was in and out of foster care,
psych hospitals,

1254
01:05:20,500 --> 01:05:22,544
{\an8}and then eventually she ran away
and dropped off the grid.

1255
01:05:22,878 --> 01:05:25,004
{\an8}There's hardly any information about her
that hasn't been scrubbed.

1256
01:05:25,005 --> 01:05:29,009
But she's classified as a telepath.
And now we have a name.

1257
01:05:32,804 --> 01:05:33,805
"Jean Grey."

1258
01:05:35,766 --> 01:05:36,724
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.

1259
01:05:36,725 --> 01:05:39,560
These are the Damage Control sites
that she hasn't hit yet,

1260
01:05:39,561 --> 01:05:41,062
so if she surfaces,

1261
01:05:41,063 --> 01:05:42,939
then my facial tracking program
will pick her up.

1262
01:05:44,066 --> 01:05:45,232
Right.

1263
01:05:45,233 --> 01:05:46,610
FRANK: Oh, yeah? What then?

1264
01:05:49,029 --> 01:05:50,863
SPIDER-MAN: Well, don't worry
about "what then."

1265
01:05:50,864 --> 01:05:51,822
- Just look after her.
- [CHUCKLES]

1266
01:05:51,823 --> 01:05:53,449
Don't worry about it, huh?

1267
01:05:53,450 --> 01:05:55,451
I'm just supposed to sit here
and babysit your girlfriend?

1268
01:05:55,452 --> 01:05:57,286
- I don't need to be babysat, so yeah.
- She's not my girlfriend.

1269
01:05:57,287 --> 01:05:59,580
All right, all right.
Look, what's the plan, huh?

1270
01:05:59,581 --> 01:06:03,209
Just gonna hope that
your facial tracking program works?

1271
01:06:03,210 --> 01:06:05,503
And you get yourself killed,
I gotta watch her the rest of my life?

1272
01:06:05,504 --> 01:06:07,838
SPIDER-MAN: I'm not gonna get killed,
Frank. I can catch her, okay?

1273
01:06:07,839 --> 01:06:08,923
I just...

1274
01:06:08,924 --> 01:06:11,426
I just have to fix my inhibitor
and then I'll be good to go.

1275
01:06:12,010 --> 01:06:13,469
Well, what do you need to do that?

1276
01:06:13,470 --> 01:06:14,804
[SPIDER-MAN CHUCKLES]

1277
01:06:14,805 --> 01:06:18,350
Frank. You do not have
what I need to do that, okay?

1278
01:06:19,893 --> 01:06:21,394
You know you've got some mouth on you.

1279
01:06:21,395 --> 01:06:23,396
What do you think,
you have an anti-static mat,

1280
01:06:23,397 --> 01:06:24,981
a tonal probe, and micro tools?

1281
01:06:25,691 --> 01:06:27,067
I got all that shit.

1282
01:06:27,651 --> 01:06:28,734
What for?

1283
01:06:28,735 --> 01:06:30,278
- Bombs.
- Bingo.

1284
01:06:31,655 --> 01:06:33,824
SPIDER-MAN: [SIGHS] Unbelievable.

1285
01:06:34,449 --> 01:06:36,451
[SIZZLING]

1286
01:06:41,957 --> 01:06:43,792
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

1287
01:06:45,669 --> 01:06:47,962
Hey, do you think it's safe
to maybe call someone

1288
01:06:47,963 --> 01:06:49,589
and let them know I'm okay?

1289
01:06:52,092 --> 01:06:53,093
Uh...

1290
01:06:54,094 --> 01:06:55,095
Like your boyfriend?

1291
01:06:56,012 --> 01:06:58,598
Mmm, no. Like my roommate.

1292
01:06:59,182 --> 01:07:00,517
Oh, um...

1293
01:07:02,644 --> 01:07:05,063
I don't think that's such a good idea,
you know, because...

1294
01:07:06,189 --> 01:07:07,773
she already knows who he is,

1295
01:07:07,774 --> 01:07:09,650
and she can inhabit anyone
she wants, so...

1296
01:07:09,651 --> 01:07:10,818
Right. Yeah.

1297
01:07:10,819 --> 01:07:12,194
Yeah, yeah, yeah. You're right.

1298
01:07:12,195 --> 01:07:14,865
- Sorry.
- MJ: No, it's fine. I totally get it.

1299
01:07:17,033 --> 01:07:18,285
If I called my boyfriend,

1300
01:07:19,244 --> 01:07:21,495
he'd just ask me a bunch of questions
that I couldn't answer,

1301
01:07:21,496 --> 01:07:24,999
and then he'd tell me
I was being withholding again.

1302
01:07:25,000 --> 01:07:27,001
PETER: Withholding?
MJ: Yep.

1303
01:07:27,002 --> 01:07:28,919
Sounds like your boyfriend's
kind of a jerk.

1304
01:07:28,920 --> 01:07:30,338
[CHUCKLING]

1305
01:07:31,673 --> 01:07:32,841
But why'd he think you're withholding?

1306
01:07:33,800 --> 01:07:37,679
I don't know. You tell me,
masked vigilante behind the curtain.

1307
01:07:38,513 --> 01:07:39,930
- Um... [CHUCKLES]
- [MJ CHUCKLES]

1308
01:07:39,931 --> 01:07:41,600
Okay, I see your point.

1309
01:07:43,602 --> 01:07:44,686
So what about you?

1310
01:07:45,312 --> 01:07:46,313
PETER: What about me?

1311
01:07:47,272 --> 01:07:50,484
Well, do you have a Mrs. Spider-Man?

1312
01:07:52,652 --> 01:07:55,071
Do I have a Mrs. Spider-Man? Um...

1313
01:07:58,450 --> 01:08:00,035
No. No.

1314
01:08:01,161 --> 01:08:02,328
MJ: Why not?

1315
01:08:02,329 --> 01:08:03,997
Why not? Because I'm...

1316
01:08:05,749 --> 01:08:07,709
I'm too withholding, obviously.

1317
01:08:08,668 --> 01:08:11,046
- Welcome to the club.
- [PETER LAUGHS]

1318
01:08:16,760 --> 01:08:17,844
There was someone.

1319
01:08:19,179 --> 01:08:20,472
- MJ: Really?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1320
01:08:23,558 --> 01:08:24,643
What happened?

1321
01:08:25,393 --> 01:08:26,394
I, uh...

1322
01:08:28,063 --> 01:08:29,481
I had to let her go.

1323
01:08:30,816 --> 01:08:31,982
To keep her safe.

1324
01:08:31,983 --> 01:08:33,985
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

1325
01:08:36,238 --> 01:08:38,240
I'm sorry.
That must have been really hard for you.

1326
01:08:39,658 --> 01:08:41,576
Yeah, it was. Yeah. It is.

1327
01:08:42,744 --> 01:08:43,787
It is really hard.

1328
01:08:46,122 --> 01:08:48,165
- [CRACKLES]
- Oh. [BLOWS AIR]

1329
01:08:48,166 --> 01:08:49,375
Are you okay?

1330
01:08:49,376 --> 01:08:50,543
PETER: Yeah. Yeah, yeah, I'm okay.
I, uh...

1331
01:08:50,544 --> 01:08:52,002
MJ: You know what,
I'm just gonna come over.

1332
01:08:52,003 --> 01:08:53,922
PETER: Uh, hold on, hold on, hold on,
hold on, hold on.

1333
01:08:55,799 --> 01:08:56,882
- What's going on?
- SPIDER-MAN: Um...

1334
01:08:56,883 --> 01:08:58,718
It just keeps overheating on me.

1335
01:08:59,553 --> 01:09:01,263
It's been stumping me for days.

1336
01:09:02,013 --> 01:09:03,180
Before I switched to aerospace,

1337
01:09:03,181 --> 01:09:07,226
I was gonna major in biochemical
engineering, so, do you mind if I...

1338
01:09:07,227 --> 01:09:08,561
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, yeah, for sure.

1339
01:09:08,562 --> 01:09:10,105
Here. There you go.

1340
01:09:12,065 --> 01:09:13,858
[SPIDER-MAN EXHALES]

1341
01:09:13,859 --> 01:09:14,860
Wow.

1342
01:09:17,904 --> 01:09:20,030
So, does the device itself...

1343
01:09:20,031 --> 01:09:23,784
I mean, does it generate
any kind of radiation or a magnetic field?

1344
01:09:23,785 --> 01:09:25,203
'Cause that would definitely interfere.

1345
01:09:25,370 --> 01:09:27,371
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, yeah,
it has a micro magnetic field,

1346
01:09:27,372 --> 01:09:29,415
but I accounted for that in the design.

1347
01:09:29,416 --> 01:09:31,375
Okay, well, what about your suit?

1348
01:09:31,376 --> 01:09:33,294
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, it actually dissipates
into the fabric,

1349
01:09:33,295 --> 01:09:34,713
which is pretty cool.

1350
01:09:35,672 --> 01:09:36,673
Okay.

1351
01:09:39,718 --> 01:09:40,844
What about those?

1352
01:09:41,970 --> 01:09:42,971
SPIDER-MAN: What about what?

1353
01:09:45,557 --> 01:09:48,183
Your goggles, or whatever you call 'em.

1354
01:09:48,184 --> 01:09:51,938
SPIDER-MAN: Uh, they would create a field.
It would be tiny, but...

1355
01:09:53,523 --> 01:09:55,941
But it's on your head,
which is very close to the inhibitor.

1356
01:09:55,942 --> 01:09:58,277
SPIDER-MAN: Which is probably why
it's overheating.

1357
01:09:58,278 --> 01:10:00,195
Oh, MJ, that is genius.

1358
01:10:00,196 --> 01:10:01,906
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

1359
01:10:01,907 --> 01:10:03,240
Okay, this has to work.

1360
01:10:03,241 --> 01:10:05,327
[WISTFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

1361
01:10:06,077 --> 01:10:08,705
- [DEVICE BEEPS]
- E.V.: <i>Inhibitor engaged.</i>

1362
01:10:10,373 --> 01:10:13,126
{\an8}<i>Suppressing selected arachnid hormones.</i>

1363
01:10:14,085 --> 01:10:16,170
SPIDER-MAN: Okay. That feels better.

1364
01:10:16,171 --> 01:10:18,047
That feels totally better.

1365
01:10:18,048 --> 01:10:20,841
Oh, my head feels so clear. [SIGHS]

1366
01:10:20,842 --> 01:10:22,176
[SOFTLY] Web, web.

1367
01:10:22,177 --> 01:10:24,345
[NORMALLY] And I'm not shooting
organic webs.

1368
01:10:24,346 --> 01:10:26,598
Oh, my God, MJ,
that, like, totally worked.

1369
01:10:27,641 --> 01:10:30,225
You know, this is some really
intense stuff you're working on here.

1370
01:10:30,226 --> 01:10:32,228
[MUSIC CONTINUES]

1371
01:10:32,979 --> 01:10:34,648
SPIDER-MAN: Well, yeah,
it's really important.

1372
01:10:37,108 --> 01:10:40,779
Yeah, but this is like, I mean,
this is like altering your DNA.

1373
01:10:42,030 --> 01:10:43,781
I mean, this is the kind of stuff
you put on, like,

1374
01:10:43,782 --> 01:10:45,492
I don't know, like a monster.

1375
01:10:47,744 --> 01:10:49,495
SPIDER-MAN: Well, if you've seen
what's been happening to me

1376
01:10:49,496 --> 01:10:52,207
over the last couple days,
then you might understand.

1377
01:10:52,916 --> 01:10:54,416
Yeah, well, I've been with you
for the last few hours

1378
01:10:54,417 --> 01:10:55,543
and that's not what I've seen.

1379
01:10:56,378 --> 01:10:57,420
SPIDER-MAN: And what have you seen?

1380
01:10:58,713 --> 01:10:59,881
From my side of the curtain?

1381
01:11:01,967 --> 01:11:05,387
A really good guy
who might just be changing.

1382
01:11:10,600 --> 01:11:14,312
Well, I don't mean to overstep.
I'll, uh, let you get back to it.

1383
01:11:18,733 --> 01:11:21,319
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
- [SEAGULL SQUAWKS]

1384
01:11:29,703 --> 01:11:32,080
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

1385
01:11:35,625 --> 01:11:36,918
Can't sleep either, huh?

1386
01:11:37,711 --> 01:11:38,712
You want coffee?

1387
01:11:39,587 --> 01:11:40,630
SPIDER-MAN: Sure.

1388
01:11:41,840 --> 01:11:43,049
You get your shit fixed?

1389
01:11:44,009 --> 01:11:46,802
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.
I've been wearing it all night.

1390
01:11:46,803 --> 01:11:47,887
So far, so good.

1391
01:11:48,805 --> 01:11:50,639
I made this other one universal.

1392
01:11:50,640 --> 01:11:55,185
So if I could get it on Jean,
it should completely shut down her powers.

1393
01:11:55,186 --> 01:11:57,355
FRANK: Hmm. You know what else would work?

1394
01:11:57,731 --> 01:11:59,148
You just shoot her.

1395
01:11:59,149 --> 01:12:00,275
SPIDER-MAN: Nice.

1396
01:12:00,984 --> 01:12:02,569
[CHUCKLES]

1397
01:12:03,028 --> 01:12:04,195
Jesus Christ.

1398
01:12:04,904 --> 01:12:07,990
[LAUGHS] That has gotta be
the goofiest shit I ever seen in my life.

1399
01:12:07,991 --> 01:12:11,118
What, you can't even take the mask off
to drink a cup of coffee?

1400
01:12:11,119 --> 01:12:12,286
[SPIDER-MAN CHUCKLES]

1401
01:12:12,287 --> 01:12:15,290
Don't take it personally, Frank.
It stays on for everybody.

1402
01:12:16,332 --> 01:12:17,375
Even her?

1403
01:12:19,836 --> 01:12:21,045
Who is she, kid?

1404
01:12:21,046 --> 01:12:22,129
SPIDER-MAN: I don't know.

1405
01:12:22,130 --> 01:12:24,256
Eh! That's horseshit. Who is she?

1406
01:12:24,257 --> 01:12:26,717
- I'm telling you, I don't know who she is.
- What are you doin'? You care about her.

1407
01:12:26,718 --> 01:12:28,010
- You're pretending not to. Why?
- I don't care about her.

1408
01:12:28,011 --> 01:12:29,928
Look, I don't know
who she is, Frank. Okay?

1409
01:12:29,929 --> 01:12:32,765
I don't have anybody. I'm like you.
I just keep to myself.

1410
01:12:32,766 --> 01:12:33,808
You're like me?

1411
01:12:35,143 --> 01:12:36,478
What do you know about me, kid?

1412
01:12:37,479 --> 01:12:38,812
You think this is a choice?

1413
01:12:38,813 --> 01:12:41,441
Living like this, it's a lifestyle?
Is that what you think?

1414
01:12:42,108 --> 01:12:43,610
Kid, this is a sentence.

1415
01:12:44,778 --> 01:12:45,779
You know somethin'...

1416
01:12:46,571 --> 01:12:47,989
If I had one second,

1417
01:12:48,948 --> 01:12:52,118
people I love were still breathing,
you think I'd be hiding behind a mask?

1418
01:12:52,744 --> 01:12:54,995
You think I'd pretend
to be something that I'm not,

1419
01:12:54,996 --> 01:12:56,748
acting like a goddamn coward?

1420
01:12:57,916 --> 01:12:59,584
[ALERT CHIRPING ON COMPUTER]

1421
01:13:02,378 --> 01:13:04,214
- SPIDER-MAN: I got a facial match.
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]

1422
01:13:07,884 --> 01:13:10,177
She's at the Damage Control HQ
in Manhattan.

1423
01:13:10,178 --> 01:13:11,387
I gotta go. Okay.

1424
01:13:15,892 --> 01:13:17,976
She's gonna be okay.

1425
01:13:17,977 --> 01:13:19,104
I'll see to it.

1426
01:13:22,148 --> 01:13:23,274
SPIDER-MAN: Thanks, Frank.

1427
01:13:25,693 --> 01:13:26,986
[FRANK SIGHS]

1428
01:13:27,862 --> 01:13:28,905
[DOOR CREAKS]

1429
01:13:30,031 --> 01:13:31,032
Hey.

1430
01:13:31,616 --> 01:13:32,617
FRANK: Hey.

1431
01:13:34,285 --> 01:13:35,870
You just gonna let him go by himself?

1432
01:13:37,372 --> 01:13:38,748
You know, I think he might need you.

1433
01:13:39,249 --> 01:13:40,542
Eh.

1434
01:13:41,668 --> 01:13:43,336
Kinda like you needed him
on Staten Island.

1435
01:13:47,298 --> 01:13:48,424
[SOFTLY] Yeah.

1436
01:13:49,717 --> 01:13:51,719
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1437
01:13:56,766 --> 01:13:58,434
[THUDDING]

1438
01:14:06,151 --> 01:14:08,069
- [SYSTEM TRILLING]
- [THUDDING CONTINUES]

1439
01:14:14,617 --> 01:14:16,786
- [THUDDING]
- [ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

1440
01:14:18,371 --> 01:14:20,206
[THUDDING]

1441
01:14:21,875 --> 01:14:23,167
[ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]

1442
01:14:23,168 --> 01:14:24,459
[RADIO CHIRPS]

1443
01:14:24,460 --> 01:14:25,752
[THUDDING]

1444
01:14:25,753 --> 01:14:27,714
You can't hide from me forever, Bill.

1445
01:14:28,423 --> 01:14:31,676
[OVER RADIO] <i>You've got a strong door,
but it's the wall you have to worry about.</i>

1446
01:14:32,677 --> 01:14:34,220
Who are you and what do you want?

1447
01:14:34,554 --> 01:14:36,347
[THUDDING CONTINUES]

1448
01:14:39,434 --> 01:14:40,685
I'm Jean Grey...

1449
01:14:41,769 --> 01:14:43,354
and you know what I want.

1450
01:14:49,485 --> 01:14:50,653
[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

1451
01:14:51,154 --> 01:14:52,697
[DISTANT THUDDING]

1452
01:14:58,119 --> 01:15:00,204
[MYSTERIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

1453
01:15:00,205 --> 01:15:02,707
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

1454
01:15:04,584 --> 01:15:06,294
[DISTANT THUDDING CONTINUES]

1455
01:15:18,473 --> 01:15:20,391
[THUDDING INTENSIFIES]

1456
01:15:23,269 --> 01:15:24,562
[THUDDING STOPS]

1457
01:15:29,692 --> 01:15:32,111
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

1458
01:15:44,040 --> 01:15:45,250
SPIDER-MAN: Jean?

1459
01:15:45,833 --> 01:15:48,503
You looked me up? I'm blushing.

1460
01:15:49,754 --> 01:15:52,131
I told you what would happen to your girl
if you got in my way.

1461
01:15:53,091 --> 01:15:54,759
SPIDER-MAN: You're not getting
near her again.

1462
01:15:55,301 --> 01:15:57,387
And you're definitely
not getting inside that vault.

1463
01:15:57,929 --> 01:15:59,179
Hmm, maybe not.

1464
01:15:59,180 --> 01:16:00,640
[DEVICE CRACKLING]

1465
01:16:03,851 --> 01:16:05,144
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1466
01:16:06,396 --> 01:16:07,647
But this guy might.

1467
01:16:10,525 --> 01:16:13,277
SPIDER-MAN: Jean, you don't know
what you're dealing with.

1468
01:16:13,278 --> 01:16:16,113
You know, you and Banner
have a lot in common.

1469
01:16:16,114 --> 01:16:20,701
Both fighting a losing battle
against the monster that lives inside you.

1470
01:16:20,702 --> 01:16:22,661
SPIDER-MAN: Jean, this is the Hulk,
you can't just...

1471
01:16:22,662 --> 01:16:24,789
- [HULK GRUNTING]
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1472
01:16:27,375 --> 01:16:29,544
- [HULK GRUNTS]
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1473
01:16:31,170 --> 01:16:33,588
- HULK: What the hell?
- [GRUNTS]

1474
01:16:33,589 --> 01:16:35,632
Oh, I see.

1475
01:16:35,633 --> 01:16:37,467
- [GRUNTS]
- [SPIDER-MAN GASPS]

1476
01:16:37,468 --> 01:16:40,929
Trying to muzzle me
like you muzzle yourself?

1477
01:16:40,930 --> 01:16:42,514
SPIDER-MAN: I can't let you in there.

1478
01:16:42,515 --> 01:16:44,642
Whatever V-Max is, you're not getting it.

1479
01:16:45,101 --> 01:16:46,643
Like hell I'm not.

1480
01:16:46,644 --> 01:16:48,061
- [ROARS]
- SPIDER-MAN: Oh, crap.

1481
01:16:48,062 --> 01:16:49,647
- [HULK GRUNTS]
- [SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

1482
01:16:52,317 --> 01:16:53,608
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]
- [HULK GROANS]

1483
01:16:53,609 --> 01:16:55,695
- [HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]
- [WINCES]

1484
01:16:56,612 --> 01:16:57,822
[GROANS]

1485
01:16:59,157 --> 01:17:00,324
[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1486
01:17:00,325 --> 01:17:02,243
Jean, don't do this.

1487
01:17:02,827 --> 01:17:04,369
- Save your breath.
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1488
01:17:04,370 --> 01:17:05,620
[SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

1489
01:17:05,621 --> 01:17:07,748
- [HULK GRUNTING]
- [GROANING]

1490
01:17:07,749 --> 01:17:09,624
[CLANGING]

1491
01:17:09,625 --> 01:17:11,251
[SPIDER-MAN GASPS]

1492
01:17:11,252 --> 01:17:13,004
- [GUN FIRING]
- [GROANING]

1493
01:17:14,005 --> 01:17:16,090
[FRANK ROARING]

1494
01:17:24,223 --> 01:17:25,558
[GUN CLICKS]

1495
01:17:29,270 --> 01:17:31,188
SPIDER-MAN: Frank,
what are you doing here?

1496
01:17:31,189 --> 01:17:32,856
What you think I'm doing?
I'm saving your ass.

1497
01:17:32,857 --> 01:17:34,983
SPIDER-MAN: This is way above
your pay grade, dude.

1498
01:17:34,984 --> 01:17:36,401
- We're fighting the Hulk.
- Oh, shit!

1499
01:17:36,402 --> 01:17:37,236
[GRUNTS]

1500
01:17:37,904 --> 01:17:39,654
[FRANK GROANS]

1501
01:17:39,655 --> 01:17:41,115
[GRUNTS]

1502
01:17:41,657 --> 01:17:43,075
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1503
01:17:43,076 --> 01:17:44,118
[FRANK GRUNTS]

1504
01:17:45,328 --> 01:17:47,330
[HULK ROARING]

1505
01:17:55,171 --> 01:17:56,005
[BEEPS]

1506
01:17:57,590 --> 01:17:58,508
[GRUNTS]

1507
01:17:59,050 --> 01:18:00,051
Really?

1508
01:18:01,511 --> 01:18:02,594
[GROANS]

1509
01:18:02,595 --> 01:18:04,555
- [WHOOSHES]
- [GASPS, PANTS]

1510
01:18:05,681 --> 01:18:07,517
[GROANS]

1511
01:18:09,602 --> 01:18:10,894
[WHOOSHING]

1512
01:18:10,895 --> 01:18:13,438
- [HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]
- [GROANING] Get out!

1513
01:18:13,439 --> 01:18:15,942
- [WHOOSHES]
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]

1514
01:18:18,319 --> 01:18:19,694
[GUN FIRING]

1515
01:18:19,695 --> 01:18:22,280
- SPIDER-MAN: Stop shooting him!
- Are you out of your goddamn mind?

1516
01:18:22,281 --> 01:18:24,534
SPIDER-MAN: He's...
Banner's not the problem! She is.

1517
01:18:27,203 --> 01:18:29,122
[INAUDIBLE CONVERSATION]

1518
01:18:34,210 --> 01:18:35,711
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1519
01:18:36,546 --> 01:18:37,547
[BANNER GROANING]

1520
01:18:38,214 --> 01:18:40,006
SPIDER-MAN: I thought I told you
to stay home and watch MJ.

1521
01:18:40,007 --> 01:18:41,174
FRANK: Yeah, you did.

1522
01:18:41,175 --> 01:18:43,176
And then she tells me
I gotta come watch you.

1523
01:18:43,177 --> 01:18:44,386
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

1524
01:18:44,387 --> 01:18:46,012
Wait, did she actually say that to you?

1525
01:18:46,013 --> 01:18:48,182
- [OBJECTS CLATTERING]
- Are you blushing, daffodil?

1526
01:18:49,058 --> 01:18:50,267
SPIDER-MAN: I'm not blushing.

1527
01:18:50,268 --> 01:18:52,144
- [THUDDING]
- [SPIDER-MAN GASPS]

1528
01:18:52,145 --> 01:18:54,938
Goddamn it.
I knew I should have brought a bigger gun.

1529
01:18:54,939 --> 01:18:56,231
SPIDER-MAN: That's a good idea,
"Bring a bigger gun."

1530
01:18:56,232 --> 01:18:57,482
What are you gonna do,
tickle him to death?

1531
01:18:57,483 --> 01:18:58,900
No. Look, change of plan.

1532
01:18:58,901 --> 01:19:01,695
First, we get this on the Hulk,
then we go after Jean.

1533
01:19:01,696 --> 01:19:02,946
FRANK: I got one better.

1534
01:19:02,947 --> 01:19:04,906
That's the highest
casualty-producing threat.

1535
01:19:04,907 --> 01:19:08,161
You contain it. I go find the source.
I take it down. You got it?

1536
01:19:08,744 --> 01:19:10,621
SPIDER-MAN: Are you just trying
to get out of fighting the Hulk?

1537
01:19:12,248 --> 01:19:13,832
- I guess so.
- SPIDER-MAN: Okay, whatever, dude.

1538
01:19:13,833 --> 01:19:14,834
I got this.

1539
01:19:15,418 --> 01:19:16,836
- Wait, no, Frank, Frank, Frank.
- What?

1540
01:19:17,211 --> 01:19:18,545
SPIDER-MAN: Do not kill her!

1541
01:19:18,546 --> 01:19:20,797
Don't start with that soft serve bullshit.

1542
01:19:20,798 --> 01:19:22,716
You know something?
I'm gonna do this, I'm gonna do it my way.

1543
01:19:22,717 --> 01:19:25,177
Just... just go, just go.

1544
01:19:25,178 --> 01:19:27,471
SPIDER-MAN: And don't get within 33 feet!
FRANK: Eh...

1545
01:19:27,472 --> 01:19:28,723
SPIDER-MAN: So frustrating.

1546
01:19:33,186 --> 01:19:35,188
[LIQUID BUBBLING]

1547
01:19:43,696 --> 01:19:44,779
JEAN: Hey.

1548
01:19:44,780 --> 01:19:46,323
- [WHOOSHES]
- [GRUNTS]

1549
01:19:46,324 --> 01:19:48,326
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

1550
01:19:49,202 --> 01:19:50,577
Whoa!

1551
01:19:50,578 --> 01:19:52,747
This guy's got issues.

1552
01:19:54,123 --> 01:19:57,125
BANNER: No. Oh, no.

1553
01:19:57,126 --> 01:19:59,837
No, not again. Oh, no.

1554
01:20:00,630 --> 01:20:03,256
SPIDER-MAN: Dr. Banner? Is that you?

1555
01:20:03,257 --> 01:20:06,426
[BREATHING HEAVILY]
Spider-Man. What happened?

1556
01:20:06,427 --> 01:20:07,552
Where am I?

1557
01:20:07,553 --> 01:20:09,471
- SPIDER-MAN: Hey, hey, hey.
- Did I do all this?

1558
01:20:09,472 --> 01:20:10,972
- SPIDER-MAN: You...
- Did I hurt anyone?

1559
01:20:10,973 --> 01:20:12,641
SPIDER-MAN: It's not your fault.
She was in your mind.

1560
01:20:12,642 --> 01:20:13,558
You weren't in control.

1561
01:20:13,559 --> 01:20:15,602
- I lost my inhibitor.
- SPIDER-MAN: Look here, here.

1562
01:20:15,603 --> 01:20:17,938
BANNER: It's the only thing
keeping the monster inside.

1563
01:20:17,939 --> 01:20:18,939
SPIDER-MAN: It's okay.
I got another one here.

1564
01:20:18,940 --> 01:20:19,856
I just need you to put this on.

1565
01:20:19,857 --> 01:20:21,650
- What is it?
- SPIDER-MAN: It's universal.

1566
01:20:21,651 --> 01:20:22,944
It should work on you.

1567
01:20:28,282 --> 01:20:29,325
FRANK: Hmm.

1568
01:20:32,328 --> 01:20:34,747
SPIDER-MAN: Please, sir, there's people
in the building. Just put it on.

1569
01:20:37,500 --> 01:20:39,668
- [GROANS]
- SPIDER-MAN: You okay?

1570
01:20:39,669 --> 01:20:43,004
My head. I think she broke something!

1571
01:20:43,005 --> 01:20:44,297
SPIDER-MAN: Is she still in there?

1572
01:20:44,298 --> 01:20:45,632
BANNER: No.

1573
01:20:45,633 --> 01:20:46,883
It's the other guy.

1574
01:20:46,884 --> 01:20:50,053
SPIDER-MAN: Bruce? Look,
I can get you out of here, okay?

1575
01:20:50,054 --> 01:20:51,596
I just need you to put that inhibitor on.

1576
01:20:51,597 --> 01:20:52,765
- Get away from me!
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1577
01:20:54,600 --> 01:20:55,935
BANNER: He's coming.

1578
01:20:56,602 --> 01:20:57,937
I can't control.

1579
01:20:58,646 --> 01:21:00,564
SPIDER-MAN: Yes, you can, Bruce!
Yes, you can!

1580
01:21:00,565 --> 01:21:04,067
Get out of the building!

1581
01:21:04,068 --> 01:21:06,820
[VOICE GROWS DEEPER] Get everyone
out of the... [GROANS]

1582
01:21:06,821 --> 01:21:09,406
[ROARING]

1583
01:21:09,407 --> 01:21:11,324
No! No!

1584
01:21:11,325 --> 01:21:13,076
SPIDER-MAN: Banner, please. Look at me.

1585
01:21:13,077 --> 01:21:14,954
[HULK ROARING]

1586
01:21:15,663 --> 01:21:18,499
[HOARSELY] No Banner. No girl.

1587
01:21:19,834 --> 01:21:21,668
Only Hulk.

1588
01:21:21,669 --> 01:21:23,504
[HULK GROWLING]

1589
01:21:25,131 --> 01:21:26,632
[GROWLS]

1590
01:21:27,800 --> 01:21:29,135
[SNARLS]

1591
01:21:31,429 --> 01:21:33,221
SPIDER-MAN: I didn't know
you could get that big.

1592
01:21:33,222 --> 01:21:35,224
[GROWLING]

1593
01:21:37,310 --> 01:21:38,603
FRANK: Whoa!

1594
01:21:39,228 --> 01:21:40,521
Good luck with that, Peter.

1595
01:21:42,523 --> 01:21:44,900
- [HULK GRUNTING]
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1596
01:21:48,863 --> 01:21:50,656
- [HULK SNARLS]
- SPIDER-MAN: There you are.

1597
01:21:52,325 --> 01:21:53,408
Just hold still. Just hold still...

1598
01:21:53,409 --> 01:21:55,453
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]
- [HULK ROARING]

1599
01:21:56,912 --> 01:21:57,913
SPIDER-MAN: Stay!

1600
01:22:03,628 --> 01:22:05,379
[ROARS]

1601
01:22:06,756 --> 01:22:08,174
SPIDER-MAN: [PANTS] Oh, God.

1602
01:22:09,508 --> 01:22:11,761
[SCREAMS, GROANS]

1603
01:22:12,428 --> 01:22:14,137
[GROANS, PANTS]

1604
01:22:14,138 --> 01:22:16,389
[FRANK WHISTLING]

1605
01:22:16,390 --> 01:22:17,725
[BOMB BEEPS, ARMS]

1606
01:22:19,560 --> 01:22:21,186
[BOMB BEEPS, ARMS]

1607
01:22:21,187 --> 01:22:22,438
[GUN COCKING]

1608
01:22:22,938 --> 01:22:24,022
No lethal rounds.

1609
01:22:24,023 --> 01:22:26,025
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1610
01:22:30,863 --> 01:22:32,698
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1611
01:22:36,952 --> 01:22:38,704
E.V.: <i>Tracking time to detonation.</i>

1612
01:22:39,080 --> 01:22:40,330
[HULK ROARING]

1613
01:22:40,331 --> 01:22:41,707
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1614
01:22:42,667 --> 01:22:43,876
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1615
01:22:46,295 --> 01:22:48,964
[SPIDER-MAN SCREAMING]

1616
01:22:49,924 --> 01:22:52,468
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING, GROANING]

1617
01:22:58,766 --> 01:22:59,809
[GRUNTS]

1618
01:23:07,650 --> 01:23:09,567
E.V.: <i>Ninety seconds to detonation.</i>

1619
01:23:09,568 --> 01:23:11,736
SPIDER-MAN: I know! I know! [GRUNTING]

1620
01:23:11,737 --> 01:23:12,822
[SNARLING]

1621
01:23:14,115 --> 01:23:16,199
[BOTH GRUNTING]

1622
01:23:16,200 --> 01:23:17,659
{\an8}SPIDER-MAN: Come on. Come on.

1623
01:23:17,660 --> 01:23:19,285
{\an8}Why is your skin so thick?

1624
01:23:19,286 --> 01:23:20,537
{\an8}E.V.: <i>Inhibitor cannot attach.</i>

1625
01:23:20,538 --> 01:23:22,081
- SPIDER-MAN: Oh, come on!
- [SNARLS]

1626
01:23:27,795 --> 01:23:28,796
[HULK ROARING]

1627
01:23:33,008 --> 01:23:34,093
[GRUNTS]

1628
01:23:37,805 --> 01:23:38,806
[GRUNTING]

1629
01:23:43,018 --> 01:23:44,644
[GAUNTLET POWERING UP]

1630
01:23:44,645 --> 01:23:47,106
- [MUSIC CRESCENDOES]
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

1631
01:23:47,690 --> 01:23:49,191
[GRUNTS]

1632
01:23:54,780 --> 01:23:56,866
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

1633
01:23:59,827 --> 01:24:01,537
SPIDER-MAN: [GROANING] Dr. Banner...

1634
01:24:02,913 --> 01:24:04,122
please.

1635
01:24:04,123 --> 01:24:05,498
[GROANING]

1636
01:24:05,499 --> 01:24:06,583
Bruce.

1637
01:24:06,584 --> 01:24:07,834
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1638
01:24:07,835 --> 01:24:09,795
- SPIDER-MAN: It's Peter.
- [GROWLS]

1639
01:24:10,546 --> 01:24:12,214
I'm your friend.

1640
01:24:14,341 --> 01:24:15,509
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

1641
01:24:23,934 --> 01:24:25,519
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

1642
01:24:29,648 --> 01:24:30,816
[GROANING]

1643
01:24:35,488 --> 01:24:37,531
[SPIDER-MAN COUGHING]

1644
01:24:41,535 --> 01:24:42,536
Bruce.

1645
01:24:45,247 --> 01:24:47,540
- [PANTING]
- [CRASHING]

1646
01:24:47,541 --> 01:24:48,834
[TIMER BEEPING]

1647
01:24:50,252 --> 01:24:51,962
[DISTANT EXPLOSION]

1648
01:24:53,839 --> 01:24:54,923
[GUNSHOTS]

1649
01:24:54,924 --> 01:24:56,550
[GUARDS GROANING]

1650
01:25:01,639 --> 01:25:04,433
Throw down your guns,
or you'll get the next one in the head.

1651
01:25:15,736 --> 01:25:17,196
Where is she?

1652
01:25:22,451 --> 01:25:23,619
[FRANK GRUNTS]

1653
01:25:26,288 --> 01:25:28,122
[INHIBITOR BEEPS, TRILLING]

1654
01:25:28,123 --> 01:25:30,000
- [WHOOSHES]
- [GROANS]

1655
01:25:30,626 --> 01:25:31,709
What did you...

1656
01:25:31,710 --> 01:25:32,920
SPIDER-MAN: It's over, Jean.

1657
01:25:33,671 --> 01:25:35,422
- [GUN FIRES]
- [GRUNTS]

1658
01:25:40,386 --> 01:25:42,429
[JEAN GRUNTING, GASPING]

1659
01:25:48,269 --> 01:25:49,270
Sara.

1660
01:26:00,573 --> 01:26:01,699
Is that my gun?

1661
01:26:02,950 --> 01:26:06,120
- [SIREN WAILING IN DISTANCE]
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

1662
01:26:10,708 --> 01:26:13,419
Is anyone hurt? It's just me?

1663
01:26:14,378 --> 01:26:15,588
Is anyone hurt?

1664
01:26:17,214 --> 01:26:18,215
METZGER: Spider-Man...

1665
01:26:20,968 --> 01:26:22,052
You saved my life.

1666
01:26:22,970 --> 01:26:24,637
And you saved God knows how many lives

1667
01:26:24,638 --> 01:26:27,390
by making sure she didn't find
what she was looking for in there.

1668
01:26:27,391 --> 01:26:28,726
EMT: Still inside.
We got her coming through.

1669
01:26:29,852 --> 01:26:31,729
SPIDER-MAN: Before she passed out,
she tried to say something.

1670
01:26:32,855 --> 01:26:35,524
A name, Sara.
Does that mean something to you?

1671
01:26:36,859 --> 01:26:38,611
Before you got the inhibitor on her,

1672
01:26:39,695 --> 01:26:41,697
she managed to get in my mind
for a moment.

1673
01:26:43,240 --> 01:26:46,702
Sara was the name of someone I worked
closely with that recently passed.

1674
01:26:47,328 --> 01:26:48,412
SPIDER-MAN: I'm sorry to hear that.

1675
01:26:49,914 --> 01:26:53,709
Somehow the memory of Sara
must have affected her.

1676
01:26:56,712 --> 01:26:59,631
SPIDER-MAN: Well, I'd love to talk to her
when she wakes up, if that's all right.

1677
01:26:59,632 --> 01:27:03,676
Of course. She'll be transferred
to our facility on Roosevelt Island.

1678
01:27:03,677 --> 01:27:06,095
Now, I'm just as eager
to get her talking as you are,

1679
01:27:06,096 --> 01:27:08,015
but let's not strain her
too much in one day.

1680
01:27:08,641 --> 01:27:09,725
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, of course.

1681
01:27:10,476 --> 01:27:11,893
METZGER: Thank you, Spider-Man.

1682
01:27:11,894 --> 01:27:12,895
SPIDER-MAN: My pleasure.

1683
01:27:14,021 --> 01:27:16,023
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

1684
01:27:24,823 --> 01:27:25,907
SPIDER-MAN: MJ!

1685
01:27:25,908 --> 01:27:28,284
It worked. She's in custody.

1686
01:27:28,285 --> 01:27:29,453
You're safe now.

1687
01:27:32,581 --> 01:27:33,582
You left this.

1688
01:27:41,882 --> 01:27:43,133
Did you want me to find it?

1689
01:27:45,260 --> 01:27:47,596
SPIDER-MAN: No. No. Um...

1690
01:27:48,347 --> 01:27:49,430
Look, I can explain, I...

1691
01:27:49,431 --> 01:27:50,849
Can you take that off, please?

1692
01:27:52,726 --> 01:27:53,727
SPIDER-MAN: What?

1693
01:27:54,770 --> 01:27:55,771
The mask.

1694
01:27:57,856 --> 01:28:02,444
I think I deserve to have
this conversation with "Peter Parker."

1695
01:28:10,786 --> 01:28:11,787
[SIGHS]

1696
01:28:28,429 --> 01:28:30,305
You came to the party
at our apartment the other night.

1697
01:28:36,854 --> 01:28:38,897
And the donut shop. [SCOFFS]

1698
01:28:40,274 --> 01:28:41,608
The year I went off to school.

1699
01:28:44,486 --> 01:28:45,612
Why didn't you tell me then?

1700
01:28:46,363 --> 01:28:47,948
I was trying to protect you.

1701
01:28:48,490 --> 01:28:51,409
Yeah, well, I've almost been killed, like,
five times in the past 24 hours,

1702
01:28:51,410 --> 01:28:52,953
so it's not really working that well.

1703
01:28:53,829 --> 01:28:55,164
PETER: I know. I'm sorry. I...

1704
01:28:56,582 --> 01:28:57,875
Were you ever gonna tell me?

1705
01:29:04,798 --> 01:29:05,799
Right.

1706
01:29:07,301 --> 01:29:09,720
So you just were gonna
make that decision for me.

1707
01:29:10,471 --> 01:29:11,679
I know. I'm sorry.

1708
01:29:11,680 --> 01:29:13,639
I don't really need you to keep saying
that you're sorry.

1709
01:29:13,640 --> 01:29:14,932
I don't know what you want me to tell you.

1710
01:29:14,933 --> 01:29:16,810
I want you to tell me
why you would do this to me.

1711
01:29:22,941 --> 01:29:24,193
I lost someone.

1712
01:29:28,155 --> 01:29:30,282
And they'd still be here
if it wasn't for me.

1713
01:29:35,079 --> 01:29:36,705
I didn't read you that letter because...

1714
01:29:37,998 --> 01:29:40,416
I didn't want anything like that
to happen to you.

1715
01:29:40,417 --> 01:29:41,709
But that's not really
your decision to make.

1716
01:29:41,710 --> 01:29:43,003
PETER: I know it's not, but...

1717
01:29:45,380 --> 01:29:46,715
You mean everything to me.

1718
01:29:49,968 --> 01:29:52,387
And I've been trying to live my life
without you, but I...

1719
01:29:54,264 --> 01:29:55,265
I can't.

1720
01:30:01,480 --> 01:30:02,481
I love you.

1721
01:30:09,655 --> 01:30:10,948
[MJ SIGHS]

1722
01:30:14,576 --> 01:30:17,663
This spell or whatever it is
that you did...

1723
01:30:21,333 --> 01:30:22,334
It worked.

1724
01:30:25,295 --> 01:30:28,549
All these memories that you're saying
that we have together, I don't...

1725
01:30:30,801 --> 01:30:31,927
I don't have them.

1726
01:30:35,722 --> 01:30:37,974
And I do see why, you know,
she would love you,

1727
01:30:37,975 --> 01:30:40,686
the girl you wrote that letter to, but...

1728
01:30:45,440 --> 01:30:46,525
I understand...

1729
01:30:47,568 --> 01:30:50,487
that you did what you had to do
to protect her.

1730
01:30:52,781 --> 01:30:55,492
And for that I'm so grateful.

1731
01:30:58,996 --> 01:30:59,997
But I...

1732
01:31:04,042 --> 01:31:05,335
I don't love you.

1733
01:31:09,715 --> 01:31:10,716
Because I don't...

1734
01:31:11,341 --> 01:31:12,926
I don't even know you.

1735
01:31:21,643 --> 01:31:24,021
I should probably go now.

1736
01:31:30,444 --> 01:31:31,945
I really am sorry, Peter.

1737
01:31:50,297 --> 01:31:51,506
I don't have a phone.

1738
01:31:52,382 --> 01:31:53,383
Um...

1739
01:31:54,718 --> 01:31:56,053
Do you mind taking me home?

1740
01:31:58,889 --> 01:32:00,056
Yeah, of course.

1741
01:32:00,057 --> 01:32:01,058
Thank you.

1742
01:32:02,935 --> 01:32:04,937
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1743
01:32:40,806 --> 01:32:41,974
[MJ GRUNTS]

1744
01:32:43,183 --> 01:32:45,601
- [SIGHS] Thank you.
- SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, sure.

1745
01:32:45,602 --> 01:32:47,937
Um, I'm going to, uh...

1746
01:32:47,938 --> 01:32:49,439
Uh, yeah, yeah. Yeah, of course.

1747
01:32:52,442 --> 01:32:53,860
[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

1748
01:32:58,949 --> 01:33:00,033
Do you wanna come up?

1749
01:33:02,202 --> 01:33:04,454
Just to say hi to Ned. Maybe.

1750
01:33:07,874 --> 01:33:08,875
SPIDER-MAN: I would love that.

1751
01:33:09,835 --> 01:33:10,918
MJ: Okay.

1752
01:33:10,919 --> 01:33:14,255
FEMALE REPORTER: <i>The Hulk,
a.k.a. Dr. Bruce Banner, is in custody,</i>

1753
01:33:14,256 --> 01:33:16,632
<i>currently being transferred
to a psychiatric ward.</i>

1754
01:33:16,633 --> 01:33:17,842
NED: Oh! So sad.

1755
01:33:17,843 --> 01:33:20,219
FEMALE REPORTER: <i>After years
as a peaceful academic,</i>

1756
01:33:20,220 --> 01:33:23,139
<i>the question the world asked today is,</i>

1757
01:33:23,140 --> 01:33:24,682
<i>"What finally snapped?"</i>

1758
01:33:24,683 --> 01:33:26,475
- [PHONE VIBRATES]
- [<i>SPIDER-MAN</i> THEME PLAYS]

1759
01:33:26,476 --> 01:33:27,727
[GASPS]

1760
01:33:27,728 --> 01:33:29,062
[PHONE VIBRATING]

1761
01:33:29,813 --> 01:33:30,896
[DOOR OPENS]

1762
01:33:30,897 --> 01:33:32,482
APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1763
01:33:32,816 --> 01:33:34,567
<i>- Hey, I'm nearby.</i>
- MJ?

1764
01:33:34,568 --> 01:33:35,943
MJ: Yeah.
APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1765
01:33:35,944 --> 01:33:37,028
[DOOR CLOSES]

1766
01:33:37,029 --> 01:33:38,362
<i>- Hey, I'm nearby.</i>
- Uh...

1767
01:33:38,363 --> 01:33:39,572
You're not gonna believe this...

1768
01:33:39,573 --> 01:33:41,574
- APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>
- ...but the Spidey Tracker app

1769
01:33:41,575 --> 01:33:42,783
- says that Spider-Man...
- APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1770
01:33:42,784 --> 01:33:44,827
- ...is in the direct vicinity.
- APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1771
01:33:44,828 --> 01:33:45,745
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, yeah? No way.

1772
01:33:45,746 --> 01:33:46,663
- That's crazy.
- APP VOICE: <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1773
01:33:47,372 --> 01:33:48,749
[DISTORTED] <i>Hey, I'm nearby.</i>

1774
01:33:49,374 --> 01:33:51,918
Uh, Ned, Spider-Man. Spider-Man, Ned.

1775
01:33:52,377 --> 01:33:53,544
It's nice to meet you, Ned.

1776
01:33:53,545 --> 01:33:54,713
Hello. [CHUCKLES]

1777
01:33:55,422 --> 01:33:56,505
I'm not, like, a weirdo

1778
01:33:56,506 --> 01:33:57,591
- or anything, I'm...
- He's a little weird.

1779
01:33:58,091 --> 01:34:00,801
Why, uh... Why are you here? [CHUCKLES]

1780
01:34:00,802 --> 01:34:02,595
- SPIDER-MAN: Oh, I...
- I was...

1781
01:34:02,596 --> 01:34:03,929
- I was on a subway platform.
- SPIDER-MAN: She was in the...

1782
01:34:03,930 --> 01:34:04,847
Platform. Right.

1783
01:34:04,848 --> 01:34:05,931
- And she was on her phone.
- Yeah, and...

1784
01:34:05,932 --> 01:34:07,016
Yeah, I got a little distracted.

1785
01:34:07,017 --> 01:34:08,225
- And the train was coming and he...
- SPIDER-MAN: I mean...

1786
01:34:08,226 --> 01:34:09,518
And I just swooped her right up.

1787
01:34:09,519 --> 01:34:11,021
- Yep. Saved me.
- SPIDER-MAN: Yeah.

1788
01:34:12,731 --> 01:34:14,316
Oh, my God.

1789
01:34:15,400 --> 01:34:16,942
Why has that never happened to me?

1790
01:34:16,943 --> 01:34:19,445
- [INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]
- So what if you're mid-swing

1791
01:34:19,446 --> 01:34:20,946
and you decide you need to pee?

1792
01:34:20,947 --> 01:34:22,573
Do you just land on top of a building?

1793
01:34:22,574 --> 01:34:23,783
SPIDER-MAN: What?

1794
01:34:23,784 --> 01:34:24,867
Do you drop down to ground level

1795
01:34:24,868 --> 01:34:26,077
and run into a coffee shop
and you're like,

1796
01:34:26,078 --> 01:34:27,411
"Hey, it's Spider-Man. I need to pee"?

1797
01:34:27,412 --> 01:34:29,246
Or do you find a rooftop somewhere?

1798
01:34:29,247 --> 01:34:31,165
SPIDER-MAN: No, I don't find
a rooftop somewhere, Ned.

1799
01:34:31,166 --> 01:34:33,250
Is this really
what you wanna be asking him right now?

1800
01:34:33,251 --> 01:34:34,835
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, dude, come on,
you can ask me anything.

1801
01:34:34,836 --> 01:34:36,420
You wanna know how my web shooters work?

1802
01:34:36,421 --> 01:34:38,047
I mean, I already know
how the web shooters work.

1803
01:34:38,048 --> 01:34:39,382
SPIDER-MAN: Is that right?

1804
01:34:39,383 --> 01:34:42,551
Well, there's obviously
some sort of a shear-thinning fluid

1805
01:34:42,552 --> 01:34:46,138
that is cycling within a chamber, right?
So it can keep its liquid form.

1806
01:34:46,139 --> 01:34:48,557
And then, when you activate it
by pressing on the triggers,

1807
01:34:48,558 --> 01:34:50,226
it runs through a Teflon turbine,

1808
01:34:50,227 --> 01:34:54,022
and then it hardens
when it interacts with the air. Right?

1809
01:34:56,316 --> 01:34:59,193
SPIDER-MAN: Uh...
I mean, not exactly, but...

1810
01:34:59,194 --> 01:35:01,570
Okay, okay, well, then tell me
what's in the web fluid.

1811
01:35:01,571 --> 01:35:04,573
I would guess something
like a long chain polymer.

1812
01:35:04,574 --> 01:35:05,991
Uh, nylon?

1813
01:35:05,992 --> 01:35:07,076
SPIDER-MAN: That's pretty close.

1814
01:35:07,077 --> 01:35:10,038
Okay, okay.
What about Nomex or, oh, Kevlar?

1815
01:35:12,624 --> 01:35:14,542
[IMITATES FRODO] "All right, then.
Keep your secrets."

1816
01:35:14,543 --> 01:35:16,752
SPIDER-MAN: [IMITATES GANDALF]
"If you're referring to the incident

1817
01:35:16,753 --> 01:35:17,753
- with the dragon..."
- [CHUCKLES]

1818
01:35:17,754 --> 01:35:19,088
"...I was barely involved."

1819
01:35:19,089 --> 01:35:20,840
[IMITATES GANDALF] "All I did was simply

1820
01:35:20,841 --> 01:35:22,883
"give your uncle a little nudge
out the door."

1821
01:35:22,884 --> 01:35:24,886
[ALL LAUGH]

1822
01:35:25,345 --> 01:35:26,512
NED: Solid reference.

1823
01:35:26,513 --> 01:35:27,638
[WATCH CHIMES]

1824
01:35:27,639 --> 01:35:29,432
Ooh, banh mi time.

1825
01:35:29,433 --> 01:35:30,891
You ordered banh mis?

1826
01:35:30,892 --> 01:35:32,184
I ordered five banh mis.

1827
01:35:32,185 --> 01:35:34,186
We have Spider-Man in the apartment.
He's gonna get fed.

1828
01:35:34,187 --> 01:35:35,939
- [CHUCKLES]
- [NED CHUCKLES]

1829
01:35:37,774 --> 01:35:40,860
Sorry about him. He's just, like,
very excited that you're here.

1830
01:35:40,861 --> 01:35:43,279
SPIDER-MAN: You kidding? This is, like,
the most fun I've had in years.

1831
01:35:43,280 --> 01:35:45,365
- [MJ CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
- I really missed you guys.

1832
01:35:47,284 --> 01:35:49,368
You guys really do look like best friends.

1833
01:35:49,369 --> 01:35:50,370
SPIDER-MAN: What do you mean?

1834
01:35:59,921 --> 01:36:00,922
You should tell him.

1835
01:36:01,673 --> 01:36:02,674
He can handle it.

1836
01:36:04,551 --> 01:36:06,136
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, I know. [SIGHS]

1837
01:36:08,263 --> 01:36:09,222
Um...

1838
01:36:12,684 --> 01:36:16,021
When she was inhabiting you
on the rooftop,

1839
01:36:17,439 --> 01:36:18,648
she kissed me...

1840
01:36:19,691 --> 01:36:21,400
and I kissed her back,

1841
01:36:21,401 --> 01:36:23,862
because I... I thought it was you,
but I didn't know.

1842
01:36:24,613 --> 01:36:26,406
And I'm... I'm really sorry.

1843
01:36:27,782 --> 01:36:29,075
I just thought you should know.

1844
01:36:31,495 --> 01:36:32,496
Thanks for telling me.

1845
01:36:36,124 --> 01:36:38,877
I mean, it's not like
I remember anything anyway, so...

1846
01:36:40,295 --> 01:36:41,462
SPIDER-MAN: Really?

1847
01:36:41,463 --> 01:36:44,381
Yeah. It was weird, it was like,
one second I was sitting at my desk,

1848
01:36:44,382 --> 01:36:46,134
and the next second
I was lying on the street.

1849
01:36:47,052 --> 01:36:48,677
I don't know,
like a light switch went off.

1850
01:36:48,678 --> 01:36:51,138
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

1851
01:36:51,139 --> 01:36:52,306
What?

1852
01:36:52,307 --> 01:36:53,683
SPIDER-MAN: So you don't
remember anything?

1853
01:36:55,727 --> 01:36:56,810
No. Why?

1854
01:36:56,811 --> 01:36:59,855
SPIDER-MAN: Metzger said he remembered
thinking about someone named Sara,

1855
01:36:59,856 --> 01:37:03,109
but what you're saying is that
you don't remember anything at all?

1856
01:37:05,237 --> 01:37:07,696
I mean, yeah, it was instantaneous.

1857
01:37:07,697 --> 01:37:08,865
That's what made it so scary.

1858
01:37:10,909 --> 01:37:12,160
SPIDER-MAN: He lied to me.

1859
01:37:13,703 --> 01:37:14,704
[LINE RINGING]

1860
01:37:15,205 --> 01:37:16,830
<i>I heard you caught leshy.</i>

1861
01:37:16,831 --> 01:37:18,207
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah. Her name's Jean Grey.

1862
01:37:18,208 --> 01:37:20,668
I need some help
determining the size of some potatoes.

1863
01:37:20,669 --> 01:37:22,545
- Potatoes?
- [SOFTLY] I think that's Black Widow.

1864
01:37:22,546 --> 01:37:24,588
SPIDER-MAN: I think Metzger lied to me
about a name.

1865
01:37:24,589 --> 01:37:28,134
<i>Can you see if there's a connection
between Jean and someone named Sara?</i>

1866
01:37:28,677 --> 01:37:31,011
Hmm. These potatoes sound meager.

1867
01:37:31,012 --> 01:37:32,596
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]
- [LAPTOP TRILLING]

1868
01:37:32,597 --> 01:37:34,349
SPIDER-MAN: Oh, wow.
That really is your office.

1869
01:37:35,058 --> 01:37:36,225
Well, well, well.

1870
01:37:36,226 --> 01:37:38,686
Internet, government records,

1871
01:37:38,687 --> 01:37:43,482
and a lot of data related to Jean Grey
has been scrubbed by Damage Control.

1872
01:37:43,483 --> 01:37:44,484
SPIDER-MAN: <i>Data about what?</i>

1873
01:37:45,443 --> 01:37:46,444
Her sister.

1874
01:37:47,153 --> 01:37:48,572
SPIDER-MAN: Wait, Jean has a sister?

1875
01:37:50,198 --> 01:37:52,241
Hmm. Sara Grey.

1876
01:37:52,242 --> 01:37:54,034
<i>Also a telepath.</i>

1877
01:37:54,035 --> 01:37:57,913
<i>Damage Control took her into custody
for study and observation.</i>

1878
01:37:57,914 --> 01:38:00,249
<i>Wow. I mean, you can probably guess
what they mean by that.</i>

1879
01:38:00,250 --> 01:38:02,626
Experimentation
and other human rights violations.

1880
01:38:02,627 --> 01:38:04,503
Hmm. Yes, exactly. Wait, who are you?

1881
01:38:04,504 --> 01:38:06,338
<i>- Hi. Ned Leeds. Big fan.</i>
- MJ: <i>I'm...</i>

1882
01:38:06,339 --> 01:38:07,715
Hi.

1883
01:38:07,716 --> 01:38:09,258
SPIDER-MAN: <i>Uh, I'm sorry. Uh...</i> [GRUNTS]

1884
01:38:09,259 --> 01:38:12,262
I'm just so happy
that the sad man has friends.

1885
01:38:13,096 --> 01:38:14,430
[SPIDER-MAN CHUCKLES]

1886
01:38:14,431 --> 01:38:16,641
Thanks. I, uh... I owe you one.

1887
01:38:17,767 --> 01:38:19,143
YELENA: <i>Good luck, Spider-Man.</i>

1888
01:38:19,144 --> 01:38:20,269
Bye.

1889
01:38:20,270 --> 01:38:21,812
SPIDER-MAN: She was
just looking for her sister

1890
01:38:21,813 --> 01:38:24,023
and I handed her
to the people that took her.

1891
01:38:24,024 --> 01:38:25,691
- I gotta go.
- MJ: Hey, Peter...

1892
01:38:25,692 --> 01:38:26,693
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah?

1893
01:38:27,736 --> 01:38:28,820
Just be careful, all right?

1894
01:38:30,697 --> 01:38:31,698
SPIDER-MAN: Yeah, I will.

1895
01:38:35,035 --> 01:38:36,535
[WEB SHOOTER CLICKS]

1896
01:38:36,536 --> 01:38:38,204
Spider-Man's name is Peter?

1897
01:38:40,332 --> 01:38:42,375
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1898
01:38:51,885 --> 01:38:54,179
Jean, who do you want to be?

1899
01:38:56,723 --> 01:38:58,099
Her. Pink jacket.

1900
01:38:59,726 --> 01:39:00,727
She's too far.

1901
01:39:01,770 --> 01:39:02,853
You're gonna have to hop.

1902
01:39:02,854 --> 01:39:04,313
JEAN: Hop?

1903
01:39:04,314 --> 01:39:06,358
First, pick someone close.

1904
01:39:07,025 --> 01:39:08,026
And then...

1905
01:39:10,195 --> 01:39:12,280
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

1906
01:39:13,573 --> 01:39:14,949
[WHOOSHING]

1907
01:39:20,914 --> 01:39:22,206
[JEAN LAUGHS]

1908
01:39:22,207 --> 01:39:23,208
Each hop has a limit.

1909
01:39:23,875 --> 01:39:27,087
But you can string them together
and go as far as you want.

1910
01:39:27,754 --> 01:39:29,547
- And when you let go...
- [WHOOSHES]

1911
01:39:30,298 --> 01:39:31,591
You're right back where you started.

1912
01:39:32,801 --> 01:39:35,053
Could you do that
to everyone in this park at once?

1913
01:39:36,012 --> 01:39:37,347
Well, yeah, maybe one day.

1914
01:39:38,056 --> 01:39:39,265
If you get really good.

1915
01:39:41,184 --> 01:39:42,560
[GIRL LAUGHING]

1916
01:39:44,813 --> 01:39:46,815
[BOTH LAUGHING]

1917
01:39:52,904 --> 01:39:53,905
How could she just...

1918
01:39:55,156 --> 01:39:56,199
send us away?

1919
01:39:57,826 --> 01:39:59,160
She wasn't really a mom.

1920
01:40:01,371 --> 01:40:02,538
Not like that, anyway.

1921
01:40:02,539 --> 01:40:04,623
She was, before we changed.

1922
01:40:04,624 --> 01:40:06,542
Yeah, well, if that's all it takes
for you to stop being a mom,

1923
01:40:06,543 --> 01:40:07,544
then you're not a mom.

1924
01:40:08,461 --> 01:40:10,588
What would you do
if you had daughters like us?

1925
01:40:11,089 --> 01:40:12,173
I'd love them.

1926
01:40:15,760 --> 01:40:17,470
- Especially the redhead one.
- Shut up.

1927
01:40:20,265 --> 01:40:21,641
We have each other.

1928
01:40:22,851 --> 01:40:23,977
Mmm.

1929
01:40:25,437 --> 01:40:27,063
SARA: And we have ice cream.

1930
01:40:28,940 --> 01:40:30,316
- One mint chip, one chocolate?
- Yeah.

1931
01:40:34,320 --> 01:40:35,655
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]
- [WOMAN GRUNTS]

1932
01:40:36,740 --> 01:40:37,741
WOMAN: Okay.

1933
01:40:39,284 --> 01:40:40,951
Now I know how you're playing.

1934
01:40:40,952 --> 01:40:42,579
- [GIRL LAUGHING]
- Oh.

1935
01:40:48,585 --> 01:40:49,753
[SARA WINCES]

1936
01:40:54,466 --> 01:40:55,717
[VEHICLE APPROACHING]

1937
01:40:58,303 --> 01:40:59,386
GUARD 1: Get down!
GUARD 2: Get down!

1938
01:40:59,387 --> 01:41:01,054
GUARD 3: Get down! Get down!
GUARD 1: Get down! Get down!

1939
01:41:01,055 --> 01:41:02,973
GUARD 2: Get down on the ground now!
GUARD 3: Get down! Get down!

1940
01:41:02,974 --> 01:41:04,058
[GASPS]

1941
01:41:05,310 --> 01:41:06,311
Sara!

1942
01:41:08,688 --> 01:41:10,106
[PANTING]

1943
01:41:11,900 --> 01:41:13,318
SARA: <i>I'm sorry, Jean.</i>

1944
01:41:14,152 --> 01:41:15,694
<i>I have to keep you safe.</i>

1945
01:41:15,695 --> 01:41:18,197
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

1946
01:41:18,198 --> 01:41:19,364
[WHOOSHES]

1947
01:41:19,365 --> 01:41:21,159
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

1948
01:41:26,039 --> 01:41:27,874
[MUSIC CRESCENDOES]

1949
01:41:28,792 --> 01:41:30,335
[GASPS, PANTS]

1950
01:41:33,505 --> 01:41:35,381
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1951
01:41:43,556 --> 01:41:45,558
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1952
01:41:47,101 --> 01:41:49,103
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1953
01:41:58,154 --> 01:42:01,282
METZGER: Subject is awake.
Heart rate is 94 bpm.

1954
01:42:01,866 --> 01:42:04,034
[FAINT TRILLING]

1955
01:42:04,035 --> 01:42:07,622
Jean, that's not gonna work anymore,
thanks to Spider-Man.

1956
01:42:08,248 --> 01:42:10,582
[GRUNTS, PANTING]

1957
01:42:10,583 --> 01:42:12,085
- [JEAN GRUNTS SOFTLY]
- Jean?

1958
01:42:12,585 --> 01:42:13,586
[GRUNTING]

1959
01:42:14,128 --> 01:42:17,090
[JEAN GRUNTS, PANTS]

1960
01:42:21,636 --> 01:42:22,970
I need you to breathe.

1961
01:42:22,971 --> 01:42:24,721
I need you to look at me and breathe.

1962
01:42:24,722 --> 01:42:26,473
- [BREATHES DEEPLY]
- METZGER: Okay?

1963
01:42:26,474 --> 01:42:27,976
You're safe. Breathe.

1964
01:42:30,562 --> 01:42:31,729
Where is she?

1965
01:42:33,147 --> 01:42:35,148
Like your sister,
you've been blessed with a power

1966
01:42:35,149 --> 01:42:37,944
that has the potential
to do tremendous good in the world,

1967
01:42:38,695 --> 01:42:40,029
or tremendous damage.

1968
01:42:40,989 --> 01:42:44,993
A power like yours in the hands of a child
is an impossible burden.

1969
01:42:45,702 --> 01:42:46,786
But imagine...

1970
01:42:47,912 --> 01:42:50,414
if that power was placed
in the hands of people

1971
01:42:50,415 --> 01:42:51,791
who actually know what to do with it.

1972
01:43:00,800 --> 01:43:02,552
Where is my sister?

1973
01:43:05,430 --> 01:43:07,432
METZGER: You're gonna change
the world, Jean.

1974
01:43:07,807 --> 01:43:08,808
Hey!

1975
01:43:09,559 --> 01:43:11,561
Hey! [GRUNTING]

1976
01:43:13,187 --> 01:43:15,189
- [MACHINERY WHIRRING]
- [GASPS]

1977
01:43:17,400 --> 01:43:19,402
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

1978
01:43:29,996 --> 01:43:31,830
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

1979
01:43:31,831 --> 01:43:33,665
- [PHONE RINGING]
- SPIDER-MAN: Frank.

1980
01:43:33,666 --> 01:43:35,667
I know where you are, what you're doing.

1981
01:43:35,668 --> 01:43:36,794
SPIDER-MAN: <i>Oh, yeah? And how's that?</i>

1982
01:43:37,420 --> 01:43:38,879
I got eyes everywhere, kid.

1983
01:43:38,880 --> 01:43:40,297
[BEEPING]

1984
01:43:40,298 --> 01:43:43,008
SPIDER-MAN: Look, Frank.
Damage Control kidnapped Jean's sister.

1985
01:43:43,009 --> 01:43:45,552
Jean was just trying to find her.
We were wrong about everything.

1986
01:43:45,553 --> 01:43:46,971
Sentimental horseshit.

1987
01:43:47,847 --> 01:43:50,015
You've seen what she can do
and what she's capable of.

1988
01:43:50,016 --> 01:43:52,560
What, you're gonna let her loose?
Is that what you're gonna do?

1989
01:43:53,770 --> 01:43:57,273
I'll tell you right now, you do that,
I handle it my way.

1990
01:43:57,774 --> 01:43:58,690
SPIDER-MAN: <i>Frank, please, can you just...</i>

1991
01:43:58,691 --> 01:43:59,608
- Eh...
- [CALL ENDS]

1992
01:43:59,609 --> 01:44:00,693
SPIDER-MAN: Frank!

1993
01:44:00,902 --> 01:44:02,904
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

1994
01:44:13,289 --> 01:44:14,456
Distance check?

1995
01:44:14,457 --> 01:44:15,791
- [KEYBOARD CLACKING]
- Forty-foot clearance.

1996
01:44:15,792 --> 01:44:17,292
METZGER: Locking down the room.

1997
01:44:17,293 --> 01:44:18,210
GUARD: Locking down.

1998
01:44:18,211 --> 01:44:19,754
[DOOR BUZZES]

1999
01:44:23,549 --> 01:44:24,550
METZGER: <i>Disengage inhibitor.</i>

2000
01:44:27,428 --> 01:44:29,096
[GROANS SOFTLY]

2001
01:44:29,097 --> 01:44:31,348
METZGER: <i>Jean, your powers
are now fully operational.</i>

2002
01:44:31,349 --> 01:44:33,601
- [HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]
- [WARBLING]

2003
01:44:35,061 --> 01:44:36,187
[JEAN STRAINING]

2004
01:44:38,272 --> 01:44:40,066
[GRUNTS, GROANS]

2005
01:44:40,817 --> 01:44:43,653
METZGER: <i>As you can tell,
we are beyond your jump radius.</i>

2006
01:44:44,278 --> 01:44:46,739
[BREATHING HEAVILY] Tell me what V-Max is.

2007
01:44:47,532 --> 01:44:49,575
You're the second person
to ask me about that. I...

2008
01:44:50,284 --> 01:44:51,786
I have no idea what that means.

2009
01:44:51,911 --> 01:44:53,454
JEAN: <i>She sent me a message.</i>

2010
01:44:54,122 --> 01:44:55,915
She was trying to help me find her.

2011
01:44:56,916 --> 01:45:00,378
She communicated with you telepathically
across all that distance?

2012
01:45:00,795 --> 01:45:03,840
We did register a huge spike
in that session.

2013
01:45:05,675 --> 01:45:06,842
Fascinating.

2014
01:45:06,843 --> 01:45:09,053
What does it mean, asshole?

2015
01:45:10,763 --> 01:45:11,806
I don't know.

2016
01:45:12,765 --> 01:45:14,182
Let's begin.

2017
01:45:14,183 --> 01:45:15,727
[DEVICE BUZZES]

2018
01:45:17,478 --> 01:45:20,064
[DEVICE POWERING UP]

2019
01:45:22,275 --> 01:45:24,651
METZGER: <i>Our work with Sara
centered on two areas,</i>

2020
01:45:24,652 --> 01:45:27,029
identifying the source of her power

2021
01:45:27,030 --> 01:45:29,365
and identifying a path towards copying it.

2022
01:45:29,615 --> 01:45:31,450
- [SYSTEM TRILLING]
- If we could find a way

2023
01:45:31,451 --> 01:45:34,036
to record a telepathic brain
during a jump,

2024
01:45:34,037 --> 01:45:37,164
then perhaps we could replicate
those pathways

2025
01:45:37,165 --> 01:45:38,916
in a mind of our choosing.

2026
01:45:40,334 --> 01:45:43,463
<i>This instrument is your sister's legacy.</i>

2027
01:45:44,589 --> 01:45:47,467
<i>We built this together
over many months of trial and error.</i>

2028
01:45:48,718 --> 01:45:50,845
I hope you and I can honor her sacrifice.

2029
01:45:54,015 --> 01:45:55,349
What are you talking about?

2030
01:45:56,851 --> 01:45:58,186
Trigger the first jump.

2031
01:45:59,645 --> 01:46:01,439
[DEVICE TRILLING]

2032
01:46:02,899 --> 01:46:05,484
Tell me what V-Max is.

2033
01:46:05,485 --> 01:46:07,152
I know that's where you're hiding her.

2034
01:46:07,153 --> 01:46:08,945
- [WHOOSHES]
- [HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2035
01:46:08,946 --> 01:46:10,031
[DEVICE TRILLING]

2036
01:46:11,449 --> 01:46:12,867
[GASPS, PANTS]

2037
01:46:16,245 --> 01:46:18,163
- [DEVICE TRILLING]
- [WHOOSHES]

2038
01:46:18,164 --> 01:46:19,874
{\an8}[SYSTEM CRACKLING]

2039
01:46:22,335 --> 01:46:23,418
She's jumping.

2040
01:46:23,419 --> 01:46:25,629
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CRESCENDOES, ENDS]

2041
01:46:25,630 --> 01:46:26,631
Copy.

2042
01:46:27,173 --> 01:46:30,258
We're in full lockdown.
Process has commenced.

2043
01:46:30,259 --> 01:46:31,260
SPIDER-MAN: What process?

2044
01:46:32,720 --> 01:46:35,056
Hey, whoa,
that's a pretty serious look there, dude.

2045
01:46:35,932 --> 01:46:37,557
Hey, hey, whoa! What the hell, man?

2046
01:46:37,558 --> 01:46:39,644
Come on. I'm a friend of Damage Control.
What are you doin'?

2047
01:46:43,106 --> 01:46:44,189
Huh.

2048
01:46:44,190 --> 01:46:45,733
It's gonna be like that. You wanna go.

2049
01:46:45,858 --> 01:46:46,859
All right.

2050
01:46:47,360 --> 01:46:48,861
All right, well, just give me a sec.

2051
01:46:49,403 --> 01:46:50,446
Give me a sec.

2052
01:46:51,280 --> 01:46:52,906
I'm not in high school anymore.

2053
01:46:52,907 --> 01:46:54,242
[GRUNTING]

2054
01:46:54,992 --> 01:46:56,576
Do you stretch? You a big stretcher?

2055
01:46:56,577 --> 01:46:57,954
I mean, you should do
in your line of work.

2056
01:46:58,621 --> 01:47:01,832
What about you? You guys stretch?
It's so good for you.

2057
01:47:01,833 --> 01:47:03,375
[GROANING]

2058
01:47:03,376 --> 01:47:04,459
You ready?

2059
01:47:04,460 --> 01:47:06,587
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2060
01:47:14,011 --> 01:47:15,012
Watch your head!

2061
01:47:19,892 --> 01:47:21,144
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

2062
01:47:23,146 --> 01:47:24,313
[GROANING]

2063
01:47:26,023 --> 01:47:27,316
- [GUARD GRUNTING]
- [SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2064
01:47:34,907 --> 01:47:36,700
Where is Jean Grey?

2065
01:47:36,701 --> 01:47:37,701
[WHOOSHES]

2066
01:47:37,702 --> 01:47:39,536
- [DEVICE TRILLING]
- TECHNICIAN: That's jump 26.

2067
01:47:39,537 --> 01:47:40,871
- Recordings look good.
- [WHOOSHING CONTINUES]

2068
01:47:40,872 --> 01:47:42,039
GUARD: Excuse me, sir.

2069
01:47:42,915 --> 01:47:44,000
We have an intruder.

2070
01:47:44,792 --> 01:47:45,918
[WHOOSHING]

2071
01:47:47,253 --> 01:47:48,337
[DOOR BEEPS, CLICKS]

2072
01:47:49,088 --> 01:47:50,380
- TECHNICIAN: You were right.
- [WHOOSHING]

2073
01:47:50,381 --> 01:47:52,425
She's much stronger than her sister.

2074
01:47:53,426 --> 01:47:54,759
Increase the frequency.

2075
01:47:54,760 --> 01:47:56,178
[DEVICE AMPLIFIES, WARBLES]

2076
01:47:56,179 --> 01:47:57,596
You're doing very well, Jean.

2077
01:47:57,597 --> 01:47:59,055
- [DEVICE TRILLING]
- [WHOOSHING RAPIDLY]

2078
01:47:59,056 --> 01:48:02,684
- [DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]
- [SYSTEM CRACKLING RAPIDLY]

2079
01:48:02,685 --> 01:48:05,479
- [DEVICE TRILLING]
- [WHOOSHING RAPIDLY]

2080
01:48:06,689 --> 01:48:08,149
[SILENCE]

2081
01:48:09,442 --> 01:48:12,028
[PANTING STEADILY]

2082
01:48:13,696 --> 01:48:15,573
[RATTLING OVERHEAD]

2083
01:48:20,077 --> 01:48:21,913
[VENT RATTLING FAINTLY]

2084
01:48:29,712 --> 01:48:31,421
[VENT RATTLING]

2085
01:48:31,422 --> 01:48:32,924
[LABEL RUSTLING]

2086
01:48:34,217 --> 01:48:35,384
[SCOFFS WEAKLY]

2087
01:48:36,761 --> 01:48:38,179
[LABEL RUSTLING]

2088
01:48:45,478 --> 01:48:46,812
METZGER: <i>Jean?</i>

2089
01:48:49,065 --> 01:48:51,233
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]
- [SYSTEM CRACKLING]

2090
01:48:51,234 --> 01:48:52,484
METZGER: Jean, can you hear me?

2091
01:48:52,485 --> 01:48:54,779
[SYSTEM CHIMING, CRACKLING RAPIDLY]

2092
01:48:56,489 --> 01:48:58,865
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2093
01:48:58,866 --> 01:48:59,950
Jean?

2094
01:48:59,951 --> 01:49:01,619
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2095
01:49:04,455 --> 01:49:05,747
You're a murderer.

2096
01:49:05,748 --> 01:49:07,583
[SYSTEM BEEPING RAPIDLY]

2097
01:49:08,000 --> 01:49:11,169
- Her frequencies are evolving.
- [SYSTEM CRACKLING]

2098
01:49:11,170 --> 01:49:12,338
This doesn't make sense.

2099
01:49:13,381 --> 01:49:17,634
The last thing
my sister saw was this room.

2100
01:49:17,635 --> 01:49:20,345
TECHNICIAN: Her brainwaves are somehow
affecting the objects around her.

2101
01:49:20,346 --> 01:49:21,429
Shut it down.

2102
01:49:21,430 --> 01:49:22,722
I'm trying, sir.

2103
01:49:22,723 --> 01:49:23,724
What do you mean you're trying?

2104
01:49:24,225 --> 01:49:29,396
The last thing my sister saw
was this goddamn room!

2105
01:49:29,397 --> 01:49:31,274
- Shut it down!
- I can't, sir.

2106
01:49:32,358 --> 01:49:33,359
Move.

2107
01:49:33,985 --> 01:49:35,819
[ALARM BLARING]

2108
01:49:35,820 --> 01:49:37,821
I can't let you do that, Bill.

2109
01:49:37,822 --> 01:49:39,824
[OMINOUS MUSICAL STING]

2110
01:49:41,450 --> 01:49:43,493
- [FIELD WARBLING]
- The only hands

2111
01:49:43,494 --> 01:49:45,578
that will wield this power...

2112
01:49:45,579 --> 01:49:48,040
- [HIGH-PITCHED RINGING STOPS]
- ...are mine.

2113
01:49:48,833 --> 01:49:50,876
- [WHOOSHES]
- [ALL GRUNTING]

2114
01:49:52,545 --> 01:49:54,547
[FIELD WARBLING]

2115
01:49:55,506 --> 01:49:57,591
[ALL SCREAMING, GRUNTING]

2116
01:49:58,843 --> 01:50:01,136
- [HORN HONKING]
- [PEOPLE GRUNTING]

2117
01:50:01,137 --> 01:50:02,220
[ALL GRUNTING]

2118
01:50:02,221 --> 01:50:03,847
[OBJECTS CLATTERING]

2119
01:50:03,848 --> 01:50:06,267
- [TIRES SCREECH]
- [CAR ALARM BLARING]

2120
01:50:07,685 --> 01:50:09,145
[BRAKES SQUEAL]

2121
01:50:10,271 --> 01:50:11,647
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

2122
01:50:12,773 --> 01:50:14,525
- [EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]
- WOMAN: What is happening?

2123
01:50:15,901 --> 01:50:17,320
MAN 1: Get inside.

2124
01:50:19,905 --> 01:50:20,948
[DOG BARKING]

2125
01:50:24,243 --> 01:50:25,327
MAN 2: Wait for me!

2126
01:50:25,328 --> 01:50:26,912
[BARKING]

2127
01:50:28,039 --> 01:50:29,707
[FIELD WARBLING]

2128
01:50:35,921 --> 01:50:37,631
- [WHOOSHES]
- [PEOPLE SCREAM]

2129
01:50:43,095 --> 01:50:45,097
[FIELD WARBLING]

2130
01:50:47,558 --> 01:50:49,560
[BREATHES HEAVILY]

2131
01:50:57,276 --> 01:51:00,071
- [HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]
- [WHOOSHES]

2132
01:51:06,369 --> 01:51:08,162
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2133
01:51:09,914 --> 01:51:11,916
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

2134
01:51:53,207 --> 01:51:55,376
[EERIE MUSIC PLAYING]

2135
01:52:00,714 --> 01:52:02,299
- What...
- ALL: What do you want?

2136
01:52:06,011 --> 01:52:08,973
SPIDER-MAN: Jean, I'm here to help you.

2137
01:52:10,307 --> 01:52:11,684
You put me here.

2138
01:52:12,351 --> 01:52:14,269
SPIDER-MAN: I know,
and I'm sorry about Sara,

2139
01:52:14,270 --> 01:52:16,355
and I'm sorry that I got it so wrong.

2140
01:52:17,064 --> 01:52:18,149
[DOOR SLAMS]

2141
01:52:18,607 --> 01:52:19,691
JEAN: If you came here

2142
01:52:19,692 --> 01:52:22,945
to save a helpless girl
from Damage Control, you're too late.

2143
01:52:24,029 --> 01:52:25,905
They're the ones who need saving.

2144
01:52:25,906 --> 01:52:27,283
And now...

2145
01:52:27,867 --> 01:52:28,868
so do you.

2146
01:52:30,119 --> 01:52:31,327
[SPIDER-MAN SIGHS]

2147
01:52:31,328 --> 01:52:32,412
Here we go.

2148
01:52:32,413 --> 01:52:33,747
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2149
01:52:41,630 --> 01:52:43,174
- [MALE NINJA GRUNTS]
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

2150
01:52:46,844 --> 01:52:48,304
SPIDER-MAN: God, that's cool.

2151
01:52:49,722 --> 01:52:51,015
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2152
01:52:54,143 --> 01:52:55,769
[SPIDER-MAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

2153
01:53:03,736 --> 01:53:05,112
SPIDER-MAN: Ow! Ow!

2154
01:53:09,366 --> 01:53:11,451
Jean! Jean, please!

2155
01:53:11,452 --> 01:53:13,204
[THUDDING]

2156
01:53:24,173 --> 01:53:25,715
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTING]

2157
01:53:25,716 --> 01:53:27,426
Come on! Come on! Come on!

2158
01:53:30,721 --> 01:53:32,347
- [FEMALE NINJA GRUNTS]
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANS]

2159
01:53:32,348 --> 01:53:33,473
[GROANS]

2160
01:53:33,474 --> 01:53:35,768
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

2161
01:53:37,811 --> 01:53:39,522
[FIELD WARBLING]

2162
01:53:42,107 --> 01:53:43,359
[WEAPONS ENERGIZING]

2163
01:53:48,113 --> 01:53:49,280
SPIDER-MAN: What the...

2164
01:53:49,281 --> 01:53:50,407
[NINJAS GRUNTING]

2165
01:53:51,075 --> 01:53:52,158
JEAN: Isn't it funny

2166
01:53:52,159 --> 01:53:55,703
how your friends from Damage Control
developed a special weapon

2167
01:53:55,704 --> 01:53:57,038
just for you?

2168
01:53:57,039 --> 01:53:58,248
[SPIDER-MAN PANTING]

2169
01:53:58,249 --> 01:54:01,000
They've got a whole task force ready.

2170
01:54:01,001 --> 01:54:02,919
Just in case you ever get out of line.

2171
01:54:02,920 --> 01:54:05,089
- [FIELD WARBLING]
- [METZGER GRUNTS]

2172
01:54:07,424 --> 01:54:08,801
People are monsters.

2173
01:54:12,555 --> 01:54:13,763
[BOTH GRUNTING]

2174
01:54:13,764 --> 01:54:16,975
You shouldn't trust them
any more than they trust you.

2175
01:54:16,976 --> 01:54:18,185
[NINJA GRUNTING]

2176
01:54:19,645 --> 01:54:20,646
[GROANS]

2177
01:54:23,148 --> 01:54:25,150
- [HORN BLARES]
- [PEOPLE SCREAM]

2178
01:54:27,528 --> 01:54:29,238
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [NINJAS GRUNTING]

2179
01:54:30,573 --> 01:54:31,823
SPIDER-MAN: I'm a little busy, Frank.

2180
01:54:31,824 --> 01:54:33,157
We got a problem, kid.

2181
01:54:33,158 --> 01:54:35,911
<i>She got ahold of everyone
within a kilometer of the island.</i>

2182
01:54:36,036 --> 01:54:37,579
SPIDER-MAN: [SIGHS] Wait, what?

2183
01:54:37,580 --> 01:54:39,372
[FIELD WARBLING]

2184
01:54:39,373 --> 01:54:40,708
[GROANS SOFTLY]

2185
01:54:42,418 --> 01:54:43,626
[WHIMPERING SOFTLY]

2186
01:54:43,627 --> 01:54:45,920
Hey, look, if you're gonna do something,
you better do it now.

2187
01:54:45,921 --> 01:54:47,006
SPIDER-MAN: I'm trying!

2188
01:54:52,511 --> 01:54:53,762
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

2189
01:54:57,516 --> 01:54:58,642
[SPIDER-MAN GRUNTS]

2190
01:55:02,354 --> 01:55:04,773
- [SPIDER-MAN GROANING]
- [NINJAS GRUNTING]

2191
01:55:06,567 --> 01:55:08,611
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

2192
01:55:12,615 --> 01:55:14,115
- [LINE DISCONNECTS]
- Kid?

2193
01:55:14,116 --> 01:55:15,992
Shit! Goddamn it.

2194
01:55:15,993 --> 01:55:18,036
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2195
01:55:18,037 --> 01:55:19,579
[TIRES SCREECHING]

2196
01:55:19,580 --> 01:55:21,080
[HORN HONKING]

2197
01:55:21,081 --> 01:55:22,666
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

2198
01:55:23,876 --> 01:55:25,377
[SPIDER-MAN GROANING]

2199
01:55:26,337 --> 01:55:27,921
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2200
01:55:35,137 --> 01:55:36,555
[COUGHING]

2201
01:55:38,599 --> 01:55:40,016
[GASPS]

2202
01:55:40,017 --> 01:55:41,977
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2203
01:55:49,735 --> 01:55:51,027
JEAN: My sister died

2204
01:55:51,028 --> 01:55:52,279
in this room,

2205
01:55:53,656 --> 01:55:55,282
surrounded by these men.

2206
01:55:56,617 --> 01:55:57,867
And her only crime

2207
01:55:57,868 --> 01:55:59,453
was that she was special.

2208
01:56:00,537 --> 01:56:02,456
- [PANTING]
- JEAN: Just like you.

2209
01:56:03,916 --> 01:56:05,125
Just like me.

2210
01:56:07,795 --> 01:56:10,798
People like us
don't get to live a normal life.

2211
01:56:13,801 --> 01:56:16,970
We don't get to have friends or a family.

2212
01:56:18,972 --> 01:56:20,349
Those people are gone.

2213
01:56:23,185 --> 01:56:24,936
That life is over.

2214
01:56:24,937 --> 01:56:27,106
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2215
01:56:38,701 --> 01:56:41,036
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

2216
01:56:51,046 --> 01:56:53,465
So why don't you just
be honest with yourself?

2217
01:56:56,427 --> 01:56:57,761
Are you Peter Parker?

2218
01:56:59,930 --> 01:57:01,306
Or are you Spider-Man?

2219
01:57:13,652 --> 01:57:15,612
[INHIBITOR BEEPS, POWERS DOWN]

2220
01:57:18,282 --> 01:57:20,200
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

2221
01:57:21,869 --> 01:57:23,454
[DISTORTED WARBLE]

2222
01:57:26,373 --> 01:57:28,375
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

2223
01:57:34,298 --> 01:57:35,381
I'm both.

2224
01:57:35,382 --> 01:57:37,676
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2225
01:57:42,890 --> 01:57:44,016
[NINJA GASPS]

2226
01:57:44,600 --> 01:57:46,602
[HEROIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2227
01:57:49,980 --> 01:57:50,981
[WHOOSHES]

2228
01:58:08,707 --> 01:58:10,000
[NINJA GRUNTS]

2229
01:58:12,336 --> 01:58:13,921
- [WEAPONS ENERGIZING]
- [GRUNTS]

2230
01:58:18,425 --> 01:58:19,426
[GUARD GRUNTS]

2231
01:58:26,141 --> 01:58:27,601
[NINJAS GRUNTING]

2232
01:58:56,004 --> 01:58:57,881
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

2233
01:59:07,641 --> 01:59:09,476
[FIELD WARBLING]

2234
01:59:17,776 --> 01:59:20,111
[PETER BREATHING HEAVILY]

2235
01:59:20,112 --> 01:59:22,155
Jean, please.

2236
01:59:23,448 --> 01:59:24,867
This won't make it right.

2237
01:59:27,035 --> 01:59:28,995
Oh, come on. You're not a killer, Jean.

2238
01:59:28,996 --> 01:59:30,289
You have no idea what I am.

2239
01:59:32,040 --> 01:59:33,667
I know that you loved your sister.

2240
01:59:37,004 --> 01:59:40,047
And I know that losing her
felt like you'd lost everything.

2241
01:59:40,048 --> 01:59:43,092
If you come any closer, he dies!
They all do!

2242
01:59:43,093 --> 01:59:44,595
[FIELD WARBLING]

2243
01:59:46,096 --> 01:59:48,098
[SIRENS WAILING]

2244
01:59:59,026 --> 02:00:00,319
[PETER PANTING]

2245
02:00:01,320 --> 02:00:02,904
You know this won't
bring her back, right, Jean?

2246
02:00:02,905 --> 02:00:04,697
- You... [GRUNTING]
- [FIELD WARBLING]

2247
02:00:04,698 --> 02:00:06,408
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

2248
02:00:11,204 --> 02:00:12,915
[HIGH-PITCHED RINGING]

2249
02:00:20,547 --> 02:00:22,674
Don't be so sure
I can't get into your mind.

2250
02:00:23,216 --> 02:00:24,842
[PETER GRUNTING SOFTLY]

2251
02:00:24,843 --> 02:00:27,095
I'm a lot more powerful
since I last tried.

2252
02:00:28,931 --> 02:00:30,515
[FIELD WARBLING]

2253
02:00:37,230 --> 02:00:38,482
[STRAINING] Go ahead.

2254
02:00:40,275 --> 02:00:41,318
[EXHALES]

2255
02:00:45,697 --> 02:00:46,823
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

2256
02:00:47,532 --> 02:00:48,533
MAY: Hey.

2257
02:00:49,910 --> 02:00:50,911
Hey.

2258
02:00:53,246 --> 02:00:56,958
You think you don't have to listen to me
now that you've got powers?

2259
02:00:56,959 --> 02:00:58,543
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

2260
02:01:01,588 --> 02:01:07,218
You know, this... this whole thing
can get really scary.

2261
02:01:07,219 --> 02:01:08,220
You know that?

2262
02:01:10,764 --> 02:01:12,933
[FIELD WARBLING]

2263
02:01:14,810 --> 02:01:17,270
[SERENE MUSIC PLAYING]

2264
02:01:26,863 --> 02:01:28,448
It's already pretty scary.

2265
02:01:29,866 --> 02:01:31,367
MAY: Yeah.

2266
02:01:31,368 --> 02:01:32,827
And things can change,

2267
02:01:32,828 --> 02:01:34,412
like, very quickly...
[SNAPS FINGERS]

2268
02:01:34,413 --> 02:01:37,498
...in ways that we can't
even imagine right now.

2269
02:01:37,499 --> 02:01:38,666
I know.

2270
02:01:38,667 --> 02:01:40,002
MAY: No. [CHUCKLES]

2271
02:01:42,421 --> 02:01:44,131
I don't think you do know.

2272
02:01:45,966 --> 02:01:47,551
What do you mean?

2273
02:01:50,679 --> 02:01:52,389
You're a really special person.

2274
02:01:54,016 --> 02:01:56,893
And I would hope that that will always
make you feel really great about yourself,

2275
02:01:58,020 --> 02:02:00,938
but I know sometimes it doesn't.

2276
02:02:00,939 --> 02:02:03,358
Sometimes, you'll be really lonely.

2277
02:02:06,987 --> 02:02:08,196
And sometimes,

2278
02:02:09,531 --> 02:02:11,033
because you're special,

2279
02:02:13,452 --> 02:02:17,122
people can do dark,
monstrous things to you.

2280
02:02:19,374 --> 02:02:20,459
But...

2281
02:02:22,002 --> 02:02:23,420
this is what I want you to know.

2282
02:02:25,422 --> 02:02:26,673
You're beautiful,

2283
02:02:27,340 --> 02:02:28,883
and the people who love you,

2284
02:02:28,884 --> 02:02:32,721
we love you not because you're special,
we love you because you're you.

2285
02:02:34,848 --> 02:02:36,308
I want you to remember that.

2286
02:02:38,560 --> 02:02:40,562
Even when it feels like
you're totally alone.

2287
02:02:43,565 --> 02:02:45,484
That's your deepest responsibility.

2288
02:02:48,779 --> 02:02:52,032
Never forget that,
no matter how powerful you become.

2289
02:02:53,075 --> 02:02:55,285
[SOMBER PIANO INSTRUMENTAL PLAYS]

2290
02:03:08,256 --> 02:03:09,341
PETER: Hey.

2291
02:03:18,809 --> 02:03:20,644
- [JEAN EXHALES SHAKILY]
- [SIGHS]

2292
02:03:25,065 --> 02:03:26,608
I'm sorry about your sister.

2293
02:03:31,905 --> 02:03:33,698
I'm sorry about your aunt.

2294
02:03:37,160 --> 02:03:38,411
Yeah, you would've loved her.

2295
02:03:42,249 --> 02:03:44,167
Just because we've lost someone...

2296
02:03:47,337 --> 02:03:49,339
It doesn't mean we have to do this alone.

2297
02:03:51,383 --> 02:03:54,385
I mean, we can't.

2298
02:03:54,386 --> 02:03:56,012
Trust me, I've been trying.

2299
02:03:59,266 --> 02:04:00,475
It doesn't work.

2300
02:04:05,313 --> 02:04:06,523
Even if that's true...

2301
02:04:10,902 --> 02:04:12,070
I have no one.

2302
02:04:16,783 --> 02:04:17,868
You have me.

2303
02:04:25,959 --> 02:04:29,212
- [MUSIC FADES]
- [SPIDER-SENSE TINGLING]

2304
02:04:33,842 --> 02:04:37,219
- [SPIDER-SENSE TINGLING]
- [GUN COCK ECHOING]

2305
02:04:37,220 --> 02:04:38,096
[GUN FIRES]

2306
02:04:42,934 --> 02:04:44,144
[PETER GRUNTS]

2307
02:04:44,936 --> 02:04:46,520
- [FIELD WARBLES, DISSIPATES]
- [METZGER GRUNTS]

2308
02:04:46,521 --> 02:04:49,441
[ALL GRUNTING]

2309
02:04:50,400 --> 02:04:52,402
[FIELD WARBLES, DISSIPATES]

2310
02:04:54,988 --> 02:04:57,239
[GASPS, PANTS]

2311
02:04:57,240 --> 02:04:58,617
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

2312
02:05:02,495 --> 02:05:03,496
Are you hurt?

2313
02:05:03,955 --> 02:05:05,957
No, I'm fine. [BREATHING HEAVILY]

2314
02:05:06,791 --> 02:05:08,293
[GASPS]

2315
02:05:10,962 --> 02:05:11,963
I'm okay.

2316
02:05:12,881 --> 02:05:14,423
- JEAN: Peter.
- I'm okay, I'm okay, I'm okay.

2317
02:05:14,424 --> 02:05:15,508
JEAN: Peter. No.

2318
02:05:19,638 --> 02:05:21,639
- Peter, Peter. No, no.
- [PETER GROANING]

2319
02:05:21,640 --> 02:05:22,973
- [COUGHS]
- JEAN: No, no, no, Peter.

2320
02:05:22,974 --> 02:05:24,725
- Peter.
- [GASPS]

2321
02:05:24,726 --> 02:05:27,228
Jean, you gotta get outta here.
They'll be looking for you.

2322
02:05:27,229 --> 02:05:29,021
No, no, no, no, no.
Please, just stay with me.

2323
02:05:29,022 --> 02:05:30,356
Come on, hold on. Come on, please!

2324
02:05:30,357 --> 02:05:31,524
Jean, you're...

2325
02:05:32,400 --> 02:05:33,902
You're gonna be okay.

2326
02:05:35,195 --> 02:05:36,278
Just go.

2327
02:05:36,279 --> 02:05:37,739
- [SNIFFLES]
- [GROANS]

2328
02:05:38,406 --> 02:05:39,407
Look at me.

2329
02:05:39,950 --> 02:05:42,117
[GROANS, BREATHES RAGGEDLY]

2330
02:05:42,118 --> 02:05:44,287
- [INHALES]
- [PETER MUTTERING]

2331
02:05:45,956 --> 02:05:47,332
[EXHALES]

2332
02:05:49,584 --> 02:05:51,586
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

2333
02:05:52,837 --> 02:05:54,673
[INAUDIBLE]

2334
02:05:57,175 --> 02:05:58,676
MALE REPORTER: <i>Shock today,</i>

2335
02:05:58,677 --> 02:06:02,055
<i>as Spider-Man arrived
at Bellevue Hospital with a bullet wound,</i>

2336
02:06:02,555 --> 02:06:04,224
<i>seemingly at death's door.</i>

2337
02:06:06,434 --> 02:06:09,144
<i>The reclusive crime fighter
is in critical condition,</i>

2338
02:06:09,145 --> 02:06:12,023
{\an8}<i>as the city's top medical experts
work to save him.</i>

2339
02:06:15,610 --> 02:06:18,363
<i>Tonight, all eyes are on Spider-Man.</i>

2340
02:06:20,407 --> 02:06:22,742
<i>The hero who saved
New York so many times...</i>

2341
02:06:23,243 --> 02:06:25,704
{\an8}<i>is now in the hands
of its best and brightest.</i>

2342
02:06:28,206 --> 02:06:31,167
<i>And the people of New York
hold their breath.</i>

2343
02:06:42,262 --> 02:06:44,264
[EKG MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]

2344
02:06:49,144 --> 02:06:51,313
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

2345
02:06:56,109 --> 02:06:58,737
[FIELD WARBLING FAINTLY]

2346
02:07:07,037 --> 02:07:09,663
[INHALES, EXHALES]

2347
02:07:09,664 --> 02:07:11,791
- [WARBLING STOPS]
- [BIRD CHIRPING]

2348
02:07:16,338 --> 02:07:18,340
[EKG MACHINE BEEPING FAINTLY]

2349
02:07:34,356 --> 02:07:35,648
[SNORING]

2350
02:07:38,026 --> 02:07:39,027
PETER: Frank?

2351
02:07:42,489 --> 02:07:43,656
Where am I?

2352
02:07:45,617 --> 02:07:48,035
- FRANK: No, no, no, no, no. Hey.
- Where's my mask?

2353
02:07:48,036 --> 02:07:49,411
Don't worry about that.
I got you covered.

2354
02:07:49,412 --> 02:07:50,455
Hey, you're good.

2355
02:07:50,955 --> 02:07:52,414
PETER: Where's Jean? Is she okay?

2356
02:07:52,415 --> 02:07:54,416
Yeah, she's okay. [CHUCKLES] She's okay.

2357
02:07:54,417 --> 02:07:55,627
PETER: Where is she?

2358
02:07:56,920 --> 02:07:58,463
I think maybe she just left.

2359
02:07:59,756 --> 02:08:04,511
She was, uh, using her magic voodoo shit
to keep you alive.

2360
02:08:05,136 --> 02:08:08,139
[CHUCKLES] Yeah... she's all right.

2361
02:08:14,813 --> 02:08:15,814
I'm sorry.

2362
02:08:20,693 --> 02:08:22,236
- Frank.
- Just... Just... I'm...

2363
02:08:22,237 --> 02:08:23,987
- Frank, it's okay.
- I'm really sorry for what I did.

2364
02:08:23,988 --> 02:08:25,072
- No, Frank, it's okay.
- FRANK: And it's...

2365
02:08:25,073 --> 02:08:27,700
No, it's a lot of things,
but it sure as shit ain't okay, all right?

2366
02:08:31,371 --> 02:08:32,372
I've seen...

2367
02:08:34,207 --> 02:08:37,794
I've seen real bravery, kid, in my day.

2368
02:08:39,546 --> 02:08:40,547
But that...

2369
02:08:42,006 --> 02:08:43,425
that was something else.

2370
02:08:46,845 --> 02:08:48,262
- You crying, Frank?
- [LAUGHS]

2371
02:08:48,263 --> 02:08:49,847
No. I ain't...

2372
02:08:49,848 --> 02:08:51,599
[LAUGHING]

2373
02:08:52,142 --> 02:08:54,018
[LAUGHING]

2374
02:08:56,521 --> 02:08:58,440
You know, you look the exact way
I thought you would.

2375
02:08:59,566 --> 02:09:00,567
You know.

2376
02:09:01,025 --> 02:09:02,193
A nice kid.

2377
02:09:04,696 --> 02:09:06,030
Never had a friend like that.

2378
02:09:07,866 --> 02:09:09,409
Are we friends now?

2379
02:09:16,374 --> 02:09:18,041
I can't believe I just saw you cry.

2380
02:09:18,042 --> 02:09:19,168
- [PETER LAUGHS]
- [LAUGHS] I didn't cry.

2381
02:09:19,169 --> 02:09:20,085
What are you talking about?

2382
02:09:20,086 --> 02:09:21,628
Bullshit.

2383
02:09:21,629 --> 02:09:23,547
[DISTANT SHOUTING]

2384
02:09:23,548 --> 02:09:25,215
Oh, yeah, this.

2385
02:09:25,216 --> 02:09:26,925
They've been doing it all night.

2386
02:09:26,926 --> 02:09:29,471
They've been here since you walked in.
Just take a look.

2387
02:09:37,145 --> 02:09:38,354
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

2388
02:09:40,231 --> 02:09:43,275
Yo, kid, when you came in,
they had to cut through the suit,

2389
02:09:43,276 --> 02:09:45,361
but when you're ready to split...

2390
02:09:46,196 --> 02:09:47,697
[SMACKS LIPS] ...I got a plan.

2391
02:10:09,636 --> 02:10:12,514
- MAN: Hey, it's Spider-Man!
- [ALL CHEERING]

2392
02:10:14,140 --> 02:10:15,641
MAN 2: Spider-Man!

2393
02:10:15,642 --> 02:10:17,727
[ALL CHEERING]

2394
02:10:19,354 --> 02:10:20,438
MAN 3: Hey!

2395
02:10:21,940 --> 02:10:23,065
[CHUCKLES]

2396
02:10:23,066 --> 02:10:24,484
MAN 3: Yeah, Spider-Man!

2397
02:10:25,902 --> 02:10:27,654
MAN 4: You're the best, Spider-Man!

2398
02:10:28,738 --> 02:10:30,031
MAN 5: Spider-Man!

2399
02:10:31,741 --> 02:10:32,909
MAN 2: Over here!

2400
02:10:33,910 --> 02:10:35,202
WOMAN: Thank you!

2401
02:10:35,203 --> 02:10:36,496
MAN 6: Spider-Man!

2402
02:10:49,300 --> 02:10:51,302
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

2403
02:11:01,896 --> 02:11:03,313
[FRANK GRUNTING]

2404
02:11:03,314 --> 02:11:05,400
[ALL CHEERING]

2405
02:11:06,943 --> 02:11:09,278
CROWD: [CHANTING] Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2406
02:11:09,279 --> 02:11:13,448
Spider-Man! Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2407
02:11:13,449 --> 02:11:18,538
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2408
02:11:20,582 --> 02:11:21,874
[BLOWS AIR SHARPLY]

2409
02:11:28,673 --> 02:11:32,759
[CHANTING] Spider-Man!
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2410
02:11:32,760 --> 02:11:36,722
CROWD: [CHANTING] Spider-Man!
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2411
02:11:36,723 --> 02:11:39,182
Spider-Man! Spider-Man!

2412
02:11:39,183 --> 02:11:41,269
[SERENE MUSIC PLAYING]

2413
02:12:14,677 --> 02:12:16,679
[SERENE MUSIC CONTINUES]

2414
02:12:42,705 --> 02:12:43,706
I've, uh...

2415
02:12:46,709 --> 02:12:48,670
Been thinking a lot about what you said.

2416
02:12:51,214 --> 02:12:53,925
And you'd be happy to know
that I've decided I'm not...

2417
02:12:55,593 --> 02:12:57,595
I'm not gonna do this alone anymore.

2418
02:13:03,476 --> 02:13:04,644
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

2419
02:13:07,105 --> 02:13:08,356
I miss you, May.

2420
02:13:16,781 --> 02:13:18,865
PETER: I mean, I've still got
a little pain in my back,

2421
02:13:18,866 --> 02:13:21,910
but I could probably get back out there
if you need me for anything.

2422
02:13:21,911 --> 02:13:24,454
DEWOLFF: <i>No.
What I need you to do is rest.</i>

2423
02:13:24,455 --> 02:13:26,581
I know, I know, but come on,
you gotta give me something.

2424
02:13:26,582 --> 02:13:28,583
I mean, how's the investigation going?

2425
02:13:28,584 --> 02:13:31,586
DEWOLFF: <i>Well, Metzger's still missing,</i>

2426
02:13:31,587 --> 02:13:34,131
but your friend, Black Widow,

2427
02:13:34,132 --> 02:13:36,842
she's been helping us dig through
all the records

2428
02:13:36,843 --> 02:13:38,970
Damage Control tried to have scrubbed.

2429
02:13:39,470 --> 02:13:41,972
<i>Had me drop by her office the other day.</i>

2430
02:13:41,973 --> 02:13:43,015
And how was that?

2431
02:13:43,474 --> 02:13:46,059
Well, uh, my skin feels amazing.

2432
02:13:46,060 --> 02:13:47,186
[ALARM BEEPS]

2433
02:13:47,603 --> 02:13:48,895
DISPATCHER: [ON PHONE]
<i>Attention, all units.</i>

2434
02:13:48,896 --> 02:13:50,897
<i>We have a confirmed
bank robbery in progress.</i>

2435
02:13:50,898 --> 02:13:51,899
Hey, are you getting this?

2436
02:13:53,568 --> 02:13:54,735
Yeah, I'm on it.

2437
02:13:54,736 --> 02:13:57,154
Hey, it's not that far from me.
I could probably meet you down there.

2438
02:13:57,155 --> 02:13:59,574
No. We can handle a robbery.

2439
02:14:00,533 --> 02:14:03,286
Just try to take care of yourself.

2440
02:14:04,996 --> 02:14:05,997
Okay.

2441
02:14:07,331 --> 02:14:08,332
You too.

2442
02:14:09,375 --> 02:14:11,043
Say hello to EJ and Marley for me.

2443
02:14:11,502 --> 02:14:13,463
[CHUCKLES] Okay.

2444
02:14:15,506 --> 02:14:16,924
Spider-Man says hello.

2445
02:14:18,426 --> 02:14:19,635
[DOOR BELL CHIMES]

2446
02:14:27,977 --> 02:14:29,270
[DEVICE CHIMES]

2447
02:14:30,313 --> 02:14:31,856
[CRUNCHING]

2448
02:14:39,989 --> 02:14:42,241
[SERENE MUSIC PLAYING]

2449
02:14:53,169 --> 02:14:54,252
Hi.

2450
02:14:54,253 --> 02:14:55,755
NED: Uh, hey.

2451
02:14:57,715 --> 02:15:01,009
Oh, oh. Uh, flower guy, right,
from... from the party?

2452
02:15:01,010 --> 02:15:02,011
Yeah.

2453
02:15:02,720 --> 02:15:03,846
I'm Peter.

2454
02:15:04,931 --> 02:15:06,307
Okay. Hello.

2455
02:15:09,852 --> 02:15:11,938
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

2456
02:15:24,867 --> 02:15:25,952
Peter.

2457
02:15:31,207 --> 02:15:33,793
{\an8}[MELLOW, MID-TEMPO SONG PLAYING]

2458
02:15:49,851 --> 02:15:51,644
[INAUDIBLE CONVERSATION]

2459
02:16:16,544 --> 02:16:18,254
[INAUDIBLE CONVERSATION]

2460
02:16:26,554 --> 02:16:29,807
{\an8}- [SONG CONTINUES]
- [INAUDIBLE CONVERSATION]

2461
02:16:46,574 --> 02:16:48,492
[INAUDIBLE SINGING]

2462
02:17:19,941 --> 02:17:21,025
[SONG ENDS]

2463
02:17:22,151 --> 02:17:24,236
[SERENE MUSIC PLAYING]

2464
02:19:22,438 --> 02:19:24,523
[SERENE MUSIC CONTINUES]

2465
02:21:26,770 --> 02:21:28,772
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

2466
02:22:55,901 --> 02:22:57,903
[TRIUMPHANT MUSIC PLAYING]

2467
02:23:53,876 --> 02:23:55,878
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

2468
02:24:22,488 --> 02:24:24,490
{\an8}[BEEPING]

2469
02:24:26,909 --> 02:24:29,995
APP VOICE: <i>New Spider-Man sighting.
Location unknown.</i>

2470
02:24:31,080 --> 02:24:32,663
<i>- Location unknown.
-</i> [DEVICE BUZZING]

2471
02:24:32,664 --> 02:24:33,873
[BEEPING CONTINUES]

2472
02:24:33,874 --> 02:24:35,501
<i>Location unknown.</i>

2473
02:24:36,543 --> 02:24:38,170
<i>Location unknown.</i>

2474
02:24:39,296 --> 02:24:40,672
<i>Location unknown.</i>

2475
02:24:45,177 --> 02:24:47,805
<i>- Location found.
-</i> [BEEPING RAPIDLY]
